window.FWN_MESMERIZING_GHOST_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_MESMERIZING_GHOST_DOCTOR_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":5001,"title":"Chapter 5001: Stir Up Trouble","paragraphs":["Chapter 5001: Stir Up Trouble","The lion crouched among the weeds, noticing the pack of fierce beasts staring intently at its position. It no longer concealed itself, rising to its feet and letting out a low growl as a warning.","The pack of fierce beasts, which had been following the scent of blood to hunt, swiftly retreated upon seeing the lion stand. They lowered their heads slightly, emitting low, subdued howls.","The lion watched them until they retreated completely, then turned and walked back to where it had come from, returning to its young master.","Over there, Song Lingbo instructed the guard to quickly tidy up the scene. After counting the spoils of war, he divided the items into two portions—one for the guard and one for the three children.","“We don’t need these. You keep them!” Hao’er shook his head, refusing to take any.","“Take them! You deserve them,” Song Lingbo said with a smile, placing the items into his hands.","Seeing this, Hao’er accepted them but immediately handed them to the two guards behind him: “Here, you take these!”","“This...” The two guards looked at him in surprise, then glanced at their Master.","Song Mi’er smiled brightly. “Just take what he’s giving you. They don’t need these things anyway.”","“Since he’s giving it to you, you should take it!” Song Lingbo finally spoke up.","Hearing this, the two guards immediately clasped their fists in salute. “Thank you, Young Master!”","“We should move to another location. This place reeks of blood; it’s not suitable to linger here any longer,” Song Lingbo said, signaling for them to pack up and relocate their resting spot.","“Understood.” Everyone responded, swiftly gathering their belongings and moving.","Compared to their forest ordeal, Feng Jiu’s days at the Song residence were far more leisurely.","When idle, she chatted with Lady Song, occasionally ventured out alone, or stayed in her courtyard reading. Sometimes she entered her spatial realm to refine medicinal pills. While awaiting the children’s return, her days passed in peaceful ease.","One day, after finishing the preparation of medicinal pills in her spatial pocket, she emerged with the lingering scent of herbs. She had the servants prepare a bath, intending to eat and rest afterward.","After bathing, she sat in the courtyard eating her meal. Seeing the maidservants and guards outside rushing past, she turned to one of the maids waiting nearby and asked, “Where are they all going?” “Why do they all look so flustered?”","The maid curtsied and replied, “My lady, it seems that guests have arrived at the front gate. However, before the patriarch left, he instructed that no visitors be received during this period. The visitors attacked the gatekeeper, so the household staff have all gone to investigate.”","Upon hearing this, Feng Jiu said no more and continued eating her meal. During her stay at the Song residence, no other guests had indeed visited besides her. Closing the doors to visitors was understandable—after all, with the male head of the household absent and only the mistress at home, anyone with sense wouldn’t choose this moment to pay a call. Unless...","Unless they were the kind who deliberately chose to cause trouble when the master wasn’t home.","However, she had heard from Lady Song these past days that although Song Lingbo and his sons were absent, the clan elders remained at the residence. Should any matter arise beyond Lady Song’s capacity, they would seek the elders’ intervention.","After finishing her meal, she set down her chopsticks, wiped her lips, and gestured. “Clear this table. Bring me a cup of tea.”","“Yes, ma’am.” The maid responded respectfully, clearing the table before turning to leave. Soon after, she returned carrying a cup of tea."]},{"number":5002,"title":"Chapter 5002: Someone","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu strolled through the courtyard to aid her digestion, calculating the time. Had it been over half a month now? They should be returning soon. She wondered if those little ones had grown more skilled since leaving.","After taking a sip of tea while pacing, she decided to head to the front courtyard.","With the head of the Song household absent, and since this was Mi'er's family, though the Song clan elders were present, Feng Jiu felt it would be better to pay a visit, especially considering the gentle nature of Lady Song.","As she made her way to the front courtyard, chaos reigned at the main gate of the Song residence. The middle-aged gatekeeper lay sprawled on the ground, blood trickling from the corner of his mouth. Several Song family guards were locked in a fierce scuffle with the intruders' own guards. Though swords and blades weren't drawn, and no lives were lost, the force behind each punch landed squarely on its target. Those hit hard enough might not be fatally wounded, but they certainly wouldn't escape with minor injuries.","\"Cease this at once!\"","A furious voice cut through the air, and both sides immediately halted their fighting. All eyes turned to the beautiful woman stepping forward. The Song family members, recognizing her, instantly stepped back to make way, bowing in unison.","\"My lady.\"","Lady Song's expression darkened slightly. She stepped forward, her gaze fixed with anger on the group ahead: \"Who are you? Forcibly entering my residence and injuring my household staff—do you intend to make enemies of the Song family?\" Even someone of gentle disposition now carried herself with the authority of the patriarch, her voice firm and commanding.","\"Heh heh, Sister-in-law, please calm your anger!\"","A man in his forties chuckled, his gaze lingering on Lady Song with a subtle appraising glance. His smile broadened as he said, \"It was truly the servants' misconduct that led to the altercation with your household staff. This was not my intention.\"","His words trailed off as he observed Lady Song, her face flushed crimson with fury, anger blazing in her eyes. He offered an apologetic tone, \"The blame rests squarely on my shoulders for failing to discipline my servants properly, allowing them such audacity. I shall personally address this matter with you, My Lady.\" With that, he moved swiftly, drawing the sword from a guard's sheath beside him. With a sharp whistling sound, the blade sliced clean through the guard's arm.","\"Aah!\"","The piercing scream jolted everyone present. As they watched the scene unfold, the expressions of the Song family members shifted noticeably.","This man had acted without hesitation, and his first move was to sever a guard's arm. It must be said, such a resolution did extinguish the smoldering anger in their hearts.","The guard whose arm had been severed let out a piercing scream of agony before collapsing to his knees under the force of the blow. The severed limb rolled to his feet. Clutching the bleeding stump with his remaining hand, his face drained of color. He dared not utter another sound, instead bowing his head. His voice trembled with restraint as he pleaded, \"Please, Lady Song, calm your anger.\"","Lady Song had never imagined this man would suddenly sever the guard's arm. She too was stunned, watching the scene unfold, momentarily speechless.","Not far away, Feng Jiu leaned against the wall, observing the scene before her. Her gaze flickered especially when she saw the middle-aged man strike and sever the arm of the guard beside him.","It was unclear what she was thinking as she stood there, watching silently.","While the expressions of the Song family members shifted slightly, the group standing behind the middle-aged man showed not a flicker of change, as if they were utterly accustomed to such violence."]},{"number":5003,"title":"Chapter 5003: Cheng Family of Longnan","paragraphs":["Chapter 5003: Cheng Family of Longnan","The middle-aged man merely chuckled, handing the sword to his guard beside him with an expression of utter indifference. His demeanor suggested he had severed not the arm of his own bodyguard, but some insignificant cat or dog.","“My lady, I apologize for startling you. Please accept my apologies here.”","He smiled, bowed slightly to Lady Song, and added, ” “I haven’t introduced myself. I’m Cheng Wanli. I came specifically to visit Brother Song. I wonder if he’s mentioned me to you. Back in Taiping Mountain, Brother Song and I faced life-and-death hardships together. I’ve long wanted to visit, but never had the chance. This time, I came here especially to see him. I never imagined my men would cause such a disturbance. I’m truly ashamed.”","Hearing the sincerity in his apology, seeing him personally deal with the troublemakers, and listening to his repeated addresses of ‘sister-in-law’ and expressions of regret, Lady Song’s anger began to dissipate.","She looked at the man before her, Cheng Wanli, and after a moment, her voice softened. “Since you have a history with my husband, I shall let this matter rest. I won’t hold this against you. However, my husband is away and has ordered the gates closed to visitors. I’m afraid we cannot entertain you all.”","Seeing this, Cheng Wanli’s eyes flickered slightly, and a trace of hesitation appeared on his face. “So Brother Song is not at home? Then my timing is truly unfortunate! But...”","His voice trailed off, a look of distress crossing his face. “However, my lady suffered a relapse of her old ailment on the journey. She’s unconscious now. Might My Lady Song allow us to rest in the manor for a day or two?”","Hearing this, Lady Song paused, a flicker of hesitation on her face. “This...” Only then did she notice two maidservants supporting a woman draped in a large cloak, who was half-reclining against them.","The woman’s face remained hidden beneath the hood of her cloak, her form entirely concealed within the dark fabric. Only the faint outline of an exceptionally beautiful visage could be discerned. As the man had said, she lay there, eyes closed, unconscious.","“What’s going on?” an aged voice echoed.","At that moment, the crowd turned to see several clan elders approaching. They had evidently come upon hearing the commotion and disturbance at the manor entrance.","The sight of the severed arm on the ground caused the elders’ brows to furrow in displeasure. One of them demanded, “What is this? Why is there bloodshed?”","“Second Elder, it happened like this...” The steward nearby promptly recounted the entire sequence of events in detail.","“Cheng Wanli?” The Fourth Elder’s expression turned surprised as he looked at the middle-aged man and asked, “You are Cheng Wanli? Which Cheng family?”","Hearing the elder’s question, the others all glanced at him, puzzled by the implication behind his inquiry.","Lady Song remained silent, lost in her own thoughts.","“The Cheng family of Longnan. My elder brother is Cheng Wanshan, the current Patriarch of the family.” Cheng Wanli said with a smile, bowing his hands. As he spoke, a hint of unmistakable pride shone in his eyes.","Hearing this, the expressions of several clan elders shifted slightly: The Cheng family of Longnan!","At that moment, their hearts trembled faintly. The Cheng family of Longnan was a truly formidable clan! Even the combined strength of their ten Song families couldn’t match a single branch of the Cheng Family of Longnan. Yet, unexpectedly, someone from their family had a prior connection with them."]},{"number":5004,"title":"Chapter 5004: Trouble Brewing","paragraphs":["Chapter 5004: Trouble Brewing","Considering the depth of the Cheng family’s roots in Longnan, the elders felt a flicker of unease. Suppressing their shock, they immediately turned to Lady Song beside them and said, “Since he and Lingbo are old acquaintances, and you are unwell, why not invite them to stay at the residence for a day or two?”","Hearing this, Madam Song furrowed her brow slightly. “But my husband specifically instructed that we not receive guests during this period.” Moreover, whether it was a woman’s intuition or not, she felt a certain dislike toward this group, especially that man named Cheng Wanli, who evoked a strong sense of aversion.","The man had severed an arm from one of the guards without so much as a flinch, showing no regard for the fact that the guard was his own man. Such ruthlessness, coupled with his unsettling manner and speech, made her uneasy.","She couldn’t fathom how such a person could be acquainted with her husband, but instinctively, she didn’t want them staying in the mansion.","“Granted, they are guests,” the Fourth Elder conceded. “But the Cheng family of Longnan is no obscure, unknown entity. Keeping them for a day or two poses no harm. Moreover, as hosts, it is our duty to extend hospitality to visitors from afar.” His words trailed off as he glanced toward the First Elder, exchanging a knowing look.","Truthfully, they believed the Longnan Cheng family was a formidable clan. Establishing connections with such a family could only be advantageous. Besides, though Song Lingbo and his sons were absent, their elders remained in the manor, so there was little to worry about.","Besides, what harm could guests from the Cheng family possibly do to the Song family? Such a thing was virtually impossible.","“Let them stay! The mansion isn’t short of guest quarters,” declared the First Elder. Turning to the steward, he instructed, “Escort the guests to their quarters and see they are well attended to.”","The steward glanced at Lady Song, who remained silent, then replied, “Yes.” He then gestured to Cheng Wanli and his companions, “This way, please.”","“Honorable Elders, Madam, thank you all. I shall seek you out later for a proper conversation.” With a bow and a smile, he followed the steward inside.","As they walked inward, Cheng Wanli’s gaze suddenly halted. He glanced toward a plain-looking woman in blue robes standing in the corner. His eyes sharpened as he scanned her, confirming she was merely an ordinary cultivator. With that, he withdrew his attention and continued stepping inside.","Feng Jiu’s gaze swept indifferently over the group, her eyes flickering with an unreadable thought. She glanced at Lady Song, who had been summoned by the clan elders ahead, paused briefly, then turned and walked back.","That group certainly didn’t look like good people. Especially that Cheng Wanli—she wouldn’t mistake him. The glint in his eyes when he misidentified Lady Song, like he’d spotted prey, was truly unsettling. And then there was that woman claiming to be his wife.","Though her face was partially obscured by dark hair, making her features hard to discern, it was clear she was very young—a girl barely twenty. And she called herself a Lady, was she married? Hmph! That was highly improbable.","“Looks like trouble brewing in the Song household,” she murmured softly, shaking her head as she turned back. She wondered when Song Lingbo and the others would return.","She silently resolved: Tonight, I’ll go investigate. Better safe than sorry if they’ve invited disaster upon themselves without realizing it."]},{"number":5005,"title":"Chapter 5005: Slap","paragraphs":["After bringing the Cheng family members to the guest courtyard, Steward Song withdrew. The Cheng household guards secured every corner of the compound, leaving the Song family members scarcely any opportunity to approach.","In the side chamber, the two maids laid the woman they had been supporting onto the bed before retreating to stand guard outside the door.","Cheng Wanli approached, sat down beside the bed, and gently released the pressure points restraining the woman. Soon, the previously unconscious figure slowly opened her eyes.","Her eyes, however, blazed with fury and hatred as she glared at Cheng Wanli. She wanted to move, but her body remained frozen. Even cursing was beyond her power.","\"Heh, had a good sleep on the journey?\" He reached out, caressing her cheek and tucking a strand of hair that had fallen across her face behind her ear, revealing a face of breathtaking beauty.","Cheng Wanli narrowed his eyes at the breathtaking beauty before him, a look of rapture spreading across his face. His hand continued to caress her face, his fingers tracing her brow, gliding down her nose, and lightly touching her crimson lips. He moved his fingers to her chin, gently lifting it, then leaned in to kiss her.","Her body stiffened, her eyes blazing with fury yet helpless, forced to endure his actions.","\"Ugh!\"","Suddenly, Cheng Wanli let out a low cry and jerked back, his face turning ashen as he glared viciously at the woman on the bed. His tongue was bitten, his lip torn, blood seeping from his mouth. The pain made his entire face darken instantly. He swung his hand, delivering a hard slap to the woman on the bed.","\"Bitch!\"","The curse erupted from his mouth simultaneously with the sharp crack of the slap. Outside in the courtyard, people heard the slap and his curses, yet none turned to look. No one showed curiosity or inquiry; they remained expressionless, standing their ground and continuing their tasks.","Inside the side room, the woman on the bed was struck hard across the face. One side of her face swelled up, and blood trickled from the corner of her mouth as she glared at Cheng Wanli. Her eyes seemed to say: If you’ve got the guts, kill her.","Slap!","Cheng Wanli spat out a mouthful of blood, wiped the corner of his lips, and lightly touched his tongue. He reached out and gripped the woman’s chin hard: \"Want to die? Trying to provoke me into killing you? Ha! Forget it. I haven’t even tasted you properly yet. How could I let you die so easily?\"","He flicked his hand dismissively and snorted coldly. \"Obey me, and you’ll suffer less. If you really piss me off, you’ll regret it!\" With that, he turned and strode out.","After he left, the woman remained alone on the bed. Staring blankly at the ceiling, her eyes held despair and sorrow. A single tear slid from the corner of her eye, trickling down her cheek and onto the pillow, leaving a faint wet trail...","In the adjoining room, Cheng Wanli was conversing with four elderly men. One of them paused, turned to Cheng Wanli, and asked, \"Second Master, shall we proceed tonight?\"","Cheng Wanli pressed his finger lightly against the ointment on his lip. \"No rush. Tonight, I’ll go and probe the situation first. It’s not too late to act once we have clarity. The main thing is not to alert those old fools, lest things spiral out of control.\"","Speaking caused his bitten tongue to throb slightly, making him frown involuntarily as his expression darkened.","Another elder nodded. \"True. From what we’ve gathered, Song Lingbo likely won’t return in the next few days.\""]},{"number":5006,"title":"Chapter 5006: No Need to Worry","paragraphs":["\"Hmph, so what if he’s back? Does he really think he can defy our Cheng family?\" another elder sneered, his words dripping with contempt.","\"The Song family is now propped up solely by Song Lingbo. His abilities are undeniably formidable, but the man refuses to be used by others. Otherwise, our Cheng family would have been eager to recruit him. What a pity.\"","Cheng Wanli sneered coldly, then seemed to recall something. His eyes flickered, and an inexplicable smile touched his lips. \"Though Song Lingbo’s wife is truly a beauty in the making. Even as the mother of several children, she still possesses such captivating charm—a unique allure.\"","\"Second Master, why haven’t you dealt with that woman you’re bringing along? Carrying her on the road could easily lead to trouble. After all, she’s not exactly the quiet type.\" an elder remarked, recalling the woman in his own quarters! Now he was eyeing Song Lingbo’s woman, inwardly shaking his head yet finding it all too familiar.","Cheng Wanli’s sole passion was beautiful women. His courtyard housed dozens, if not hundreds, each possessing unique charms. Little did anyone expect his tastes would grow so peculiar—now he even coveted married women.","\"That’s a woman I plan to bring to the back courtyard. She’s still untouched! Besides, her wounds haven’t healed yet. I’ve no interest in touching a woman covered in scars.\" He touched his lips again, revealing a sinister smile. \"This woman is fiery, like a wild horse. I have all the time in the world to tame her!\"","\"Second Master, would you like me to accompany you tonight?\" an elderly man inquired, observing him. \"There are quite a few hidden guards watching over the Song residence. I fear you might not be able to handle them all.\"","\"Alright, one escort will suffice.\" He stroked his chin, his thoughts drifting to the Lady Song’s beauty and figure, his heart racing with anticipation.","At that moment, Lady Song was walking towards Feng Jiu’s courtyard. Upon entering, she saw Feng Jiu strolling about and approached, calling out, \"Lady Xuanyuan.\"","Feng Jiu turned and raised an eyebrow at her. \"Why have you come, Lady Song?\"","\"I came to inform you that some guests have arrived at the mansion—all men, no less. I’m concerned you might encounter them if you go out.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled and said, \"So that’s what this is about. Just now, I heard from a maid that guests had arrived and were causing a commotion in the front courtyard, so I went to take a look. I saw those people too.\"","Madam Song’s brows knitted slightly, and she said with some unease, \"I don’t know why, but looking at those people, I feel a vague sense of unease. They say they are from the Cheng family. Do you know the Cheng family? They’re the most prominent clan in the Longnan region. Their status is extraordinary because their family has produced nine Supreme-level cultivators.\"","She sat down at the stone table in the courtyard, a trace of worry between her brows. \"Our Song family is a lineage of culinary cultivators. My father-in-law—our Song family’s patriarch—has been in seclusion for years. Some say he might have attained enlightenment through meditation, others say he couldn’t break through. Rumors outside run wild. Now, only my husband holds the Song family together. Families like ours naturally can’t compare to the Chens of Longnan. So even though I dislike those people, when several clan elders spoke up asking them to stay, I couldn’t bring myself to refuse.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu chuckled softly and said, \"Actually, there’s no need for you to worry so much.\""]},{"number":5007,"title":"Chapter 5007: Debauched","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu smiled, walked over to the table, and sat down. \"If they wish to stay, let them stay. It’ll be interesting to see what they’re up to.\"","Madam Song paused, her gaze lingering on Feng Jiu’s serene expression and the calm, faint smile at the corner of her lips. Somehow, her heart settled a little.","She composed herself and apologized, \"I’m afraid I’ve made a spectacle of myself. There’s no one else in the house I can talk to, and I find I get along well with you, so I ended up sharing these things with you.\"","\"It’s fine,\" Feng Jiu said with a smile. \"I’m happy to listen. Besides, I don’t think the Song family is any less than the Cheng family.\"","A gentle smile blossomed on Mrs. Song’s face. \"My husband’s reputation as a culinary master is indeed far-reaching, and his skills are truly formidable. Throughout this region, the various clans show him considerable respect. No one has ever troubled our Song family.\" Mentioning her husband, her face lit up with pride.","Her voice paused, and her expression turned serious. \"However, compared to the Cheng family, the Song family truly falls short. Right now, I only hope they’ll rest for a day or two and then leave quickly, to avoid any trouble arising.\"","The two chatted idly in the courtyard for a while. Before long, Lady Song rose first and departed. After she left, Feng Jiu also returned to her room to prepare for sleep.","As night fell, Feng Jiu slipped quietly out of her courtyard and made her way to the guest quarters where the Cheng family resided. From the shadows, she observed that the compound was guarded with meticulous vigilance—guards patrolled both inside and outside. Earlier that day, she had also noticed four formidable-looking elders following closely behind Cheng Wanli.","Therefore, as she approached the courtyard, she exercised extreme caution. Evading the watchful eyes, she slipped silently into the compound. Her figure leapt up and landed on the rooftop, blending into the night shadows. Unnoticed, she lay concealed.","Lying low, she listened intently to the sounds below. Faintly, she heard Cheng Wanli’s voice drifting from the rooms beneath.","\"Apply the medicine! Treat her wounds immediately! She’s an eyesore!\" Cheng Wanli swept his sleeve as he exited the room and headed to another chamber. Shortly after, two maidservants emerged, having applied the medicine, and took up guard outside the door.","She lifted a corner of the roof to peer down. On the bed, the woman who had been unconscious during the day was now awake, yet lay motionless beneath a quilt. It appeared she wore no clothing underneath.","After a quick glance, she replaced the lifted corner of the blanket and leapt lightly onto the roof of the adjacent room.","Inside the room, one of the elders addressed Cheng Wanli: \"The night is deep now. If you must go on your errand, go. But if you fail to discover where the Song family’s treasure is hidden, remember to administer the drug afterward to erase her memory of tonight. We mustn’t alert the enemy prematurely.\"","\"I know, rest assured! I know what I’m doing.\" Cheng Wanli chuckled, rising to his feet and adjusting his robes. His face beaming, he added, \"I’ll head out now, Old Fu. Let’s go! I’ll handle things inside; you keep watch outside.\"","\"Understood.\" One of the elders replied, stepping beside him as they walked out together.","After watching them leave the room, Feng Jiu suppressed her aura and slipped into the night, heading toward the main courtyard.","Her eyebrows arched slightly. She hadn’t expected this man to be so impatient—arriving today and already attempting to sneak into the main courtyard tonight. Truly, his lust had made him utterly reckless!"]},{"number":5008,"title":"Chapter 5008: Cold Glint","paragraphs":["Inside the house, three elderly men shook their heads. \"If Second Master doesn’t rein in his little hobby, I’m genuinely worried he’ll cause trouble someday.\"","\"Reign in? Hah! That’s his only passion—how could he possibly reign it in? That woman in the main hall—if not for her wounds dampening his interest, he’d have plucked that flower long ago. How could she still be pure and untouched?\"","\"Hmph. I’d say it wasn’t about losing interest at all. He just happened to get excited when Song Lingbo’s wife showed up. But this time, we’re mainly here to retrieve that item from the Song family. We didn’t plan on letting the Second Master indulge in his pleasures.\"","\"On the way here, he wasn’t just indulging in one pleasure. Who remembers any of those women afterward? Truth be told, that potion really is something special.\"","\"Exactly. But that potion is reserved only for the Cheng family’s direct line or those of the highest standing within the clan...\"","Feng Jiu listened from the rooftop for a while before cutting off the conversation, primarily out of concern for Lady Song in the main courtyard. If Mi’er’s mother were to be taken advantage of right under her nose, she’d never be able to show her face again.","Without a moment’s hesitation, she turned and slipped away, heading toward the main courtyard.","The Cheng family’s cultivation was indeed superior to the Song family’s. The two men made their way toward the main courtyard, easily evading the hidden guards and bodyguards within the estate, arriving silently at the main residence.","Cheng Wanli gave the elder a discreet signal. The elder remained hidden in a secluded spot within the courtyard, while only Cheng Wanli advanced silently.","At that moment, Lady Song wore only a white undershirt, a book in her hand as she leaned against the headboard. Yet, she seemed to have fallen asleep, unaware even as the book slipped slightly from her grasp.","Her head rested on one hand as she lay on her side, the quilt drawn only to her waist. By the dim night lamp, strands of hair fell loosely across her cheek, adding a touch of allure to her striking beauty.","Because she lay slightly turned, the opening at her neckline revealed a glimpse of snow-white skin, intensely tempting in the soft glow.","Cheng Wanli, observing this scene from the rooftop, couldn’t help but swallow hard. His gaze swept over her from head to toe, growing increasingly intense with every passing moment.","Noticing she lay alone in the bed, he silently drew an object from his sleeve. Lightly igniting it, he let the dangling wick drift into the room.","Wispy smoke began to waft through the air, its faint scent imperceptible to the sleeping figure unless one possessed an exceptionally keen sense of smell.","Madam Song on the bed seemed to catch the scent and tried to open her eyes. But her heavy eyelids held her captive, and in the next instant, consciousness slipped away. A flicker of alarm crossed her mind, yet she could do nothing as she plunged into endless darkness...","Seeing her collapse onto the bed, Cheng Wanli, perched on the roof, let out a sinister smile. He flipped down from the roof, leaping directly through the window to the bedside, where he gazed at the sleeping beauty.","\"Hmm, hmm. Song Lingbo is truly blessed! This woman is indeed beautiful, with a unique charm all her own!\" \" he murmured, approaching her and pulling back the blanket covering her. His gaze grew intense as he took in her figure.","At that moment, Feng Jiu slipped quietly into the courtyard. She saw that the person lurking in the shadows had fallen unconscious at some point, leaving only the elderly man from the Cheng family guarding the darkened area. A cold gleam flashed in her eyes. With a swift movement, she darted forward."]},{"number":5009,"title":"Chapter 5009: Came Late","paragraphs":["The old man lurking in the shadows waited with narrowed eyes, his outward-projected divine sense allowing him to detect any approaching presence even with his eyes closed.","Yet, his misfortune was encountering Feng Jiu—a being whose power far surpassed his own, and who could conceal her aura completely, leaving no trace detectable to others.","Concerned for Lady Song inside the room, Feng Jiu wasted no time. She swept through the night, arriving behind the old man and seizing his throat before he could react.","She had intended to snap his neck outright, but in that instant, a thought crossed her mind. Her other hand darted out, a silver needle instantly piercing his pressure point.","The old man’s eyes snapped open wide in terror as his throat was seized. He tried to shout but no sound came out. Before he could even see who was behind him, a numbing sensation spread through his acupoints, and in the next moment, he collapsed unconscious.","Inside the room, the previously unconscious Lady Song was now bound by a rope that cinched tightly around her voluptuous figure, accentuating her curves. The sight left Cheng Wanli parched and breathless with excitement.","He produced a small vial, opened it, and waved its contents near her nostrils. Soon, the unconscious Lady Song slowly stirred awake. Upon seeing Cheng Wanli standing by the bed and realizing she was bound, her face instantly drained of color. She opened her mouth to cry out, only to discover she could not make a sound.","\"Lady Song, awake?\"","Cheng Wanli smiled at her. \"Who knew Brother Song enjoyed such good fortune? To have such a lovely wife at home yet still leave her for ten days or even half a month—that takes some nerve!\"","Watching her struggle on the bed, trying desperately to shout, he chuckled. \" Don’t be afraid, don’t panic. We have all night to play. I, Cheng Wanli, have seen countless beauties. Truly, the beauties of this world come in all shapes and forms, each unique. Especially someone like you, Lady Song, you are truly exceptional.\"","As he spoke, he took another step closer, sat down beside the bed, and reached out to touch Lady Song’s thigh.","Lady Song recoiled in alarm, scrambling to the corner of the bed to evade his hand.","Her reaction only fueled his smug excitement. \"Heh, no need to panic. After tonight, you won’t remember a thing come morning. Even if we share a night of passion, I have ways to erase tonight’s events from your mind. Even if Song Lingbo returns, he’ll never know his woman has been with me.\"","\"Oh? What method? So powerful?\"","A soft, slow voice drifted over, tinged with nonchalance. Yet within that voice lay a thread of coldness, unnoticed by anyone.","\"Who’s there!\"","Cheng Wanli shouted with annoyance, attempting to turn, only to feel something pierce his body. He froze instantly, his entire body’s spiritual energy sealed, leaving him utterly immobilized.","Huddled in the corner of the bed, Lady Song saw the figure in azure appear. Her expression flickered between surprise, shock, and worry. She hadn’t expected that with just one move, she had subdued Cheng Wanli.","\"My apologies for arriving late and causing you alarm.\"","Feng Jiu glanced apologetically at the pale-faced Lady Song in the corner. With a flick of her finger, she released the acupoints binding her. Another wave of her hand dispelled the spiritual energy from the celestial rope binding her, leaving it as a useless, ordinary rope that fell to the floor."]},{"number":5010,"title":"Chapter 5010: Clean Up","paragraphs":["\"Lady Xuanyuan, how did you get here?\"","Lady Song rose swiftly, grabbed her outer robe, and pulled it on before approaching her. Her face still bore a hint of pallor, but she forced down her panic and regained her composure.","Feng Jiu smiled, glancing at Cheng Wanli. \"I noticed his gaze toward you was off earlier today. When I came out for a stroll at night, I saw him sneaking toward your quarters in the dark. That’s why I followed to check.\"","Her voice trailed off as her gaze fixed on the man. \"Lady Song, what do you suggest we do with him?\"","\"This...\"","Lady Song froze, momentarily at a loss. Killing him was out of the question—the Cheng family was far too powerful for the Song clan to provoke. But if they spared him, word of tonight’s incident would spread...","\"Lady Xuanyuan, what should we do? I... I don’t know what to do...\" Tonight’s fright had left her shaken. Though she had calmed down somewhat, her heart still hadn’t fully settled. Asking her to handle this, she truly didn’t know how to proceed.","\"Who are you? \"Have you no desire to live? Daring to touch me? Do you not fear ending up with no place to bury your remains?\" Cheng Wanli’s voice was dark and menacing. He realized that aside from his spirit energy being sealed and his body immobilized, he could still speak.","However, he noticed that at some point, a soundproof barrier had been cast over the room. Thinking of this woman who had appeared without a sound, he narrowed his eyes and stared intently at the woman before him.","She wore plain azure robes, unremarkable and inconspicuous, much like her unassuming features. On the street, she likely wouldn’t draw a second glance.","Yet, her gaze was serene and detached. Her aura was restrained, making her cultivation level hard to gauge, yet an unusual presence emanated from her.","That presence... was that of a powerful being!","\"No place to bury my remains?\" Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow, a smile fleeted across. She then fixated her gaze, when an indescribable grin appeared on her face. With a flick of her finger, several streams of energy struck him three inches below his navel.","\"Hmph!\"","A muffled groan escaped him as his face twisted. \"What did you do to me?!\"","\"Merely crippled your seed.\" Feng Jiu’s lips curved. \"It was bound to be useless eventually anyway. Isn’t it more efficient for me to disable it now?\"","\"You bitch! I’ll kill you!\" he roared, veins bulging on his neck from the fury, yet unable to break free from his immobilized body.","\"Shut your filthy mouth!\"","As Feng Jiu’s voice cut through the air, her hand shot up, and a shadow streaked past.","\"Smack! Smack! Smack!\"","Three resounding slaps landed on Cheng Wanli’s face. She hadn’t used her palms to strike him; instead, she’d channeled the force of her palm wind. The power generated by that wind was no less devastating than a direct palm strike.","After the three slaps, his face swelled up, and a thread of blood appeared at the corner of his mouth.","\"How dare you hit me! You should—\"","His words trailed off as a piercing scream erupted. Lady Song froze beside them, her hands clamped over her mouth. Stunned and horrified, she watched as Lady Xuanyuan lift her leg directly, aiming a kick straight for Cheng Wanli’s groin. The sheer force of that strike made her wince in pain just watching, let alone how the receiver felt.","\"Thud!\"","Cheng Wanli stumbled backward, unable to maintain his balance. He collapsed onto the ground, his face instantly draining from crimson rage to deathly pallor. An indescribable agony surged through him, leaving him gasping for breath in agony."]},{"number":5011,"title":"Chapter 5011: Refuse to Speak","paragraphs":["Capítulo 5011: Refuse to Speak","“Can’t handle this much?” Feng Jiu sneered coldly, planting her foot squarely on his arm and crushing it clean off. A faint gasp reached her ears.","Only then did she seem to recall Lady Song standing nearby. Withdrawing her foot, she flashed an apologetic smile and turned to her. “Did I scare you? Honestly, I’m not usually like this.”","Lady Song’s heart pounded wildly. Her eyes held disbelief, as if seeing Feng Jiu for the first time. She swallowed hard and shook her head. “I-I’m not scared. I just... I just never imagined Lady Xuanyuan would be like this...”","She wasn’t frightened, but she simply couldn’t have imagined that the gentle, approachable Lady Xuanyuan she’d known these past days could be... this kind of person.","What kind of person? For a moment, she couldn’t find the words to describe her. All she knew was that this Lady Xuanyuan made her feel strangely secure. Everything she herself dared not do, this woman had done.","“Um, Lady Xuanyuan, what should we do with him now? His men are still staying in the guest quarters. If something happens to him...” She glanced at Cheng Wanli, lying on the ground, barely clinging to life after his torture, and felt a pang of worry.","Her worry wasn’t about his death itself, but the trouble it would bring upon the Song family if he died.","“Oh, don’t worry,” Feng Jiu patted her shoulder and smiled. “I’ve got everything covered! Not just them—even if the entire Cheng family came looking, I could protect your Song family without a care.”","Hearing her words, seeing the confidence in her tone and the resolute gleam in her eyes, Lady Song found herself momentarily lost in thought.","After a moment, she said, “Then let’s do this! Drive them out of the Song manor. Such people shouldn’t be allowed to stay here. With my husband away, if you hadn’t been here tonight, the consequences would have been unimaginable.”","Recalling the earlier incident, a wave of dread washed over her. Had Lady Xuanyuan not arrived in time, she feared she might have been...","The thought filled her with fury. Stepping forward, she mimicked Lady Xuanyuan’s action, delivering a vicious kick straight to his groin. “That damned man! I wish I could kill him!”","At this moment, Cheng Wanli could only emit muffled groans and cries of pain. His most vulnerable spot had been struck twice—both kicks heavy and vicious. That he hadn’t fainted on the spot was fortunate enough.","“I heard they came to your manor to retrieve something,” Feng Jiu stated, her gaze fixed on the pale-faced Cheng Wanli on the ground.","“What do they want?” Lady Song froze, utterly bewildered.","“Then we’ll have to ask him.” Feng Jiu smiled, twirling a dagger in her hand as she fixed her gaze on Cheng Wanli. “Speak! Why did you come to the Song manor for? What did you intend to take?”","“You bitch! You’ll never get a word out of me!” he snarled, glaring at the woman in the blue robe.","He seethed inwardly: Once he discovered who this woman truly was, he would wipe out her entire clan! She would have no place to be buried! No—she would die a thousand cuts, suffering every possible humiliation!","“Arghhhhhhh!”","Suddenly, another piercing scream echoed through the room. Feng Jiu, twirling a dagger in her hand, drove it viciously into Cheng Wanli’s thigh. The blade pierced clean through, blood instantly seeping out, soaking his trousers and dripping onto the floor."]},{"number":5012,"title":"Chapter 5012: Truth","paragraphs":["Capítulo 5012: Truth","“Not talking? It’s alright. I’ll just use you for practice.” Feng Jiu tugged at the corner of her mouth, a smile playing on her face, though her eyes remained icy cold.","She pulled the dagger from Cheng Wanli’s thigh, drawing a spurt of blood with it. Her hand rose, and the dagger fell again—this time, striking the exact same spot, the same wound.","“Arghhhh!”","The same wound was stabbed again. This time, the blade wasn’t withdrawn but slowly twisted inside, practically carving out a bloody hole. The excruciating pain made him feel like he was dying and coming back to life over and over.","He nearly passed out several times, only to be woken by the agony each time. Now, he couldn’t even scream. His lips trembled, unable to form a single word.","Feng Jiu pulled the dagger free, wiping it on Cheng Wanli’s clothes. Glancing at the bloodstains on the floor, she turned to Lady Song beside her and said, “I’ve dirtied this room. Have it cleaned properly later.”","“Yes, yes.” Lady Song nodded blankly, utterly speechless.","“Will you talk or not?”","Feng Jiu pressed, twirling the dagger in her hand. Truth-inducing medicinal pills were plentiful in her spatial pouch, but why spare this despicable man? He’d dared covet a married woman and fallen into her trap—she wouldn’t let him off easy.","Watching the dagger spin in her hand, Cheng Wanli’s eyes filled with terror. Forcing himself to speak, he gasped, “I... I’ll tell you... I... I came for the Song family’s Rainbow Faceted Spirit Stone.”","He swallowed hard, afraid she wouldn’t believe him, and hurriedly added, ” Truly, I truly came for that Rainbow Faceted Spirit Stone. We knew the Song family possessed one—an exceedingly rare treasure—and intended to present it to the Old Predecessor as a birthday gift.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu shot him a glance. Seeing the terror etched across his face, she snorted derisively before turning to Lady Song beside her: “Is there such an item?”","Lady Song paused at the mention of the Rainbow Faceted Spirit Stone. Hearing Lady Xuanyuan’s inquiry, she nodded. “Our Song family does indeed possess a Rainbow Faceted Spirit Stone. It was a treasure obtained by our Song family’s Old Predecessor. However, I’ve only seen it once.”","She never imagined this Rainbow Faceted Spirit Stone would draw the attention of a family like the Chengs, who now sought to seize it. Her husband had mentioned it was a rare treasure, but she’d never inquired about its rarity or purpose. After all, it had remained in the cave abode of the Old Predecessor for so long, unseen.","“I’m not lying. I truly came for that Rainbow Faceted Spirit Stone. Really, please let me go! Release me, and this matter ends here. I won’t trouble you, nor will I trouble the Song family.” Cheng Wanli spoke, glancing at the green-clad woman playing with her dagger. A flicker of fear crossed his eyes as he added, ” If you kill me, the Song family will face trouble. It could even lead to a clan-wide catastrophe. Have you... have you thought this through?”","Hearing this, Lady Song’s heart sank with worry. Yet, glancing toward Lady Xuanyuan, she saw the woman’s expression was relaxed and composed, showing not a trace of fear or panic. Her own initial concerns gradually eased.","Though she knew nothing of Lady Xuanyuan’s background, the fact that she dared to strike at Cheng Wanli like this suggested she had some backing. At worst, they could always turn to the Azure Emperor for help. After all, with his three disciples as intermediaries, if the Azure Emperor intervened, the Cheng family wouldn’t dare lay a finger on the Song family."]},{"number":5013,"title":"Chapter 5013: Sweep in like the wind","paragraphs":["Capítulo 5013: Sweep in like the wind","Listening to his half-threatening words, Feng Jiu laughed. She shot a playful glance at Cheng Wanli, whose face had gone deathly pale, and asked, “And who is that woman in the room?”","“She’s my wife...” He was cut off before he could finish.","“You’d better tell me the truth. Try to pull the wool over my eyes, and you know the consequences.” She toyed with the dagger in her hand, speaking slowly and deliberately.","His face twitched as he looked at the dagger. His lips quivered slightly before he finally said, “She’s a woman I abducted. I intended to take her home as a concubine.”","Feng Jiu, who had long suspected as much, showed no surprise. Fixing her gaze on Cheng Wanli lying on the ground, she curled her lips into a cold smile. “Killing you would only dirty this courtyard. Instead, I’ll strip you of your cultivation! Upon returning, have the Cheng family bring substantial gifts to apologize. Otherwise, I’ll ensure your family plummets from a top-tier noble house to a third-rate minor clan!”","As the words fell, she reached out and stripped him of his cultivation. A piercing scream erupted as his face rapidly aged, his body withering away until he lay on the floor, barely clinging to life, twitching faintly.","Feng Jiu swept her sleeve, dispelling the sound-proofing barrier within the room. She turned to Lady Song beside her and said, “Summon some servants. Have them thrown out.”","“Yes.” Lady Song responded with a slight pause, obediently following her instructions. She glanced down to check her clothes before walking to the door. Upon opening it, she saw the figure lying in the courtyard.","Her eyes flickered, lips pressed together. She drew a deep breath, ready to call for help, but then seemed to recall something. Turning back to Feng Jiu, she hesitated, “Lady Xuanyuan, if we call for help now, the Cheng family’s men will surely sweep in like the wind. We...”","“It matters not. Have them come. The Cheng family’s men are no threat.” Feng Jiu said with a faint smile.","Seeing her confident demeanor, Lady Song finally called out, “Where are the guards?” Her voice, infused with spirit energy, carried clearly across half the estate.","Almost instantly, the hidden guards heard her voice, their hearts sinking and expressions shifting. They swiftly made their way to the main courtyard. Upon arriving, they witnessed Lady Xuanyuan, clad in azure, crippling the cultivation of an unconscious elderly man from the Cheng family lying in the courtyard. They couldn’t help but gasp slightly.","Suppressing their shock and fear, several hidden guards quickly stepped forward, clasped their fists, and bowed: ” Your servants pay their respects, My lady!”","As soon as the words left their mouths and the salute was completed, the leader of the guards glanced around the courtyard. Smelling the scent of blood spreading, he asked, “My lady, what has happened?”","“First, drag the person out of the room. Then check if our men are unconscious or if anything has happened to them,” Lady Song instructed, signaling for them to proceed to the room and pull the person out.","“Yes, my lady!”","Hearing that someone had entered the lady’s chambers, their hearts tightened. They immediately entered the room only to be stunned by the scene before them. Cheng Wanli, whom they had seen welcomed into the courtyard as an honored guest just today, now lay covered in wounds, drenched in blood. His cultivation had been completely stripped away, and his entire being appeared aged and emaciated.","Recalling how Lady Xuanyuan had stripped that old man of his cultivation upon entering the courtyard earlier, and now witnessing this scene, it wasn’t hard to deduce that Cheng Wanli’s current state was her doing.","Quickly regaining their composure, they dragged him out and tossed him into the courtyard. Just then, a furious shout echoed through the air."]},{"number":5014,"title":"Chapter 5014: Rush In","paragraphs":["Capítulo 5014: Rush In","“Who dares to harm a member of the Cheng family!”","The Cheng family members in the courtyard rushed over, led by three elders followed by guards. Their arrival swiftly encircled the entire main courtyard.","The three elders landed in the courtyard and swiftly approached the other elderly man beside Cheng Wanli. Upon seeing his state, they all gasped in unison.","“Whoa!”","“His cultivation... his cultivation has been crippled!”","Having one’s cultivation stripped away meant one’s entire being was rendered useless. Cheng Wanli was somewhat fortunate—his age was still relatively young, and though his cultivation was gone, his lifespan remained intact. But for the other elder? With his cultivation stripped, he likely had little time left to live.","“Who? Who did this?!”","The three elders roared in fury, their rage boiling over. How could they possibly explain this to the Patriarch? Cheng Wanli was the Patriarch’s own flesh and blood. The Patriarch had always treated him with great favor, rarely reprimanding him even when he acted recklessly outside. Now, with his cultivation destroyed, they could only imagine the terrifying wrath they would face upon returning.","“What’s happened? What’s going on?”","The Song family elders, hearing the news, hurried over in their outer robes, some still tying their garments as they walked. Seeing the furious expressions on the Cheng family members in the courtyard, they paused slightly, their gazes settling on the two individuals whose cultivation had been stripped.","After a moment’s scrutiny, they recognized them as Cheng Wanli and an elderly member of the Cheng family. Yet at this moment, both lay on the ground, barely clinging to life.","The elders exchanged glances, their brows furrowing in concern. Instead of questioning the Cheng family members, they turned directly to Lady Song and demanded, “What is going on? Aren’t those two from the Cheng family? Why are they in the main courtyard?”","“Cheng Wanli infiltrated the main courtyard at night with ill intent toward me,” Lady Song stated simply. Her words alone were enough for everyone present to understand the situation.","A flicker of anger flashed across the faces of the clan elders upon hearing this. Yet, upon seeing the two men on the ground—their cultivation stripped and their bodies covered in wounds—they suppressed their fury.","They had believed the Cheng family, a noble house backed by nine formidable experts, would be beneficial allies for the Song clan. Little did they expect these men to harbor such ulterior motives!","“To think such shameless scoundrels exist within a family of mighty warriors!” declared the Grand Elder, his aged voice thick with anger and contempt.","“Hmph!”","An elder of the Cheng family let out a heavy snort, his imposing aura surging toward the Song family members. Narrowing his eyes with a grim expression, he barked, “To cripple the cultivation of two of my Cheng family members—you Song family have quite the skill!”","His gaze swept over the crowd in the courtyard, yet he could not discern anyone capable of crippling two members of the mighty Cheng clan.","“Who dared to strike? Come forward now! Or else, do not blame us for slaughtering your entire Song family tonight!” The elder’s grim eyes scanned the assembled crowd as his voice, thick with murderous intent, echoed through the courtyard.","Hearing this, several Song family elders exchanged bewildered glances. How could they possibly know who had crippled those two? Yet, since it happened on Song family grounds, they were undoubtedly implicated.","As they pondered, a voice emerged, unhurried and deliberate. At the same time, a figure stepped forward at a measured pace."]},{"number":5015,"title":"Chapter 5015: Kneel","paragraphs":["Capítulo 5015: Kneel","“Exterminate the entire Song family? That’s quite the boast.”","Feng Jiu stepped forward slowly. Yet, the instant her foot moved, a green figure flickered like a ghostly apparition. In a flash, it darted behind one of the elders, its hand clamping down on his throat.","“Ah!”","The old man gasped in shock. His throat was seized and lifted upward, forcing his entire body to involuntarily rise onto tiptoes, chin slightly raised in a futile attempt to ease the suffocating pressure.","The stench of death enveloped him in that instant. The scene unfolded so unexpectedly that he had no time to react before falling into the other’s grasp, his life force choked, unable to move.","“You’re the one who crippled their cultivation!”","Seeing the unassuming woman in green strike, the other two elders immediately realized they had fallen victim to this woman!","She was quite skilled indeed, managing to strip both of their cultivation and wound them so severely.","At this realization, their eyes narrowed, a flash of icy coldness passing through them. “If I were you, I’d release him and flee for your life right now. Otherwise, you’ll end up with no place to bury your remains!”","“Is that so?” Feng Jiu sneered coldly. Her other hand shot out, instantly stripping the cultivation from the old man she held captive.","“Aah!”","A piercing scream of agony and refusal rang out. Visibly, the old man rapidly aged before their eyes, his body shriveling and wasting away until, his cultivation completely destroyed, Feng Jiu tossed him aside.","“To avoid defiling this main courtyard, I’ll show mercy and spare your lives—granting you a few more days.” Feng Jiu curled her lips, wiping her hands with a handkerchief. Her gaze shifted, landing on the two elders frozen in shock and terror. “Will you cripple yourselves? Or shall I do it for you?”","“Who... who are you?”","One who could seize them with a single move possessed strength far surpassing their own. Especially when this woman, who rarely acted, unleashed such ruthless, decisive killing intent—it sent an inexplicable chill down their spines.","Her calm gaze, those bottomless eyes, and the faint smile playing at her lips all made her seem profoundly mysterious and dangerously unpredictable in that moment.","“Demoness! Take this old man’s palm!” An elderly man clenched his blade, channeling spirit energy as he lunged forward. His palm strike whistled through the air toward Feng Jiu. Unexpectedly, the powerful blow was effortlessly deflected by a flick of her sleeve.","As he stared in stunned disbelief, her voice echoed through the air.","“Demoness? Hah! The last person who called me that hasn’t even left behind a skeleton.”","Feng Jiu laughed coldly, simultaneously unleashing a palm strike that slammed heavily into the old man’s body, sending him flying backward.","“Thud!”","“Pfft!”","The old man’s body slammed into the corner, blood spurting from his mouth. He struggled to rise, but after a long struggle, he couldn’t even stand. Finally, he collapsed there, gasping for breath.","“What are you all standing around for? Get in here!” another old man roared, summoning the guards stationed outside.","The Song family elders were about to intervene when suddenly, the figure of the green-robed woman Shadow One. In an instant, she appeared before the enraged elder.","The Cheng family elder stared at the green-robed woman before him. A powerful aura of intimidation washed over him, overwhelming him completely. He collapsed to his knees, unable to withstand it."]},{"number":5016,"title":"Chapter 5016: Who","paragraphs":["Capítulo 5016: Who","Thud!","The heavy thud of knees striking the hard ground echoed through the air. The old man’s face instantly drained of color, cold sweat the size of beans beading on his forehead and trickling down his cheeks.","His heart raced with terror as he stared at the woman in the blue robe before him, despair welling in his eyes.","The others before him had either been stripped of their cultivation or left gravely wounded. As for him, death seemed inevitable. This thought filled him with bitter resentment, yet he was utterly powerless.","For at this moment, he understood clearly that this woman’s power far surpassed theirs. Their own aura exerted no pressure on her whatsoever. On the contrary, the moment her aura manifested, they dared not even draw a breath, forced to their knees against their will.","Feng Jiu cast a cold glance at the old man on the ground. With a flick of her sleeve, she sent the advancing guards flying. Simultaneously, she ordered, “Seize them.” Her gaze shifted indifferently to the captain of the Song family’s secret guards.","“Yes.” Almost instinctively, the Song family’s secret guard captain responded. The moment the words left his mouth, he froze, glancing at their mistress. Seeing no reaction from her, he swiftly moved forward to seize the guards.","“I spare your lives for two reasons: first, I refuse to soil this courtyard with blood; second, I need you to deliver a message back—tell the Cheng family Patriarch to personally bring substantial gifts to apologize, otherwise, I won’t hesitate to make you suffer!”","As her words fell, she swept her sleeve again. The man kneeling on the ground was violently flung away, crashing beside the old man in the corner.","The Song family members hadn’t even had a chance to speak. No, more accurately, they had been frozen in shock the moment the green-clad woman appeared. Who was she? How dare she? And how had she so effortlessly reduced them to the brink of death, leaving them utterly powerless to resist?","“Throw them out of the Song manor.” Lady Song commanded.","“Yes, ma’am!” The shadow guards responded, swiftly dragging the men out of the estate.","She then ordered maidservants to clean the courtyard, thoroughly removing every trace of blood.","The Song family elders, other members, and the shadow guards all watched this scene in stunned silence. They had expected a fierce battle, perhaps even needing to intervene themselves. Yet suddenly, it felt as though they had merely come to make up the numbers, utterly useless.","Under cover of night, as the discarded Cheng family guards escorted the dying men away, the Song family’s secret guards dispatched one or two men to secretly follow them.","Back in the main courtyard, Feng Jiu turned to Lady Song and said, “Now that we’ve driven them out, there shouldn’t be any trouble for the time being. Have someone check on that woman in the room to see what’s going on. I’ll leave the rest to you. I’m going back to rest.”","With that, she waved her hand and strode toward the exit, intending to return to her quarters for sleep.","After she departed, the Old Predecessor of the Song family gathered around and asked, “Who is she? How did she get involved in this? Now that the elders of the Cheng family have stripped their cultivation and suffered grievous injuries, who is it that dares demand the Cheng family come apologize? Is that even possible? I fear our Song family has stirred up a huge mess this time.”","The elders shook their heads and sighed softly. Recalling tonight’s events, their moods grew increasingly heavy."]},{"number":5017,"title":"Chapter 5017: Ke Meng","paragraphs":["Capítulo 5017: Ke Meng","Lady Song, seeing this, spoke up: “Since things have come to this, further words are useless. I’ll send word for Lingbo and the others to return first. For now, let’s go see that woman in the guest quarters!” With that, she took several people and headed toward the guest quarters.","The next day, around noon, Lady Song arrived at the courtyard where Feng Jiu resided and waited. She had many questions to ask her and couldn’t sleep, so she decided to come here and wait for her to wake up.","When Feng Jiu finished washing up and stepped out of her room, she saw Lady Song sitting there. She walked over and said, “Good morning.”","“Lady Xuanyuan, I have matters I wish to discuss with you, hence my early arrival.” She spoke as she watched her sit down, then inquired, “Lady Xuanyuan, regarding the Song family’s departure in such a manner—you suggested they come to apologize. Considering their family standing, I doubt that will suffice. Not only will it likely fail, but it may provoke them to retaliate against the Song family. What do you think of this...”","“Rest assured, I won’t leave until this matter is resolved!” She smiled, lifted the teacup before her, and took a light sip. “Did Mi’er never mention my background to you?”","At this, Lady Song paused slightly, then shook her head. “Mi’er didn’t say. She only mentioned you were a very important friend of hers and asked me to treat you well.”","Hearing this, could it be... she possessed some astonishing background? Thinking of the three children Mi’er had brought back this time—those three claimed to be disciples of the Azure Emperor, and she seemed familiar with them. Could it be... this Lady Xuanyuan was acquainted with the Azure Emperor?","A flurry of thoughts flashed through her mind, sparking a vague suspicion. If she were indeed acquainted with the Azure Emperor—and on particularly good terms—it would explain why she looked down on prominent families like the Chengs and why she possessed the power to cripple those elderly Cheng elders.","This thought brought her some measure of calm. “By the way,” she said, “I went to that guesthouse last night. That young lady is the daughter of a minor family. Because of her beauty, Cheng Wanli took a fancy to her. He wiped out her entire family, leaving only her alive, and then took her away.”","Her voice softened as she sighed, “The poor girl bears numerous wounds, both large and small. Yet she mentioned that since her injuries hadn’t healed, Cheng Wanli never touched her. She remains a pure maiden to this day. When I arrived, I instructed the servants to help her bathe and groom herself. She’ll be coming over shortly to thank you in person.”","Lady Song paused before adding, “One more thing—because of the incident at the mansion, I sent word last night to Lingbo and his father and brothers, asking them to return sooner.”","Feng Jiu nodded. “Yes, I understand.” As they spoke, the corner of her eye caught a figure approaching the courtyard gate, and the maid’s voice drifted in from outside.","“My lady, Lady Xuanyuan, Miss Ke requests an audience.”","Lady Song glanced at Feng Jiu before calling out, “Let her in!”","Shortly after, a woman dressed in plain white robes entered. Her gaze swept over the two women, lingering longer on the plain-featured woman in the blue robe before she curtsied to both of them.","“Ke Meng greets both ladies.” After her bow, she knelt before the woman in blue: “Ke Meng thanks you, My lady, for saving my life.”"]},{"number":5018,"title":"Chapter 5018: A Beauty Who Brings Misfortune","paragraphs":["Capítulo 5018: A Beauty Who Brings Misfortune","Feng Jiu glanced at her. After a night’s rest, the woman’s spirits had lifted considerably. She wore a simple white gown, with only a small white flower in her hair. Her exquisite features were tinged with a touch of sorrow and melancholy between her brows, adding a delicate vulnerability to her beauty. Combined with her slightly pale complexion and a slender waist that seemed too fragile to grasp, one couldn’t help but acknowledge she was a beauty who stirred pity in any man who laid eyes on her.","No wonder a lecher like Cheng Wanli would wipe out her entire family for a woman like this.","It could only be said: a beautiful woman is a source of trouble.","Sometimes, a woman’s peerless beauty is not necessarily a blessing. Without formidable strength to match such stunning looks, she invites disaster upon herself and may even drag her family into ruin.","She herself possessed such a face, one that had brought her no small amount of trouble—though she had always managed to defuse it. The woman before her, with such beauty yet lacking powerful backing or strength, was bound to catch the eye of lecherous men. It was hardly surprising.","“How did Cheng Wanli come to target you?” Feng Jiu stirred her tea absently, her question laced with casual indifference. She made no move to help the woman rise, allowing her to remain kneeling.","“It began when I was stopped by him one day while out. But I never imagined he would dare to invade my home under cover of night, slaughtering every last one of my family—over a hundred souls!” Ke Meng’s eyes flashed with hatred as she recounted this, but recalling Lady Song’s words from last night, she took a deep breath and suppressed the bitterness within.","“I thought I too would fall victim to his cruelty. Yet My lady saved me. Her kindness is beyond measure. Ke Meng has no way to repay such a debt... I can only...” She was cut off before finishing her sentence.","“Enough.” Feng Jiu replaced the lid on her tea cup, then looked at the kneeling Ke Meng. “You may withdraw.”","Ke Meng paused, glancing up at her before quickly lowering her head again. “Yes, Ke Meng takes her leave.” She rose, performed a curtsy, and exited.","Lady Song had been watching quietly from the side. Seeing Feng Jiu dismiss the servant, she asked with a smile, “Does Lady Xuanyuan dislike her?”","Feng Jiu smiled faintly, meeting her gaze. “To me, she is merely a stranger. There is no question of liking or disliking.” She paused, then inquired, “I wonder how Lady Song intends to arrange matters for her?”","Lady Song’s face softened into a gentle smile as she replied softly, “She is still injured. Once her wounds have healed, she shall be sent away.”","“Very well,” Feng Jiu nodded, satisfied with this arrangement. Moreover, such a decision showed that Lady Song possessed clear-sightedness.","Within the Song residence, Song Lingbo was in the prime of his life, and his three sons were all grown men. Keeping such a woman—one of breathtaking beauty and delicate grace that stirred pity in all who saw her—within the household was hardly a wise move. Letting her go was indeed the best arrangement.","Meanwhile, back in the guest quarters, Ke Meng sat before the mirror in her room, lost in thought. She was no longer a wealthy young lady. Her entire family had been wiped out. Now, she was merely a homeless, lonely woman.","And a woman of extraordinary beauty at that.","Gazing at the exquisite face reflected in the mirror, she drifted into a daze. According to Lady Song, Cheng Wanli had been stripped of his cultivation and suffered severe injuries. Even if he hadn’t died, he was nothing more than a cripple now."]},{"number":5019,"title":"Chapter 5019: Knowing","paragraphs":["Capítulo 5019: Knowing","Has her family’s vengeance been fulfilled? But where does she go from here? With a face like hers, stepping outside would surely draw the attention of lecherous men once more.","She raised her hand to gently caress her exquisite features, her brow furrowing slightly. A trace of sorrow graced her face, making her appear all the more pitiable and captivating.","“What should I do?” she murmured softly.","Meanwhile, deep within the forest, Song Lingbo and his companions all wore delighted smiles. Yesterday, they had discovered many valuable items in this area and even hunted down several high-tier fierce beasts. After working through the night, they had just finished their tasks and sat down to rest.","“Father, something’s happened at home! Mother says we must hurry back!” Song Lingbo’s second brother stowed the gathered ingredients into his interspatial ring before noticing the message from his communication jade. He immediately relayed the news to his father.","“We received word from Mother too. She says we should return quickly,” added Song Lingbo’s third brother.","Song Lingbo’s heart sank upon hearing this. “Did your Mother say what happened?” he asked, retrieving his own communication jade to listen.","“She didn’t say much, just told us to hurry back,” the brothers replied, shaking their heads.","After hearing the message from the communication jade, which confirmed their words, Song Lingbo immediately barked at the group, “Pack up and return to the city swiftly!”","Song Mi’er, Hao’er, and the other three had just returned after washing their faces. Before they could approach, they overheard the order. Exchanging glances, they hurried over.","“Father, did Mother mention what happened?” Song Mi’er asked.","“She only said something happened at home. It must be serious—otherwise, your mother wouldn’t have summoned us,” Song Lingbo replied, his brow furrowed with worry. Concerned about the situation at home, he ordered everyone to prepare quickly, skipping rest to make ready for the return journey.","Hearing this, Song Mi’er promptly retrieved her communication jade from her interspatial ring. Unlike her three brothers and Father, her message stated that something had happened at home, but her friend, Lady Xuanyuan, had offered assistance. She also inquired about Lady Xuanyuan’s background.","“Lady Xuanyuan? The friend you mentioned?” Song Lingbo heard the message and turned to ask Mi’er.","“Oh, yes, that’s her.”","Mi’er paused, then nodded. “Father, brothers, don’t worry. With Lady Xuanyuan at our home, nothing bad will happen.” Her Master was incredibly capable! With her staying as a guest in their home, even if something truly happened, she wouldn’t stand idly by.","Song Lingbo frowned and asked, “Then who exactly is Lady Xuanyuan? How do you know nothing will happen with her here? What is her background? How could she possess such immense power? She resolved an issue that even our Song family elders couldn’t handle?”","“Hehe, Father, this Lady Xuanyuan—she’s quite formidable!” she said mysteriously, then laughed. “But since she’s here now, and we’ve gained quite a bit during this time, let’s head home! But don’t worry, everything will be fine at home.”","Hao’er and the other two nodded in agreement beside her. With their Mother residing at the Song family estate, who would be so foolish as to cause trouble for the Song family? Wouldn’t that be courting death?","Yet, despite her words, Song Lingbo couldn’t help but feel anxious knowing trouble had struck home. Glancing up at the sky, he declared, “We can save considerable time by flying our swords out of the forest. But flying our swords will inevitably bring us face-to-face with those Vittle Spirit Birds. Everyone, prepare for battle!”"]},{"number":5020,"title":"Chapter 5020: Returns","paragraphs":["Capítulo 5020: Returns","“Yes!” the guards responded in unison.","“Three share one sword. One focuses solely on piloting the sword flight, while the other two prepare for combat. Yi Hong, you and the others protect Mi’er and the three children in the center. I’ll lead the way. Jingwei, pilot your swords to guard the perimeter. Avoid prolonged engagements—our primary goal is to exit the forest! Is that understood?” Song Lingbo’s command rang out, his voice resonant and commanding. Instantly, the spirits of the Jingwei warriors were stirred, each preparing for battle.","“Understood!” the group responded in unison, swiftly forming ranks before soaring alongside him in the sword. They shot upward from the dense canopy, sweeping past towering trees and soaring high into the sky.","Hao’er and the others wanted to protest that they could fight and didn’t need protection, but seeing the solemn expressions on the Song family members, they held their tongues.","Learning of trouble at home, they were likely eager to return. Yet, the more anxious they were, the more likely they were to encounter further peril.","Hao’er and the others each followed one of the Song brothers. Surrounded by Jingwei guards and with Song Lingbo leading the way, they flew a distance without incident. Soon, however, a shrill cry pierced the sky.","“Vittle Spirit Bird! Everyone, beware!” a guard cried out, instantly tightening the atmosphere.","Hao’er turned to look and saw a flock of Vittle Spirit Birds flapping their wings and screeching as they flew toward them. Their numbers were so great that they appeared as a dark, oppressive mass.","Song Lingbo also spotted the massive flock of Vittle Spirit Birds. His heart sank slightly at the sheer number, but the blade in his hand shifted. Spirit energy surged as he suddenly drew a deep breath and swung his blade down with tremendous force toward the advancing Vittle Spirit Birds.","“Hah!”","A low shout erupted simultaneously with a whistling blade aura. Spirit energy currents and the blade aura coalesced into a massive, visible blade that roared through the air, slashing down at the flock of Vittle Spirit Birds.","Whoosh!","The blade’s aura sliced through the air, scattering the flock of Vittle Spirit Birds. Most veered left or right to evade the strike, but a few were caught unawares. They were cleaved clean through, letting out shrill cries as they plummeted into the forest below.","“Flutter, flutter, flutter...”","The Vittle Spirit Birds drew ever closer, their wing beats growing louder as they approached. Dispersed by that single slash, they now surged forward in a wave, closing in from all sides. Huge talons and beaks attacked simultaneously, clawing and tearing at them.","“Hah!”","“You’re asking for death!”","The Jingwei warriors roared, their swords and blades striking out at the same moment, slashing at the diving Vittle Spirit Birds.","Hao’er and the others were shielded in the center. Even as the Vittle Spirit Birds closed in to attack, they couldn’t immediately reach the group in the middle.","“Sssshhh!”","Chaotic screeches filled the air, mingled with the faint flutter of falling feathers. The Song brothers and Mi’er shielded Hao’er and the others. When the birds found their attacks blocked, some wisely soared high, then dove down from above.","“Kill them!”","Song Lingbo roared, soaring into the air. His blade swept downward, slicing a diving Vittle Spirit Bird clean out of the sky. His blade spun again, striking at the surrounding Vittle Spirit Birds.","Despite their formidable strength and combat prowess, the relentless barrage left many among them wounded. Scratches of varying sizes marred their skin—some resembling claw marks, others like gashes torn by beaks.","Hao’er and the others watched, clenching their fists tightly. Had they not been bound by Mother’s warning to conceal the existence of the ancient Sacred Beast, they would have rushed to aid their comrades in that very moment."]},{"number":5021,"title":"Chapter 5021: It’s Me","paragraphs":["However, Song Lingbo’s strength was indeed formidable. Coupled with the fact that the guard birds accompanying them this time were all top-tier fighters, though wounded, their injuries were not life-threatening. After a fierce battle, the Vittle Spirit Birds ceased their harassment, and the group pressed onward, each bearing their wounds...","The next day, as soon as the city gates opened, they headed toward the Song family estate. As it was still early, the streets were relatively empty. Nevertheless, when the passersby saw the group returning, each bearing wounds and looking thoroughly exhausted, they stared in astonishment for a long while.","Hao’er and Muchen kept pace with the others as they hurried along, while Yue’er slept soundly, carried on Mi’er’s back.","After knocking open the mansion gate, Song Lingbo strode inside, instructing those behind him, \"Guard, go rest first! Yihong, you three also go wash up before coming back. Tend to your wounds a bit so that your Mother won’t worry. Mi’er, take the three children back to the courtyard to sleep.\"","\"Yes, sir.\" They responded in unison, watching him stride deeper into the mansion before dispersing.","When Song Lingbo returned to the main courtyard, Lady Song had not yet awakened. As the door creaked open, he entered with hushed footsteps, drawing a chill breeze into the room.","Startled, Lady Song jolted awake, eyes snapping open as she sat bolt upright. \"Who’s there!\"","Ever since that fateful night, her sleep had grown restless, her heart constantly guarding against the fear of intruders.","\"My lady, it’s me,\" Song Lingbo said, striding to the inner bedside.","Hearing the familiar voice, Lady Song’s heart settled. She lifted the bed curtain to see him, startled by his disheveled state. She hurriedly rose, asking, \"Why so much blood? Where are you hurt?\" Her hands gripped his arms as she examined him, yet found no visible wounds.","\"It’s nothing. Not my blood—it’s from some fierce beasts. We had to rush back and didn’t have time to change or clean up.\" He hurried to reassure her.","\"That’s good, that’s good. By the way, how are Yihong and the others? And the three children? Are they all right?\" she asked again.","\"They’re all fine, don’t worry. The guard birds sustained some injuries, but none are life-threatening. We just returned. I had Yihong and the others go change and wash up first before coming over. I had Mi’er take the three children to rest in the courtyard.\"","Song Lingbo spoke as he guided her to the table and sat her down. \"My lady, what happened at home? Did something frighten you?\" He had deliberately softened his footsteps entering the room. Normally, she wouldn’t have jolted awake so suddenly.","Hearing this, Lady Song finally explained, \"You don’t know—that day, a man named Cheng Wanli arrived with some attendants and four elders. He claimed to have an old connection with you and came to pay a visit. Right at the door, he injured the gatekeeper. At the time, the clan elders intervened, saying the Cheng family was a prominent clan from Longnan. Since they had an old connection with you and had come to the door, it would have been inhumane to refuse them again.\"","Her voice faltered as she continued, \"But no. After inviting them to stay in the manor that night, Cheng Wanli actually sneaked into the main courtyard and entered my room. He drugged me unconscious, bound me with a rope, and attempted to assault me.\" As she recounted this, she seemed to relive that night’s events, shuddering involuntarily as goosebumps prickled up her skin."]},{"number":5022,"title":"Chapter 5022: Recounting the Matter","paragraphs":["\"Damn it!\"","Song Lingbo roared with fury, slamming his fist hard onto the tabletop with a thunderous crash. The impact sent the teacups on the table rattling with a sharp clatter.","Lady Song clasped his hand and whispered softly, \"Don’t lose your temper. Let me explain.\"","He took a deep breath, clasped her hand in return, and suppressed his rage. \"Speak.\"","\"Fortunately, My Lady Xuanyuan appeared and saved me, sparing me from such a fate. Had it not been for her, the consequences would have been unimaginable.\" \"She continued, \"She intervened, crippling Cheng Wanli’s martial prowess and forcing him to reveal his purpose for coming to our Song family. Only then did I learn he was after our family’s Rainbow Faceted Spirit Stone. As for me... I succumbed to temptation that very night...\"","She recounted the events of that night in meticulous detail, concluding, \"That’s the whole story. Given the circumstances, I truly couldn’t think of any better solution than Lady Xuanyuan’s actions. I only worry about retaliation from the Cheng family, which is why I urgently asked for your swift return.\"","Hearing this, Song Lingbo exhaled deeply, a wave of dread washing over him. \" Thank goodness you’re unharmed, and thank goodness My Lady Xuanyuan was staying at our residence. Later, My lady and I will go to pay our respects to this Lady Xuanyuan personally and express our gratitude.","\"Very well. I’ll have someone prepare a bath for you first!\" Lady Song said, rising to her feet. She fetched her outer garments from the bedside, dressed, and went to the doorway to give instructions.","Meanwhile, in the guest quarters, Mi’er was escorting Hao’er and the other two children back when the steward mentioned Lady Xuanyuan was staying in the very courtyard the children occupied. Upon entering the courtyard, she dismissed the servants. The three children immediately dashed inside.","Just as she was about to knock, Hao’er paused and whispered, \"Why don’t we bathe and change first? We can come see Mother after we’re all clean and tidy. Let her sleep a little longer?\"","Muchen glanced at the still-early hour and recalled how much his mother loved sleeping in. He nodded in agreement. \"Yes, let Mother sleep a little longer.\"","\"Mm-hmm, we’ll put on clean, pretty clothes before finding Mother.\" Yue’er had woken up upon entering the mansion, her little face still drowsy. Hearing her brothers’ words, she nodded in agreement.","Upon hearing their words, Mi’er gave instructions to the maidservant outside the courtyard before approaching them quietly. \"I’ll head back first and return later. I’ve already had the maidservant prepare hot water for your baths. If you need anything, just have the servants arrange it.\"","\"Alright.\" The three responded. Watching her leave, they each returned to their own rooms.","With Feng Jiu’s cultivation, how could she not know the three were whispering outside her door? Hearing their voices, she knew they had returned. Lying in bed, she smiled as she opened her eyes, yawned, and thought about the three little ones saying they would bathe and change first. She wasn’t in a hurry to get up, so she lay in bed for a while before rising to wash and dress.","Stepping outside, she instructed the maidservant to have the kitchen prepare some food. Raising her hand, she cast a sound-blocking barrier around the courtyard before sitting down to wait for the children to emerge from their rooms.","\"Mother!\" Muchen was the first to come out. Spotting her seated at the stone table in the courtyard, he immediately ran toward her.","\"Chen’er, you’ve grown taller again,\" Feng Jiu said with a smile, opening her arms to embrace the boy as he ran toward her."]},{"number":5023,"title":"Chapter 5023: Joyful Reunion","paragraphs":["After not seeing him for a while, she noticed he’d grown taller again, and couldn’t help but smile. Lifting him up, she sat him on her lap. Watching the little guy’s face flush with embarrassment, she found it utterly amusing.","\"What’s this? You’re shy when your Mother holds you?\" She teased him playfully, gently tapping his nose with her finger.","\"Mother, I’m a boy. I can’t always let you hold me.\" He tried to keep a straight face, but the slight upturn of his lips betrayed his inner delight.","\"It’s alright. Even if you’re a boy, you’re still Mother’s precious son. Mother can not only hold you, but also kiss you.\" With that, she planted a kiss on his little face. Watching her son blush all the way to his ears, she couldn’t help but chuckle softly.","\"Son, who do you take after to be so shy?\" she asked with amusement.","Muchen’s face flushed crimson, tinged with embarrassment, yet his eyes sparkled with delight. After a moment’s thought, he replied, \"Like Father.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu chuckled softly and nodded in agreement. \"Yes, just like your Father. Remember back then? Your father fainted from sheer excitement after just one kiss from Mother.\" Recalling the incident, she couldn’t help but laugh aloud.","\"Mother!\"","\"Mother!\"","Two joyful voices rang out simultaneously. As the door swung open, Hao’er and Yue’er both scampered toward her.","\"Mother, Mother, I missed you so much!\" Yue’er, being a girl, knew how to be the most affectionate. She threw herself into Feng Jiu’s arms and nuzzled against her.","\"Mother.\" Hao’er, acting like the big brother, simply came to her side and called out.","\"Sit down, both of you! Tell Mother how you’ve been doing out there these past days?\" Feng Jiu set Mu Chen down, letting him sit beside her. She motioned for Hao’er to sit as well, while Yue’er burrowed into her embrace, climbing onto her lap and wrapping her arms tightly around her.","What else could Feng Jiu do but sigh helplessly? She smiled fondly, running a hand through her daughter’s still-damp hair. \"Sit still. Mother will dry your hair a bit. You know it’s easy to catch a cold like this, right?\"","\"I heard Mother talking to Brother, so I quickly dried off and ran out,\" Yue’er said, settling into her seat without fidgeting.","Feng Jiu used her spiritual energy to draw the moisture from Yue’er’s hair, then carefully re-tied it before cradling her. As she held her soft, plump daughter, she raised an eyebrow, looked down, and chuckled, \"Yue’er, have you gotten fatter again?\" The little body felt so soft and plump in her arms, noticeably heavier too.","\"Hehe,\" Yue’er beamed up at her, then buried her face shyly in her mother’s embrace. \"Mother, the food at Sister Mi’er’s house is so delicious! And her brothers make us all these tasty, pretty treats.\"","\"Hmm, Mother knows. That’s how you’ve gotten so plump.\" She gently pinched her chin and shook it playfully. \"You’re still young, so eating more is alright. You’ll slim down once you grow taller. But no matter how delicious things are, you must eat in moderation. Don’t always stuff yourself—it’s bad for your health, understand?\"","\"Mm-hmm, Yue’er understands.\" She nodded eagerly.","\"Hao’er, did you learn anything following the Song family?\" Feng Jiu turned to the boy seated beside her.","\"Yes, Mother. We hunted game ourselves, and we also...\" Hao’er recounted their forest adventures."]},{"number":5024,"title":"Chapter 5024: Greets","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu listened as Hao’er spoke, and soon Yue’er chimed in with a few remarks. Muchen, standing nearby, also joined the conversation. After hearing the three children recount the amusing incidents and their journey home, she nodded approvingly and praised, \"You did very well.\"","Hearing their Mother’s words of praise, the three children exchanged glances and smiled in unison.","A maid arrived carrying breakfast, but upon seeing the barrier around the courtyard, she did not enter. Instead, she waited at the courtyard gate.","Feng Jiu noticed this. After exchanging a few words with the children, she removed the barrier and allowed the maid to bring the food inside.","\"You must be hungry after returning so early. Eat quickly! Afterwards, those who feel sleepy can go back to their rooms for a nap.\" \" Feng Jiu instructed them.","\"Yeah.\" The three replied, joining her for breakfast.","After breakfast, Feng Jiu accompanied the children on a stroll around the courtyard to aid digestion. She then sent them back to their rooms for a nap, planning to take them out for an outing at noon.","The moment the children heard she would take them out to play, they immediately agreed and returned to their rooms to sleep.","Not long after the children went to their rooms, Song Mi’er arrived. Upon entering the courtyard and seeing only Feng Jiu there, she approached and called out, \"Master, where are the three of them?\"","\"I sent them to sleep for a while to catch up on rest. I’ll take them out to play at noon,\" Feng Jiu said with a smile, sitting by the table sipping tea.","\"Then I’ll take you out at noon. I know this city well.\" Mi’er added, \"Master, I visited my Mother and learned about the family situation. I truly thank you for this. My father and mother are waiting behind. They said they’d come personally to thank you. Oh, and my father kept asking about your identity, but I didn’t say anything.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled and said, \"Originally, I planned to return to the island once you came back. But now that your family has this trouble—and it’s likely because of me—I can’t leave until the Cheng family matter is resolved. So we’ll stay here for now. Once that’s settled, we can depart.\"","Song Mi’er paused, then asked, \"But wouldn’t the Cheng family dare retaliate?\" Didn’t they say that our Master had crippled the cultivation levels of their four powerful elders? If the head of the Cheng family knows this, he probably won’t come looking for revenge, right?","After all, whoever could cripple the cultivation of those four must be quite powerful. The Cheng family wouldn’t risk provoking someone like that again.","Feng Jiu chuckled softly, twirling her teacup as she replied, \"You don’t understand. Some people—even when you choose to spare them—still insist on walking down a path to their own destruction. What will the Cheng family do? I don’t know. But I believe we’ll find out soon enough.\"","Hearing this, Song Mi’er said no more, for she spotted her parents approaching. \"Master, my parents and three brothers have arrived.\" With that, she walked towards them.","From the moment he entered the courtyard, Song Lingbo had been observing the green-clad woman seated there sipping tea. Her simple, elegant attire and unremarkable features made her seem almost forgettable. Yet, as she sat there, an air of unshakable composure emanated from her, commanding an inexplicable respect.","With his keen eye for judging people, he instantly recognized her as a formidable figure concealing profound strength.","He stepped forward, clasped his hands, and said, \"Song Lingbo greets Lady Xuanyuan.\""]},{"number":5025,"title":"Chapter 5025: My Name is ’Feng Jiu’","paragraphs":["\"Master Song, no need for formalities.\" Feng Jiu gestured, \"Please sit.\"","Song Lingbo and his wife approached the stone table and sat down. Lady Song then said, \"Lady Xuanyuan, these three are Mi’er’s brothers.\" She turned to look at the trio.","Understanding the gesture, the three stepped forward and bowed in unison: \"Song Yihong.\"","\"Song Yiming.\"","\"Song Yifan, paying our respects to Lady Xuanyuan.\" They spoke in unison, bowing with utmost reverence.","\"Mi’er has often spoken of you three. To meet you today, Lady Song, truly speaks to your good fortune,\" Feng Jiu said with a smile, looking at Lady Song.","Hearing this, Lady Song couldn’t help but smile. Her gaze toward the children held satisfaction and joy, yet she humbly replied, \"Not at all. Don’t be fooled by their appearance—they’re usually quite troublesome.\"","\"My lady, I’ve heard from my wife about the events at the estate. This time, we truly owe it all to you. Song Lingbo is profoundly grateful,\" Song Lingbo stood and declared, this time bowing deeply toward her.","Seeing this, Feng Jiu interjected, \"This is Mi’er’s home. I happened to be staying here as a guest. It was merely a small gesture.\"","\"Lady Xuanyuan’s small gesture saved my wife and averted a crisis for the Song family. To Lady Xuanyuan, it was a mere trifle, but to us, it is a great favor.\"","Song Lingbo gazed at her and continued, \"Given Lady Xuanyuan’s extraordinary abilities, I doubt I could have done much for you. The only way I can show my gratitude is to personally cook for Lady Xuanyuan during your stay at my residence.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled. \"If you offered anything else, I truly wouldn’t need it. But I do have a passion for fine cuisine. To have the legendary Culinary God Song personally prepare a meal for me would be an immense honor.\"","\"Right? I told you Father, if he wanted to repay her, the best way would be to cook for her himself, didn’t I?\" Mi’er, standing nearby, winked at her father and said with a beaming smile.","\"Yes, yes, you’re the smartest,\" Lady Song said with amusement, shooting her a playful glare.","\"Lady Xuanyuan, I have another matter to discuss with you today,\" Song Lingbo stated, his gaze fixed on her.","Seeing this, Feng Jiu smiled and asked, \"Are you wondering who I truly am?\"","Song Lingbo nodded solemnly. \"Precisely. I’m deeply curious about Lady Xuanyuan’s identity. Beyond mere curiosity, I also fear that the Cheng family won’t let this rest. I hope you’ll reveal your background so I can prepare myself mentally.\"","His desire to know her identity stemmed partly from curiosity, but more so from apprehension about the Cheng family returning. Should that happen, he knew full well the combat strength his Song family possessed when faced with powerful adversaries at their doorstep. Even as a major clan themselves, they stood no chance against a prestigious family like the Chengs. Thus, he needed to understand her background and origins before making any arrangements.","Feng Jiu’s lips curved slightly as she looked at him and Lady Song, speaking slowly, \"My name is Feng Jiu.\"","\"Feng Jiu?\" Lady Song froze, the name leaving her utterly bewildered.","Song Lingbo, however, was jolted to his senses. His eyes widened in disbelief as he shot to his feet, his face betraying unmistakable shock. \"You... you are...\"","A tidal wave of disbelief crashed through his mind, leaving him utterly speechless.","Feng Jiu?","Wasn’t that the name of the Empress Phoenix Sovereign? Could she... be that legendary Phoenix Sovereign who ascended from the lower realms, became a sovereign ruler, and then slew the Great Emperor Northern Flame, her fame echoing across the lands?"]},{"number":5026,"title":"Chapter 5026: Shocked","paragraphs":["He couldn’t help but glance at Mi’er, who was smiling radiantly beside him, and asked, \"Mi’er, is she truly...\"","\"Yes, yes, she’s exactly the one Father guessed.\" Song Mi’er nodded cheerfully as she spoke.","Upon hearing this, Song Lingbo immediately prepared to kneel before Feng Jiu in greeting, saying, \"Song Lingbo is blind and ignorant, not realizing it was...\" But as he tried to kneel, he found himself unable to do so. It was as if an invisible force was supporting him, preventing him from kneeling.","He looked up to see Feng Jiu smiling faintly. \"Master Song, there’s no need for such formalities. I’m disguised here and wish not to alarm others.\"","\"Yes, yes,\" he hurriedly nodded in agreement, rising to his feet. Feeling somewhat constrained, he dared not sit back down at the same table with her.","The Empress Phoenix Sovereign!","She was the supreme being! People like them had only heard of her existence, never expecting that one day they would witness her in person—and that she would come to their very home.","For a moment, he felt lightheaded, as if the whole scene were unreal.","The three sons of the Song family heard the name and felt a vague sense of familiarity, though they couldn’t quite place it. Seeing their father’s shocked and excited expression, they exchanged glances, their faces filled with astonishment.","Song Yifan discreetly beckoned to Mi’er, and the group moved to a corner, lowering their voices as they spoke.","\"Mi’er, who exactly is Lady Xuanyuan? Why did Father look so startled the moment he heard the name Feng Jiu? I feel like I’ve heard that name before too, but I just can’t place it. Who is she?\" Song Yifan asked in a hushed tone.","The other two turned to Mi’er, waiting for her to solve the mystery.","\"You don’t know?\" Song Mi’er blinked, a hint of surprise in her voice. She looked them up and down. \"Who told you to stay home buried in your new recipes? You have no idea what’s going on outside.\"","\"Mi’er, tell us quickly! What do you want to eat later? Third Brother will cook it for you.\"","Hearing this, Song Mi’er grinned, amused by their flustered expressions. \"No way! You’ll have to ask Father yourselves later. But whatever you hear here stays within our family. Don’t let anyone else know—especially not the name Feng Jiu. Never mention it to others.\"","\"Why is that?\" the three asked, their eyes instinctively turning toward Lady Xuanyuan, who was conversing with their parents.","\"Trust me, you won’t regret it,\" she said cheerfully, offering no further explanation. In a few quick hops, she joined her parents.","After chatting with Feng Jiu in the courtyard for a while, Song Lingbo and the others departed. After watching them leave, Mi’er approached Feng Jiu, her face alight with a smile. \"Master, you disguised yourself precisely to keep your identity hidden. Why did you tell my father?\"","\"The Song family and the Cheng family are worlds apart in strength. If I hadn’t revealed my identity to your father, do you think he could have remained at ease all this time?\" Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow, glancing at her. \" \"But you... seeing how startled your Father was by my identity, you seemed rather pleased?\"","\"Hehe, really? I’m always this happy!\" She cupped her face with both hands, smiling brightly as she sat down at the table. \"Master, let me take you to try the city’s famous snacks for lunch! Our local delicacies are renowned and unique—you won’t find them anywhere else.\""]},{"number":5027,"title":"Chapter 5027: No Worries Any Longer","paragraphs":["\"Alright.\" Feng Jiu replied, a faint smile curling her lips.","Meanwhile, back in the main courtyard, Song Lingbo sat down in a chair in his room and let out a quiet sigh. He leaned back, silent for a long while, his eyes gleaming with excitement, his expression difficult to describe.","Seeing him like this, Lady Song couldn’t help but worry: \"Husband, are you alright?\" Ever since hearing that Lady Xuanyuan’s name was Feng Jiu, his expression had been off. Now, back in his room, he sat there lost in thought.","Song Yihong and the other two exchanged glances and asked, \"Father, who exactly is this Feng Jiu? Why did you react so strongly upon hearing that name...\" Before he could finish, Song Lingbo abruptly stood up, gestured for silence, and strode toward the door. Only after confirming no servants were in the courtyard did he close the door and cast a sound-blocking barrier.","Seeing this, the others froze, their expressions turning solemn.","\"We have a distinguished guest in our home—this Lady Xuanyuan is extraordinary!\" He spoke with unmistakable excitement. \"The name Feng Jiu—that’s the name of the Empress Phoenix Sovereign, no mistake about it. This Lady Xuanyuan is the Empress Phoenix Sovereign herself, the very one who slew the Northern Flame Emperor shortly after her ascension.\"","Hearing this, Song Yifan slapped his thigh in excitement. \"No wonder the name sounded familiar! It’s that Empress Phoenix! But I heard she favors red robes and possesses unparalleled beauty. The lady in our home seems quite ordinary. Could we have mistaken her? Or is it just a coincidence of names?\"","\"Exactly! That one is a legendary figure. How could she possibly visit our home? Father, could it be someone with the same name?\" Song Yihong chimed in, his mind filled with disbelief. He couldn’t fathom such an unapproachable figure coming to their house.","\"No mistake. It must be her. There’s no doubt.\"","Song Lingbo affirmed, adding, \"Think about it—if it weren’t her, who else could single-handedly cripple the combat abilities of four elders from the Cheng family? Who else would dare to disregard the Cheng family like she did? Besides, Mi’er confirmed it was her—there’s no mistake.\"","Lady Song, listening nearby, finally grasped the meaning and asked, \"So you’re saying that with her in our home, even if the Cheng family comes seeking revenge, we needn’t worry?\"","\"Not just one Cheng family—even ten of them coming, with her alone in our residence, would ensure the entire household remains safe!\" Song Lingbo declared, his heart finally settling completely.","He had been contemplating sending out invitations far and wide, summoning powerful allies he knew for support. Yet now, it seemed unnecessary.","With Feng Jiu alone in their residence, they needn’t fear even ten Cheng families!","\"That’s wonderful, that’s wonderful.\"Lady Song’s heart finally settled. \"Lady Xuanyuan said she’ll wait until the matter with the Cheng family is resolved before leaving. She won’t let our family suffer any ill effects.\"","\"By the way, this matter must remain confidential. Do not reveal Lady Xuanyuan’s identity, nor mention the name Feng Jiu. She came disguised, likely wishing to keep a low profile and avoid drawing attention to her whereabouts,\" Song Lingbo instructed."]},{"number":5028,"title":"Chapter 5028: Meeting","paragraphs":["\"Alright, we understand.\" The others silently took note.","\"For the time being, I’ll personally oversee her meals here at our residence! You three will assist me. Come, let’s head to the kitchen first.\" He gestured, briefly addressing his wife before leading his three sons out.","At noon, Feng Jiu led the three children into town, guided by Mi’er. Before leaving, Mi’er had informed her parents, who thus knew their father would be cooking that evening. Dinner tonight would be back at the manor.","As Mi’er and Feng Jiu’s group departed, the manor bustled with preparations for the evening meal. Meanwhile, most of the Song household had already forgotten about Ke Meng, who remained recuperating in the guest quarters.","Ke Meng learned that the head of the Song family and several young masters had returned, and the household was bustling with activity. Sitting in her courtyard, lost in thought, she realized her situation within the Song family was truly awkward.","She wasn’t quite a guest, nor was she an old acquaintance of the Song family. There were no ties binding her to them. Lady Song had visited her courtyard only once that day and hadn’t returned since, seemingly having forgotten her entirely.","The Song family had kindly allowed her to stay and recover, and she was grateful. Her wounds were gradually healing. Yet, as her physical injuries improved, a growing sense of anxiety and restlessness took root within her.","For she had no idea where she would go next.","After sitting in the courtyard for a while, lost in thought, she stood up and began to walk out. With nowhere to go and no way out, sitting here in a daze wouldn’t solve anything. Better to go out for a walk to clear her mind and see what the Song family was busy with.","Ke Meng, clad in a simple white gown, possessed such exquisite beauty. Combined with the faint sorrow in her brow, she radiated an aura of tender vulnerability that stirred pity in others.","As she walked through the estate, the guards couldn’t help but glance at her.","As long as she avoided restricted areas, no one stopped her. Thus, as she strolled, she found herself unconsciously approaching the main courtyard.","She thought she should properly thank Lady Song for allowing her to recuperate at the Song residence. Unexpectedly, before she even entered the main courtyard, Lady Song emerged from within.","\"Madam,\" she curtsied and addressed her.","\"Miss Ke, what brings you here?\" Lady Song inquired, her gaze flickering slightly as she studied Ke Meng before her.","A woman’s charm lies in her simplicity. This saying held true.","As a fellow woman, Lady Song observed her in plain white robes, a small white flower pinned in her hair, her face free of makeup. Yet, she possessed a fresh, otherworldly beauty that evoked pity and affection.","Hearing her words, Ke Meng paused before replying, \"I’ve been recuperating in the courtyard. Having been confined for so long, I found myself walking here without realizing it. Seeing the servants so busy, I wondered if there might be anything I could assist with?\"","\"I see,\"","Madam Song smiled. \"Miss Ke is our honored guest, and with your injury, you should focus on recuperating. Those chores are for the servants—you mustn’t trouble yourself.\"","Her voice paused briefly before continuing, \"My husband and three sons have returned. As an unmarried young lady, moving about the estate during your recovery might prove inconvenient. Unless something urgent arises, Miss Ke, you may simply send a servant to attend to your needs.\"","Hearing this, Ke Meng’s eyes flickered slightly. She lowered her head and said, \"Very well, I understand. I shall return to my room now and not disturb you further, Madam.\" With that, she gave a light curtsy before turning to leave."]},{"number":5029,"title":"Chapter 5029: Self harm","paragraphs":["Watching Ke Meng leave, a complex expression flashed across Mrs. Song’s eyes.","It wasn’t that she needed to guard against Ke Meng’s aloofness, but rather that the girl was born too beautiful. Now, being homeless, who could say if she might suddenly harbor some wicked thoughts?","\"Ah!\" She sighed softly, turning back toward the courtyard with a hint of resignation.","Ke Meng didn’t wander elsewhere but returned directly to her room in the courtyard. Sitting before the mirror, she gazed at her reflection, her eyes flickering slightly. One hand gently caressed her own face.","\"I used to think that as a woman, possessing such a beautiful face was a blessing. Yet, it was precisely this face that brought ruin upon my family, leading to the annihilation of our clan. Now, having narrowly escaped death, it feels like being reborn. But looking at this exquisite face again, I see it as the very root of all misfortune.\"","She murmured to herself, recalling Lady Xuanyuan’s cold indifference and Lady Song’s distant detachment. She knew it was all because of this face.","\"Leaving the Song household, bearing such an exquisite beauty, I might one day attract another villain like Cheng Wanli. If that’s the case, perhaps it’s better to destroy it...\"","Her voice was eerily calm, almost as if she were speaking to herself. The hand that had been caressing her face now reached toward the dressing table, picking up a hairpin and slowly raising it toward her face. Her gaze remained fixed on the mirror.","She gazed at her own flawless, exquisite beauty reflected back at her. Her hand trembled slightly. Pressing her lips together, she slowly closed her eyes. The hairpin pressed against her skin. Its icy touch sent an involuntary shiver through her. The next moment, she applied force, driving the pin into her flesh. It sliced downward, heavy and deliberate.","Crimson blood dripped down the hairpin. As it cut, it left a deep, bloody gash on her face. The force was so great that the flesh was slightly torn and turned outward. Yet she bit her lip tightly, not even letting out a whimper. She swallowed the tears and the blood seeping from her bitten lip...","Feng Jiu and the others, who had been out sightseeing, returned to the Song residence by evening. Dinner was set in the front courtyard. Lady Song, thinking they hadn’t all sat down for a proper meal together in a while, decided they should all dine together tonight.","\"Set all the tables properly. Move those flower arrangements over a bit to open up the space,\" Lady Song directed the servants as she arranged the scene. Then she remembered Ke Meng staying in the guest quarters. Considering her a guest of the mansion, it would be rather rude not to invite her over. She instructed the maid beside her, \"Go invite Miss Ke to join us for dinner tonight!\"","\"Yes, ma’am.\" The maid responded and headed toward the guest quarters.","\"Mother.\" Song Mi’er approached, observing the bustling activity. She smiled as she slipped her arm through her mother’s. \"Who else are you inviting to dinner, Mother?\"","\"Miss Ke Meng from the guest quarters,\" Mrs. Song replied.","\"Oh, is that the young lady we saved that night? Then I’ll go invite her! I haven’t met her yet anyway.\" She called out to the maid, \"You don’t need to go. I’ll handle it.\" Releasing her hand, she headed toward the guest quarters.","Seeing this, Madam Song shook her head helplessly and instructed the maid, \"Go check if the dishes are ready. Have them brought up!\" \" She then instructed another maid, \"Have you prepared the dessert I asked for?\"","While the front courtyard bustled with activity, Song Mi’er arrived at the guest quarters. Seeing the quiet courtyard with only two maids standing guard outside, she asked, \"Is Miss Ke inside?\""]},{"number":5030,"title":"Chapter 5030: Declining","paragraphs":["\"Miss, Miss Ke is in her room. Shall I fetch her?\" the maid inquired.","\"No need. I’ll go myself.\" Song Mi’er shook her head, about to step inside, but paused and asked, \"Tell me, is Miss Ke truly beautiful?\"","Hearing this, the two maidservants looked at her uncertainly, hesitating. Would their young mistress be displeased if they praised another girl’s beauty in her presence?","\"Speak up! Why are you staring at me?\" Song Mi’er urged.","\"Miss Ke is exceptionally beautiful. Everyone in the mansion says so,\" the maidservants replied, quickly lowering their heads, fearful of angering their young mistress.","\"Oh?\" She seemed unimpressed. Ever since witnessing her mistress’s peerless beauty, she believed no other woman could compare.","Walking further in, she glanced around before approaching the central door and knocking. \"Miss Ke, it’s Song Mi’er. My mother sent me to invite you to dine in the front courtyard.\"","She called out, then stood waiting by the door, intending to see how beautiful she truly was once she opened it.","Inside the room, Ke Meng paused slightly upon hearing the sound. She retrieved a gauze scarf to bind over her face, only to find it too thin—the blood seeping from her wounds still faintly visible through the fabric. She tore a piece of lining from her clothing and secured it over the gauze scarf.","\"Miss Ke?\" Hearing movement inside but no response, Song Mi’er called out again, feeling slightly puzzled.","\"Coming.\"","As Ke Meng’s voice echoed from within, the door opened. Dressed in plain white robes, she stood by the doorway, her face concealed by a white cloth. Only her eyes, peeking out from beneath the fabric, were visible.","\"Miss Song.\"","She gave a slight curtsy, her voice slightly hoarse. The wound on her face, left untreated, had become inflamed and swollen. Speaking now pulled at the injury, the pain making the face beneath the white cloth grow even paler.","\"Miss Ke, why are you wearing that?\" Song Mi’er pointed to the white cloth on her face, asking in surprise.","Bending her knees slightly, she bowed again. \"Miss Song, I’m feeling rather unwell and fear I cannot go. Please convey my gratitude to Madam for her kindness. Once I recover, I shall personally come to thank her.\"","Seeing that despite the veil, her expression truly looked extremely weak, and her voice was slightly hoarse, Song Mi’er said, \" Very well! If you’re unwell, Miss Ke, rest well. I’ll have the household physician come examine you later.\"","\"There’s no need to trouble yourself. Resting will suffice. Thank you, Miss Song,\" she replied.","Seeing this, Song Mi’er said no more, simply wishing her a good rest before departing.","Watching her leave, Ke Meng closed the door and returned to lie on the bed. The wound on her face burned fiercely, throbbing in waves of pain. Closing her eyes, she thought: Just endure these two days, and it will be over.","Meanwhile, Song Mi’er relayed Ke Meng’s words to her mother.","Lady Song sighed softly upon hearing this and said, \"Very well. Later, have your brother set aside a portion for her. The servants can deliver it.\"","\"Yes, Mother,\" Song Mi’er replied with a bright smile.","That evening, besides Feng Jiu and the three children dining with the Song family, several clan elders also attended. While the Song family members were joyful and carefree, the elders were so troubled they barely touched their food."]},{"number":5031,"title":"Chapter 5031: Bid Farewell","paragraphs":["Finally, after the meal ended and everyone dispersed, several clan elders hurriedly stopped Song Lingbo.","\"Lingbo! What on earth is going on? Why did you come back only to dive straight into the kitchen and start cooking? The matter between our Song family and the Cheng family—it’s far from over! As the head of the household, how can you not be worried at all?\" one elder said with concern.","\"Indeed! With such a major crisis upon us, you still find time to eat and drink?\" another elder shook his head. His mind was so preoccupied with worry that even though Song Lingbo had prepared tonight’s feast, he couldn’t bring himself to eat.","Hearing this, Song Lingbo replied, \"Elders, there’s no need for worry. The Cheng family likely won’t dare come again. Even if they do, there’s no cause for concern. Put this matter out of your minds and return to rest. Trust me—the manor will be fine.\" With that, he turned and left without waiting for further discussion.","Several days later, at dawn, Ke Meng arrived outside the main courtyard and addressed the maidservant at the gate: \" Please inform the Madam that Ke Meng has come to take her leave.\"","The maid went inside to report. Lady Song came to the courtyard and had Ke Meng brought in. When she entered, Ke Meng wore a veil over her face, and her white robe had been replaced with a slightly darker beige gown. She looked like herself, yet there was something different about her.","\"Have your wounds healed, Miss Ke?\" Lady Song inquired gently.","\"Thank you for your concern, Madam. My injuries have fully recovered. Having stayed in your residence for so long, I have come today to take my leave. I am deeply grateful for the shelter you provided during my convalescence.\" She bowed respectfully, her gratitude sincere.","Upon hearing this, Lady Song nodded and inquired, \"You have no home now. What are your plans for the future?\"","\"The world is vast,\" she replied softly. \"There will always be a place for me to call home. There is no need for you to worry about Ke Meng.\" She added, \"Ke Meng wishes to bid farewell to Lady Xuanyuan. Might you kindly escort her there?\"","Lady Xuanyuan had also been kind to her. Now that she was leaving, it was only proper to bid farewell.","\"Very well. I was just about to go myself. You may accompany me!\" Lady Song said, leading her towards the courtyard where Fengjiu and the children resided.","Early that morning, the three children had risen and were practicing their boxing in the courtyard. Feng Jiu sat nearby watching, occasionally offering guidance, while Mi’er chatted with her.","When Mi’er spotted her mother approaching, she sprang to her feet, running toward her with a beaming smile. Taking her hand, she led her into the courtyard. \"Mother, why have you come?\"","Then, glancing at Ke Meng beside her, she called out cheerfully, \"Miss Ke has come too!\"","\"Miss Song,\" Ke Meng nodded briefly in her direction.","\"Miss Ke, why are you still wearing a veil? Could it be you’re not quite well yet?\" Mi’er asked. She had been hoping to see what Ke Meng actually looked like, but both times she’d met her, Ke Meng had been veiled.","Ke Meng smiled. Though the veil hid her faint smile, the slight curve of her eyes revealed her amusement.","\"I’ve fully recovered. I came today to bid farewell to Lady Xuanyuan.\" She looked toward the woman in green seated at the stone table.","At that moment, Lady Song interjected, \"Lady Xuanyuan, Miss Ke says she must depart and has asked me to bring her to bid you farewell.\"","\"Hmm.\" Feng Jiu responded indifferently, her gaze shifting to Ke Meng.","\"Ah? You’re leaving already?\" Mi’er looked at her in surprise."]},{"number":5032,"title":"Chapter 5032: Stunned","paragraphs":["\"Yes, I’ve been staying at the mansion for quite some time now. My injuries have healed, and it’s time for me to leave.\" Ke Meng said softly.","\"Where will you go after you leave?\" Mi’er asked curiously. She had heard from her mother that Ke Meng’s entire family had been wiped out, leaving her alone in the world.","\"I haven’t decided yet. But I’ll take things one step at a time. I believe heaven never abandons those in need, and I’ll find a place to call home.\" She spoke softly, offering Song Mi’er a gentle smile.","Mi’er knew a smile must be playing on her face right now. Yet, the veil hid her features, preventing her from seeing that smile—or the face behind it, one the household members often praised as exceptionally beautiful.","A flicker of emotion stirred within her. She grinned, her face lighting up with a radiant smile. Stepping forward, she said, \"Miss Ke, your eyes are truly beautiful! I’ve seen you twice now, yet I’ve never seen your face. You’re leaving? Before you go, surely you can let me see what you look like? Otherwise, if we meet again out there, I won’t recognize you.\"","Ke Meng paused, gazing at Song Mi’er who had approached. She lowered her eyes slightly and replied, \"It’s not that I don’t want you to see, but... I fear I might frighten you.\"","Hearing this, Lady Song was slightly startled, a hint of confusion in her expression.","Meanwhile, Feng Jiu, seated at the table sipping tea, paused briefly. After taking a sip, she set down her cup and lifted her gaze.","Song Mi’er paused, then said, \"Scared me? How could that be? Though I’ve never seen your face, the servants in the mansion say you’re exceptionally beautiful. It’s precisely because they’ve always praised your beauty that I’ve been curious to see just how beautiful you truly are.\"","She added with a bright smile, \"Besides, I’m quite brave. Ordinary things don’t scare me.\"","Ke Meng hesitated. She hadn’t intended for them to see her disfigured face—both to avoid frightening them and to prevent leaving them with the lasting impression of a horrifying visage.","Lady Song asked in confusion, \"What happened to your face, Miss Ke? I saw you wearing a veil today and assumed it was to conceal your appearance for traveling. Wasn’t that the case?\"","At that moment, neither Lady Song nor Song Mi’er, nor even Feng Jiu, could have imagined—nor did they expect—that she would have disfigured her own exquisitely beautiful face.","\"Miss Ke, please remove your veil so I can see you! I mean it—with that veil on, I might not even recognize you if we meet outside someday!\" Mi’er pleaded, her eyes brimming with anticipation.","Seeing this, Ke Meng loosened one side of her veil. As it fell to the side, revealing her disfigured face, both Lady Song and Song Mi’er involuntarily gasped.","\"Gasp! How could this be!\"","Feng Jiu’s gaze fell upon Ke Meng’s face. Her eyes flickered slightly, a hint of surprise flashing through them. She truly hadn’t expected this.","\"I thought it would be safer to go out like this,\" she said, trying to keep her voice steady. Then, she walked forward slowly, came before Feng Jiu, and knelt down in a deep bow.","\"Ke Meng takes her leave of Lady Xuanyuan. Your great kindness, Lady Xuanyuan, Ke Meng will remember forever.\" She performed the full formal bow as she knelt down in reverence, distinct from the light curtsy she’d given Lady Song.","For she knew this woman had saved her life, crippled Cheng Wanli, and avenged her wrongs. Thus, she deserved this kneeling salute."]},{"number":5033,"title":"Chapter 5033: Show the way","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu watched Ke Meng performing the formal kneeling bow, her fingers tapping lightly on the tabletop. \"Since you have nowhere to go,\" she said, \"I shall show you the way.\"","Hearing this, Ke Meng froze, lifting her head to look at her.","\"Mi’er, ink and brush.\" Feng Jiu turned to Song Mi’er beside her.","\"Right away,\" Song Mi’er replied, scurrying into Yue’er’s room to fetch the brush, ink, and paper Mi’er used for her calligraphy practice.","After placing the items on the table, she stepped back to stand nearby, watching Ke Meng kneeling on the floor. She was shocked that someone would deliberately disfigure their own face.","She was truly ruthless toward herself. For a woman to disfigure her face like this showed just how resolute she must have been.","Feng Jiu wrote silently. Those who hadn’t approached couldn’t see what she wrote, only watching as she sealed it in an envelope, then wrote two sentences on another piece of paper, folded it, and handed it to Ke Meng.","\"Go now! Open it outside the city. This paper contains the address you must go to, and it also specifies to whom you should deliver this letter.\"","Hearing this, Ke Meng took it and said, \"Thank you, Lady Xuanyuan.\" She asked no further questions, simply stowed away what she had been given before rising to her feet.","Seeing her disfigured face, Feng Jiu sighed inwardly and said, \"Once your cultivation reaches the Upper-Level Divine, if you wish to restore your appearance, come seek me at the Song residence.\"","Hearing these words, Ke Meng’s heart jolted, and she couldn’t help but look at her. Her face was so horribly ruined—could she really restore it? Shocked, she suppressed her thoughts and said, \"Thank you, Lady Xuanyuan. Ke Meng takes her leave.\" She bowed again to Lady Song and Song Mi’er before turning to depart.","\"I’ll see her out,\" Song Mi’er said, quickly following to escort her from the estate.","Feng Jiu took out a communication jade and handed it to Lady Song, saying, \"This communication jade is yours. Keep it. Should anything arise in the future, you may use it to send messages.\"","\"Very well,\" Lady Song replied, accepting it and putting it away.","Before long, Song Mi’er returned, asking curiously, \"Master, where did you send her? Why didn’t you just tell her directly? Why write it on paper?\"","Lady Song, standing nearby, felt a flutter in her heart when Mi’er addressed Feng Jiu as \"Master.\" A faint smile touched her lips. Since learning Fengjiu’s true identity, she had also discovered that their Mi’er had chosen her as her master. It was precisely because of this that Feng Jiu had come to the Song family and done so much to help them.","Thinking back to how that crazy girl had accidentally ended up recognizing Feng Jiu as her master, they still found it utterly unbelievable.","Feng Jiu smiled faintly. \"I told her to seek out the Jiang family and find Immortal Qinghua. Whether she goes to the Jiang family or not is entirely her own decision.\"","Hearing this, Song Mi’er understood. She knew of Immortal Qinghua—the patriarch of the Jiang family. With him making arrangements, it would likely be a good place to go. However, whether Ke Meng would actually go to the Jiang family depended entirely on her own choice.","Yet, recalling how Ke Meng had left alone, Mi’er’s eyes darted about. Curiosity piqued, she asked, \"Master, why not keep Ke Meng by your side? She has no family left—only herself.\"","Feng Jiu arched an eyebrow, a faint smile playing at the corners of her lips. Her clear gaze settled on her as she replied with a hint of amusement, \"Do you think I take in just anyone? Do you expect me to take in every orphaned girl with nowhere to go and keep her by my side?\""]},{"number":5034,"title":"Chapter 5034: Thunderous Wrath","paragraphs":["\"Mi’er, you mustn’t disregard proper etiquette or fail to recognize hierarchy,\" Lady Song admonished her.","Mi’er stuck out her tongue and said nothing more.","Feng Jiu smiled and said, \"It’s fine. There aren’t many rules around me anyway.\" She looked at Song Mi’er and continued, \"I’m letting you follow me because you possess extraordinary culinary skills, and I happen to need someone like you by my side. Of course, that’s assuming I find you agreeable.\"","She spoke with a smile, noticing Song Mi’er’s face light up with delight at her words. She continued, \"As for Ke Meng, she possesses no outstanding qualities. What use is she to me? Her strength is insufficient to protect me, she’s incapable of serving as a handmaid or servant, and she certainly lacks loyalty. Why would I keep such a person by my side?\"","She propped her cheek with one hand, speaking leisurely, \"Though one thing did surprise me—her ruthlessness in disfiguring herself. Clearly, she possesses a certain ferocity. Since she dares be so cruel to herself, I’ll show her a path forward. That’s the least I can do.\"","Madam Song nodded in agreement beside her. Indeed, someone like Ke Meng—even she wouldn’t keep her close, let alone someone as noble and powerful as the Phoenix Mistress.","Song Mi’er responded with a vague understanding: \"Oh, I see.\" At that moment, she felt profoundly grateful that she at least possessed exceptional culinary skills.","\"Alright, Mi’er, stay with Lady Xuanyuan. I’ll return first.\" Lady Song said with a smile before returning to her courtyard.","Several days later, when the Cheng family in distant Longnan saw Cheng Wanli and his entourage return, they were nearly struck by thunderous fury.","\"Who? Who did this?!\" Cheng Wanshan, the head of the Cheng family, roared with rage, his eyes fixed on the Cheng family guards kneeling in the hall.","\"Master... it was the Song family—the family of the culinary god, Song Lingbo!\" a guard stammered.","\"The culinary god Song Lingbo? A mere cook dares cripple four of my family’s revered elders and even cripple my own brother, Cheng Wanshan? The Song family has the audacity!\"","His dark voice carried a sharp killing intent and overwhelming fury. His fist slammed heavily onto a nearby chair, shattering it into a pile of splinters with a loud crash.","\"The Song family? Impossible! Even if they have some local fame, they couldn’t possibly cripple four of our family’s revered elders!\" An elderly man entered, followed by several other elders.","\"Supreme Elder.\" Cheng Wanshan rose to his feet and bowed upon seeing them.","The leading elder sat down in a chair, nodded briefly to Cheng Wanshan, then turned to the guards. \"Now, tell me exactly what happened.\"","\"It happened like this. Second Master and the four elders went to the Song family to retrieve a multicolored spirit stone as a birthday gift for the Patriarch. When they arrived, Song Lingbo and the others happened to be away...\" The guard recounted the entire sequence of events in detail.","\"That’s it. But that woman also said... she also said...\" The guard hesitated, unable to continue.","\"Speak! \" Cheng Wanshan’s rage flared, and he barked the order.","\"Th-that woman said... she said the Cheng family must bring a substantial gift to apologize in person. Only then would this matter be settled. Otherwise... otherwise, she said... she said Second Master and the others would face dire consequences...\" The guard’s voice grew fainter and fainter. By the end, his head was bowed so low it nearly touched the ground.","\"What an arrogant, ignorant woman, so full of herself she doesn’t know her place!\""]},{"number":5035,"title":"Chapter 5035: The Cheng Clan of Longnan","paragraphs":["The Supreme Elder narrowed his eyes, his expression darkening as a terrifying aura of murderous intent radiated from him.","\"What an ignorant, insolent woman! She dares to inflict such grievous wounds upon my clan, yet expects us to come to her doorstep to apologize and make amends? She truly deserves to die!\" Cheng Wanshan’s voice was deep and ominous, his chest heaving violently with rage.","The Supreme Elder then demanded, \"What does this woman look like? How old is she? What distinguishing features does she have? Describe her carefully. I want to see just who this upstart is who dares to speak with such insolence!\"","\"Yes, the woman wore azure robes. Her features were merely plain and ordinary, nothing remarkable. If anything, it was the terrifying aura emanating from her. At the time, I was merely glanced at by her, yet I felt my entire body grow icy cold, as if plunged into hell. It was truly dreadful.\"","Recalling that moment, the guard’s face paled slightly, and he couldn’t help but shiver involuntarily.","\"Supreme Elder, how shall we handle this matter?\" Cheng Wanshan looked at him inquiringly, his voice suppressing anger and murderous intent.","The old man stroked his beard, paused for a moment, and asked, \"What of Wanli? And the others—have they all been seen by doctors?\"","\"They have. All have had their cultivation completely stripped away. Their inner cores shattered, they can never cultivate again. The four reverends are barely clinging to life, death imminent. As for Wanli, besides his cultivation being destroyed, he bears multiple wounds. Even if he doesn’t die immediately, he’ll live as nothing but a cripple.\"","As he spoke, his fist clenched tightly, cracking audibly.","That damned woman in green! He longed to go personally and cripple her, making her taste a life worse than death!","\"To cripple four revered elders, this woman’s cultivation must be formidable. Very well! You send men to investigate the identity of the woman described by the guards. I’ll go with several Supreme Elders to seek the Patriarch’s guidance on how to handle this matter.\"","\"Understood. I’ll dispatch investigators immediately.\" Cheng Wanshan replied, knowing full well that the Patriarch’s final decision would most likely be to send several Supreme Elders to the Song family to annihilate both the Song clan and that woman in green!","After all, they had crippled a member of the Cheng family—a direct affront to the family’s honor! Given the Cheng family’s current standing and influence, how could they tolerate such humiliation from a mere Song family? If the Song family wasn’t annihilated, how could the Chengs maintain their foothold in Longnan?","That night, in the Cheng family’s council hall, the nine seated elders sat within the chamber. At the head of the table sat an elderly man with hair and beard as white as snow.","Though his hair and even his eyebrows were snow-white, his complexion was rosy, and his spirit seemed robust. Yet now, his face was grave, his lips pressed together as he surveyed the assembly and asked, \"What are your views on this matter?\"","\"What’s there to consider? They carved the name of the Cheng family, yet they’ve brought shame upon us. The Song family and that mysterious woman in green—they cannot be spared!\" declared a middle-aged man who appeared to be in his forties or fifties.","He appeared to be in his forties or fifties, but his true age was anyone’s guess. After all, those seated in this council hall were certainly no ordinary individuals.","\"Indeed, the Song family must not be spared. They must be wiped out! To prove the might of the Cheng family of Longnan!\" another declared.","\"Has the identity of that woman in green been thoroughly investigated?\" another inquired, turning his gaze toward Cheng Wanshan seated nearby."]},{"number":5036,"title":"Chapter 5036: Here","paragraphs":["Cheng Wanshan shook his head. \"No, there’s almost no trace of her. Women with such formidable power are few and far between. We’ve checked every possible lead, but none match. To this day, we still don’t know who that woman truly was.\"","\"But it’s just the Song family, just some woman of unknown origin. What’s there to hesitate about? Kill them if they must be killed, wipe them out if they must be wiped out. It’s no big deal.\"","The speaker was a woman in her thirties, dressed in a red gown that revealed a hint of skin. She sat casually, idly twirling her slender fingers. The survival of an entire clan seemed as insignificant to her as the life of an insect.","Listening to the others, the elder seated at the head of the table stroked his beard, glanced at them, and said, \"In that case, you shall undertake this mission. My birthday approaches in a few days. Return swiftly.\"","The speakers exchanged glances, smiles touching their lips. They bowed in unison, replying, \" Very well, we shall personally undertake the journey. While there, we will also retrieve that multicolored spirit stone from the Song family to present as a birthday gift to the Ancestor.\"","\"Heh heh, then this old man shall await your return.\" The elder in the seat of honor chuckled, stroking his beard and narrowing his eyes. \"I trust the downfall of the Song family will elevate the prestige of our Cheng family to new heights!\"","The others in the hall exchanged glances, their unspoken understanding evident in their smiles.","The speakers made no further delay. Rising, they set off together for the Song manor. As the Patriarch had instructed, they would depart swiftly and return just as quickly. With their strength, dealing with the Song family and that mysterious woman was merely a matter of completing a journey—the outcome already predetermined.","Cheng Wanshan stood outside the council hall, gazing at the sky where the figures of the Supreme Elders had long vanished. With their cultivation and abilities, capable of traversing vast distances in an instant, he was certain they would reach the Song family estate swiftly.","The Song family, and that woman—you shall meet your end!","The Song Family","That day, Feng Jiu accompanied the three children on an outing before returning home. She had them practice their body techniques in the courtyard while she entered her room to retrieve a book.","Her days at the Song manor were relatively uneventful, affording her time to search for a way to break through the barrier isolating the Upper Heaven Realm from the other Heaven Realms.","Over the past two days, she had found a clue in an ancient text regarding this matter. She continued her search, hoping to solve this problem as soon as possible.","If she could break through this barrier between the heavens, she would be able to travel freely between the different celestial realms. This was quite important to her.","As she pored over the book in her room, the children in the courtyard did not disturb her. It was not until evening, when Mi’er brought the supper and knocked on her door, that she emerged.","\"Master, my father made something delicious again today. You must come and try it,\" Mi’er said cheerfully, ladling her a bowl of soup while recounting the day’s amusing events.","Feng Jiu listened while glancing at the sky. \"Another day has passed.\" The Cheng family had remained quiet these past days. She thought to herself that if she stayed ten more days, something was bound to happen within that time.","By then, whether she stayed or left, and whether the Cheng family perished, should become clear.","After the family finished their meal, the three children went out to play in the front courtyard. Feng Jiu strolled about the inner courtyard when suddenly, her brow furrowed as she looked outside."]},{"number":5037,"title":"Chapter 5037: Trapped","paragraphs":["\"Looks like the Cheng family has arrived,\" Feng Jiu murmured softly, her lips curving into a faint smile as her gaze fixed on the darkening sky.","At that moment, an overwhelming aura of power enveloped the entire Song residence, shrouding it completely as if it had been forcibly trapped.","Almost simultaneously, the Song family members sensed it. Song Lingbo stepped out first. Seeing the entire estate shrouded by this formidable aura, he immediately ordered in a grave tone, \"Have everyone below return to their quarters! The Dark Guards and Elite Guards, secure every point within the estate!\"","\"Yes, Madam!\"","The crisp reply echoed as the hidden guards and elite guards swiftly made arrangements. The family head had given prior instructions and briefed them on the situation. Preparations had been underway throughout the estate during this period, ensuring they wouldn’t be caught off guard when danger struck.","\"Could it be the Cheng family?\" Lady Song followed out, her voice tinged with worry.","\"Who else could it be?\" Song Lingbo replied, turning to her. \"My lady, please return to your quarters and stay inside. I’ll go check the front.\"","Knowing she couldn’t help him, Lady Song refrained from interfering. Watching him stride toward the front courtyard, she instructed the shadow guards stationed in the yard: \"Go fetch Yihong and the others.\"","\"Yes, madam!\" A voice echoed, and a figure darted away toward another courtyard.","In the courtyard, Mi’er, Hao’er, and the others were exploring the estate when they sensed the aura enveloping the entire Song residence. They all stopped in their tracks and looked up.","The sky had already darkened, pitch black with not a single star visible, the moon hidden behind heavy clouds.","\"Let’s return to the courtyard first!\" Mi’er sensed something was amiss and hurriedly led the three children toward the rear courtyard. But just as they started walking, they encountered her three elder brothers.","\"Eldest Brother, Second Brother, Third Brother!\" Mi’er called out, quickening her pace to catch up. \"Where are you going?\"","\"We’re going to check the front. Mi’er, take them to Mother in the main courtyard! If you hear any noise, don’t come out. We’ll handle things outside. Just take good care of Mother,\" Song Yihong said.","\"But...\"","\"No buts! Haven’t you seen that powerful aura enveloping our entire Song family? The Cheng family must have sent quite a few people. Hurry!\" Song Yifan quickly called out.","Seeing this, Mi’er swiftly led Hao’er and the other two toward the main courtyard.","\"Shouldn’t we go find Mother?\" Yue’er asked softly.","\"No need. The master will definitely go to the front courtyard. You don’t need to worry about her. Just take care of yourselves,\" Mi’er said, quickening her pace toward the main courtyard.","The elders of the Song family stood pale as death. Staring at the invisible aura in the air, they murmured, \"It’s over... It’s over... Our Song family is finished this time...\"","The Cheng family had truly arrived. Worse still, they had immediately sealed the entire Song residence within this barrier—clearly leaving no escape. This time, escape seemed impossible.","Outside the Song manor gates stood four figures: two elders, a middle-aged man, and a woman clad in red.","After watching the elder seal the entire Song household within the barrier, the group exchanged glances and smiled. \"This way, not a single member of the Song family will escape!\"","\"Four of our Cheng family’s Nine Strong are here. Beyond death, what other path to survival could the Song family possibly have?\""]},{"number":5038,"title":"Chapter 5038: Entering the Manor","paragraphs":["The woman in red flicked a strand of hair from her cheek with one finger, twirling it lightly between her fingers. A contemptuous smile played on her lips, and a flicker of murderous intent crossed her eyes as she gazed at the mansion ahead.","As if struck by a thought, she chuckled softly. \"The rest of the Song family are yours. As for that woman in azure, I shall claim her life myself!\" Her voice paused, her laughter turning vicious and cruel. \"Only in my hands will she truly taste the agony of a fate worse than death.\"","The middle-aged man glanced at her. \"The returning guards said this green-clad woman is formidable. To avoid mishaps, I’ll accompany you.\"","Hearing this, the red-clad woman snorted dismissively. \"What? You don’t trust me? Do you really think I’d lose to some woman who appeared out of nowhere?\"","\"You two, go together!\"","The old man beside them spoke up, glancing at both of them. \"Yuehong, deal with that green-clad woman. If you find her too much, then it’s two against one! No matter what it takes, that woman must die! Don’t let any accidents happen!\"","Seeing him speak, the red-clad woman didn’t say anything else, merely tugging at the corner of her mouth as she listened to him speak.","\"Aside from Song Lingbo, the rest of the Song family aren’t much to worry about. Fourth Brother, you handle Song Lingbo and the others. As for me, I’ll head to the rear mountain where the Song family patriarch is in seclusion. Force him out and slay him. Bring back that multicolored spirit stone as a birthday gift for the Patriarch.\"","Hearing this, the others exchanged glances and responded in unison: \" \"Agreed! It’s settled!\" As soon as the words left their mouths, three of them leaped into the Song residence, while the fourth circled around toward the rear mountain.","With their Supreme-level strength, annihilating the insignificant Song family was a foregone conclusion. Even though they knew the green-robed woman was formidable, none of the four took her seriously.","When the trio landed in the Song family’s front courtyard, they saw only Song Lingbo, his three sons, and several elderly men. Judging by their appearance, these elders were likely the Song family’s clan elders. However, their strength was utterly insignificant in the eyes of the attackers.","\"Song Lingbo.\"","The elder among the three spoke, his gaze fixed on Song Lingbo. \"Have you come here to die?\"","Song Lingbo looked at the three, shielding his sons behind him with his own aura to protect them from the oppressive pressure of the Supreme Masters. \"Are you three among the nine Supreme Masters of the Cheng family?\"","\"Correct!\"","They were well aware the Song family’s ultimate demise was inevitable, so they felt no urgency to kill them immediately. The elder’s piercing gaze fixed on him as he declared, \"The Song family conspired with others to strike a deadly blow against my Cheng family. We are well aware of this. We have come tonight to claim the lives of every last member of your Song family!\"","Hearing this, Song Lingbo replied in a deep voice, \" The fault lies with your Cheng family. Did the guards sent back not inform you that you were to bring generous gifts and come to apologize?\"","\"Ha ha ha ha! What a joke! Bring generous gifts and come to apologize? Is your Song family even worthy of that?\" The old man threw his head back and laughed loudly. His aged yet powerful voice carried a formidable pressure that filled the air, the laughter itself reverberating so intensely it made one’s eardrums ache."]},{"number":5039,"title":"Chapter 5039: Nothing special","paragraphs":["His laughter abruptly froze, his gaze darkening with murderous intent. \"In this world, might makes right! You expect the esteemed Cheng family to apologize to your Song family? Ha! Utterly preposterous!\"","Hearing his words, the faces of several elders standing nearby paled. They hurried to Song Lingbo’s side, their voices urgent. \"Lingbo, you told us not to worry. What plan do you have? The Cheng family has come to our doorstep! Speak up!\"","They were truly at their wits’ end. The Cheng family had arrived, and not just any members—three of the nine revered elders. If only two had come, perhaps these old bones, combined with Song Lingbo, could have put up a fight. But three? That was an entirely different matter.","Even if they pooled all their strength, they couldn’t possibly fight three Supreme Masters!","Song Lingbo pressed her lips together, saying nothing.","\"Where is that woman?\" the red-clad woman asked impatiently.","Hearing her words, several clan elders immediately stepped forward. \"What woman? Let us tell you! Today, even if we have to fight with our old bones, we will never let you harm a single member of the Song family!\"","\"With just you lot?\"","The woman in red sneered coldly, a flash of murderous intent darting through her eyes. Suddenly, she raised her hand and hurled a hidden weapon at the oldest elder standing at the front: \"If you’re so eager to come forward and die, I’ll grant you your wish!\"","\"Whoosh!\"","A fierce energy blade, carrying the overwhelming pressure of a supreme powerhouse, shot forth, aiming to strike down the foremost elder by surprise and make the Song family taste the terror of impending death.","\"Watch out!\"","As the hidden weapon flew, its speed was so great that only its shadow could be seen, not its form. Yet the pressure emanating from the supreme powerhouse was too immense to ignore.","Song Lingbo stepped forward to intercept the projectile, only to hear a clang as the weapon—one he hadn’t even seen clearly—was knocked to the ground.","Clang!","Song Lingbo and his three sons froze, watching as a gold coin fell beside the projectile not far ahead.","\"Who’s there!\" The red-clad woman’s expression darkened instantly upon seeing the projectile deflected.","Feng Jiu approached from a short distance away, clad in simple azure robes. Her features were plain and unremarkable, yet her clear, cool eyes held an unflappable calm. Her pace was measured and unhurried, her aura so deeply concealed that her cultivation level remained entirely unreadable.","\"My apologies for being late,\" Feng Jiu offered an apologetic smile to the Song family and others. With a flick of her wrist, several items flew through the air, landing securely in the hands of the three Song brothers.","The Song brothers stared in stunned silence at the items now resting in their hands or laps. With their discerning eyes, they could tell these were all top-tier treasures, but where had they come from?","In contrast to the Song family’s bewilderment, the three members of the Cheng family were jolted by a wave of shock. Their hearts surged with alarm as they cried out in disbelief, \"How did those things end up in your possession?!\"","Feng Jiu smiled and addressed the Song family members: \"On my way over, I happened to deal with an old man who snuck in. It took a bit of time. Those items came from him. Consider them a gift to you.\" Her gaze shifted from the Song family to the three men, and she offered a faint smile.","\"So you’re the ones sent by the Cheng family? Looks like you’re nothing special.\""]},{"number":5040,"title":"Chapter 5040: The Power to Fight Back","paragraphs":["\"You... you... you killed him? That’s impossible!\" The old man exclaimed, unable to believe her words were true.","The middle-aged man and the woman in red both grew solemn. Impossible? If it were impossible, how could those three items be in her possession? How could she have given them away? After all, those three were the Supreme Elder’s most cherished possessions!","In that instant, they finally shed their contempt and dismissiveness, reevaluating this seemingly unremarkable woman in green robes.","To silently eliminate a Supreme Peak-tier powerhouse without a sound—this woman’s strength was terrifying!","\"Who exactly are you?\" the middle-aged man asked cautiously. In that instant, he suddenly realized that if they handled this wrong, all three of them might well die here tonight!","Yet, a woman possessing such formidable power shouldn’t be someone they’d never heard of.","\"I offered your Cheng family a way out,\" Feng Jiu said indifferently, her cold eyes fixed on their faces. \"But you chose the path of death. Don’t blame me for that. Now that it’s come to this, why don’t you decide how you want to die? I might just grant your wish.\"","\"You ambushed him, didn’t you? With the Supreme Elder’s cultivation, how could he be killed without a sound in a fair fight? You’re a cowardly ambusher!\" The red-clad woman’s voice was dark and venomous. Her hand moved, gripping a long sword. \"No matter how strong you are, could you possibly overpower the three of us combined?\"","Her gaze was dark and intense. She thought of Cheng Wanli, the disciple she had personally trained, crippled by this woman. She thought of the Supreme Elder, killed by this woman! A murderous intent surged within her heart.","\"I will sever the tendons in your hands and feet! I will chop off your hands! I will gouge out your eyes and hang them upside down before the Song family’s gates! I will slice the flesh from your body piece by piece!\" Her voice dripped with hatred. As the words fell, she clenched the sharp blade in her hand and lunged toward the azure figure ahead.","Feng Jiu curved her lips into a faint smile, one that didn’t reach her eyes. She didn’t dodge or retreat. Instead, she watched the red-clad woman charge at her with sword raised. Only when the blade’s tip neared her face did she extend her hand and clamp it between her fingers.","The overwhelming pressure and sword energy that had radiated from the blade’s tip—the very essence of a supreme warrior—dissipated naturally before it could touch Feng Jiu. Now, with just two fingers lightly pinching the sword, the red-clad woman could not advance another inch.","\"Hmph!\"","Gritting her teeth, the red-clad woman intensified her spiritual energy and aura, attempting to thrust the sword forward once more, aiming for the woman’s throat. Yet, the blade refused to advance another inch.","Feng Jiu regarded the crimson-clad woman before her, her voice calm and detached. \"Do you know why not a single sound has been made?\" Though she held the sharp blade, not a trace of her aura spilled outward.","She tugged at the corner of her mouth, narrowing her eyes as she spoke. \"Because he doesn’t even have the strength to fight back.\" As the words fell, a powerful aura surged from her, instantly enveloping the woman.","In that instant, the red-clad woman’s heart trembled. She felt an overwhelmingly terrifying pressure engulf her, as if all her strength had been drained in an instant. She froze solid where she stood..."]},{"number":5041,"title":"Chapter 5041: Might we ask your name?","paragraphs":["A chill shot up from her feet, piercing straight to her heart with a sharp whizz. The bone-chilling cold engulfed her entire being, plunging her into an abyss. Behind her, cold sweat seeped out, and every hair on her body stood on end. In that moment, her throat felt as if gripped by a ghostly hand, leaving her unable to breathe, frozen in place.","Feng Jiu’s two fingers, clutching the blade, moved forward. With a swift motion, she snatched the sword from her grasp, twisting it to hold it in her own hand. A flash of cold steel erupted, accompanied by the whistling sound of sword qi. Simultaneously, the tearing of fabric echoed through the air. Pieces of red fabric scattered chaotically to the ground, revealing the woman’s undergarments beneath.","She stood frozen, eyes wide with terror and horror, staring at the green-clad woman who had seized her blade. In that moment, she finally understood why the Supreme Elder had been killed without uttering a sound.","Simply because this woman was too powerful!","\"That red outfit of yours is truly an eyesore,\" Feng Jiu said calmly, raising the sword in her hand to press it against the woman’s throat. \"Though I’d love to grant you the death you just described, it would probably be too gruesome. How about we try a different method instead?\"","The woman’s eyes narrowed in shock. She tried to speak, but no sound came out. In that instant, she saw only a flash of cold steel. A chill touched her throat, and the next moment, her body collapsed to the ground.","The elderly man and middle-aged man from the Cheng family watched the scene unfold, involuntarily taking a step back. Their eyes held horror and shock, unable to believe that such a supreme-level powerhouse had been killed right before their eyes—throat pierced by a single sword thrust from the azure woman! And without any chance to resist!","The scene was too horrifying, too shocking, leaving them frozen in that instant, their minds filled with trembling dread.","They knew they should flee immediately! Yet their feet felt rooted to the ground, weighted down as if filled with lead, too heavy to move even half a step.","If they were this paralyzed, the elders of the Song family were even worse. Their eyes were wide with disbelief. In that moment, they finally understood why this woman called Lady Xuanyuan had said they had nothing to fear with her present—she was truly formidable!","The middle-aged man from the Cheng family was the first to snap out of it. His expression changed instantly as he stared at the green-robed woman holding her sword, her gaze fixed on them. \"Please wait a moment!\" he exclaimed in alarm.","He feared that if he spoke too slowly, the sharp blade in her hand might turn, and they too would fall silent to the ground like the already dead Yuehong.","Having reached the Supreme level of strength, they valued their lives more than anyone. In this situation, they desperately sought any glimmer of survival.","\"Any last words before you die?\" Feng Jiu didn’t seem particularly concerned. In her eyes, these two were already as good as dead; letting them speak their final words was no trouble.","Hearing this, the middle-aged man’s heart sank. He had intended to speak up to grasp a sliver of hope, but in this moment, he understood clearly that no matter what he said or did, the outcome would be the same—death was inevitable.","The old man beside him grasped the same truth. They exchanged a heavy glance, took a deep breath, and swallowed the words they had been about to speak. Instead, the old man said, \"Your power is formidable. We know we cannot escape death tonight. But before we die, might we ask your name?\""]},{"number":5042,"title":"Chapter 5042: Seeking a way out","paragraphs":["For a mighty sovereign-level powerhouse to die without even knowing who struck the fatal blow—that would be a truly pathetic end.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu arched an eyebrow, glancing at the two men. A faint smile touched her lips as she spoke calmly, \"My name is Feng Jiu.\"","Feng Jiu!","The eyes of the two men from the Cheng family narrowed sharply. In that instant, they recognized the name. They stared in horror at the indifferent-faced woman in azure robes before them, their hearts churning with dread.","Feng Jiu! The Phoenix Empress!","It was her!","Heavens! How had the Cheng family provoked such a figure?","The elder staggered backward, his body swaying precariously. He seemed to age a decade in an instant, his face ashen as he muttered, \"The Phoenix Empress... Heaven seeks to destroy the Cheng family. Heaven seeks to destroy us...\"","The middle-aged man’s face had also drained of color. He stared at Feng Jiu in her blue robes, at her ordinary, unremarkable features, and in that moment finally understood why they’d found no information about her.","She had been disguised!","The Phoenix Empress! Such a being was far beyond what the Cheng family could possibly oppose. She alone had slain the Emperor of Northern Flame, causing his entire realm to change hands overnight. This terrifying figure, known only through legend, now stood before them alive and well—and they had dared attempt to kill her!","After all they’d done, could the Cheng family possibly survive?","\"I dare not trouble Your Majesty to strike. This old man... this old man will take his own life!\" The elder trembled as he spoke, looking at Feng Jiu. \"I know the Cheng family faces inevitable doom. I only beg Your Majesty to show mercy and spare our descendants. I would be eternally grateful.\"","With that, he collapsed to his knees with a thud, performing the full kneeling bow before Feng Jiu. After three loud kowtows, he raised his hand to strike the crown of his own skull.","\"Pfft!\"","A mouthful of blood spurted forth as his entire body slumped backward.","Watching the old man strike his own crown, the middle-aged man’s heart trembled. Pressing his lips together, he knelt beside the old man’s body and performed a deep bow toward Feng Jiu: \"Please, Phoenix Empress, show mercy and spare the lives of the Cheng family’s descendants.\" Before Feng Jiu could respond, he struck his own crown.","Blood splattered as the middle-aged man collapsed. With that, the courtyard fell silent.","No one spoke. Not even the sound of breathing could be heard. Only the gentle night breeze stirred, dispersing the lingering scent of blood in the air...","Feng Jiu gazed at the two corpses, her eyes flickering slightly. These men, knowing their fate was sealed, still sought a path to survival for the future generations of the Cheng family. Their devotion was, in its own way, admirable.","She exhaled softly, tossing the sword beside the woman’s body before turning to Song Lingbo. \"We’ll depart tomorrow,\" she said calmly. \"We’ll stop by the Cheng residence to handle your final troubles. You may dispose of these bodies yourselves.\"","With that, she made no further stay, striding back toward the rear courtyard.","After watching her leave, Song Lingbo stepped forward, gathered the belongings from the corpses, and handed them to his eldest son. \"Take these to Lady Xuanyuan,\" he instructed. \"And tell your mother that everything is settled. She needn’t worry.\"","\"Understood,\" Song Yihong replied. Taking the items, the three brothers departed together."]},{"number":5043,"title":"Chapter 5043: Somber","paragraphs":["Song Lingbo instructed the shadow guards to dispose of the body. Turning around, he saw several clan elders still standing frozen in place. He stepped forward and called out, \"Elder?\"","Seeing no response, he tapped the lead elder on the shoulder: \"Elder?\"","\"Huh?\"","The elder snapped back to attention. Recognizing Song Lingbo before him and recalling the earlier incident, he began, \"Lingbo, that Lady Xuanyuan just said her name was...\" His words were cut off.","\"Let’s discuss this back at the residence! Have them clean up here first.\" Song Lingbo said, giving them a meaningful glance. Though they were all servants of the same household, the Phoenix Empress’ status made it inappropriate to discuss matters here.","\"Right, right. We’ll go inside to talk. Inside, inside.\" The Elder recovered, nodded, and took a deep breath. Watching the corpses being carried away for disposal, he still felt a bit dazed.","He couldn’t believe the crisis facing the Song family had been resolved so easily. Even more unbelievable was that Lady Xuanyuan was none other than the Phoenix Empress!","That night, after Song Lingbo briefly recounted Feng Jiu’s story to them, he went to attend to other matters.","The next morning, Feng Jiu, Song Mi’er, and the three children arrived at the main gate accompanied by members of the Song family. Along the way, Song Lingbo and his wife repeatedly reminded Mi’er to take good care of herself and urged her to stay close to Feng Jiu, working diligently by her side.","\"Father, Mother, I know. You needn’t worry,\" Mi’er said with a bright smile. \"It’s not like I won’t come home. I’ll return whenever I get the chance.\"","\"Listen carefully to Lady Xuanyuan and don’t cause trouble outside,\" Song Lingbo reminded her.","\"Got it, got it!\" Mi’er replied, quickly running over to Hao’er and the other two children, afraid they might linger longer.","\"This is as far as we’ll go,\" Feng Jiu said with a smile, looking at them. \"Thank you for your kindness during this time.\"","\"Not at all, Lady Xuanyuan, you flatter us. It is our Song family’s honor to welcome such a distinguished guest to our estate,\" the senior elder hastened to say.","Feng Jiu smiled, bid them farewell, and added, \"Once matters with the Cheng family are settled, I’ll have Mi’er inform you. Goodbye.\" With that, she led Mi’er and the three children away.","Cheng Family Manor, Longnan","At that moment, the Cheng family manor was shrouded in a dark cloud, the atmosphere oppressively heavy. The servants moved with trembling caution, afraid to make even the slightest mistake.","In the council hall, the family’s supreme elders, the ancestral patriarch, and the current head, Cheng Wanshan, sat in silence. Each wore a grave expression, deep in thought, their brows furrowed with hidden worry.","After a long silence, the family patriarch finally spoke: \"I summoned you all here early this morning to inform you of this matter. Now that their divine spirit lamps have been extinguished, what course of action do you propose?\"","This outcome had been unforeseen. Overnight, not a single one of the four Supreme Elders dispatched to the Song family had returned alive. Four lamps had extinguished simultaneously in the tower where their divine spirit lamps were enshrined. For the Cheng family, this was no trivial matter—a single misstep could spell disaster, potentially leading to the annihilation of their entire clan!","\"No one in the Song family possesses the strength to kill them. It must have been that woman in azure who took their lives. There’s definitely something wrong with her identity!\" one of them said, his face heavy with gravity."]},{"number":5044,"title":"Chapter 5044: As if facing a formidable enemy","paragraphs":["\"I fear this matter won’t end so easily.\"","Another voice spoke in a low tone, turning to the elder seated at the head of the table with solemn gravity: \" The guards who returned alive already brought word from that woman. She said that if our Cheng family sent generous gifts and apologized in person, the matter would be settled. But instead of sending apologies, we dispatched four Supreme-level experts to annihilate the Song family. Now those four are dead. If I’m not mistaken, the next target will likely be our Cheng family.\"","The hall fell silent at these words. Clearly, they too had considered this possibility.","\"Could she alone have killed all four of them? Perhaps she had hidden allies. That might explain their deaths,\" Cheng Wanshan said, still finding it hard to believe that a single woman could have slain four Supreme-level masters of the Cheng family.","\"The question now isn’t who killed those four,\" an elderly man seated at the back of the hall shook his head and sighed. \"It’s what we must do next to protect our Cheng family. If we mishandle this, it could spell the annihilation of our entire clan! Had we known this day would come, we should have sent someone to their doorstep back then. None of this would have happened.\"","His voice trailed off before he continued, \"The Supreme Elder stands at the pinnacle of power, surpassing all of us in strength. Within the entire Cheng family, only the Patriarch slightly outranks him. Consider this: what kind of being could kill him—and do so without even giving him a chance to relay any message to us?\"","\"Could it be someone from one of the reclusive families?\" someone asked, deep in thought.","The elder shook his head, sighing softly. \"I fear our entire Cheng family may face annihilation. This matter is no trivial affair. We cannot sit idly by waiting for doom. We must make arrangements early to avoid being caught unprepared.\"","\"Hmm, that was precisely my intention,\" the Patriarch in the seat of honor nodded. \"Cancel the birthday banquet! Have the mansion make the necessary arrangements. Additionally...\"","His hand paused mid-stroke on his beard, clutching at the hair as hesitation washed over him. \"Send the younger generation of Cheng descendants away immediately. Let them lie low for now. If our family survives this ordeal, they may return.\"","Hearing this, the mood among the assembled grew heavy. Having seen too much of the world, they knew they had misjudged this situation and been careless. Things needn’t have escalated to this point, but now...","\"Everyone, there’s no need to overthink this. After all, we still have so many people here. The situation may not be beyond redemption.\" Cheng Wanshan spoke, hoping to ease their minds, but no one paid him any mind.","Those present had lived long enough. Could they not recognize their fate when it stared them in the face?","\"I’ll make preparations first—deploying a defensive formation throughout the estate.\" An elder rose, announced his intention, and departed.","\"I’ll prepare as well,\" another declared, rising to follow.","The others departed one after another. Finally, only the Cheng family patriarch and Cheng Wanshan remained in the hall. Looking at the empty meeting chamber, Cheng Wanshan’s expression darkened. \"Patriarch...\"","The patriarch rose and waved his hand. \"Enough. No need to say more. Go make the arrangements. Close the doors to visitors. Cancel the birthday banquet. Also, select a group of Cheng family descendants to send away today.\""]},{"number":5045,"title":"Chapter 5045: Trepidition","paragraphs":["\"Yes.\"","Cheng Wanshan acquiesced. At this point, there was no other option but to proceed with this arrangement. He could only hope that the woman wouldn’t dare to actually come to the door. Otherwise, this would inevitably become a life-or-death battle.","The fear within the Cheng family had become palpable to its descendants, especially after batches of young members were secretly sent away.","Externally, guests who had prepared to attend the Cheng family’s birthday banquet were astonished upon learning of its cancellation. Members of various noble families and factions keenly sensed the unusual atmosphere.","After all, the invitations for the Cheng family’s birthday banquet had been sent out long ago. Now, to announce its cancellation without elaborating on the reasons—if anyone claimed there was nothing unusual about this, even a three-year-old child wouldn’t believe it.","Those with keen interest probed discreetly and learned that the Cheng family had suffered the loss of four supreme masters under unknown circumstances. The younger generation of the family had been secretly relocated and sent away. It seemed the Cheng family had provoked some formidable figure. They had even discreetly invited allied powerful figures to station themselves at the Cheng residence. The entire family was preparing for battle, naturally leaving no room for thoughts of a birthday banquet.","The Chengs lived in this tense, anxious atmosphere, unsure when their great calamity would strike. They remained vigilant day and night, daring not to relax for a moment. They even stationed spies to watch the city gates, reporting immediately upon spotting any outsiders.","Several days later, Feng Jiu, accompanied by Mi’er and the three children, entered the territory of Longnan.","That day, after entering the city, they found an inn to rest. A Cheng family guard, disguised as a beggar and stationed at the city gate, was startled to the core the moment he saw Feng Jiu. He dared not even glance at her again, immediately burying his head.","Once he saw them enter the inn, he dashed toward the Cheng residence.","\"Master! Master!\"","Cheng Wanshan, who was discussing matters with the Patriarch and others in the main hall, saw the guard in beggar’s garb rushing in frantically. His face darkened as he barked, \"What a disgraceful spectacle! What is it? Speak quickly!\"","Noticing the Patriarch and others present in the hall, the beggar-clad guard finally suppressed his panic. Swallowing hard, he stammered, \"Master... it’s... that woman. She’s here...\"","\"You say that woman has arrived?\"","The Patriarch, seated at the head, immediately sat up straight. No one noticed the slight tremor that ran through his body at that moment. Steeling his voice, he fixed his gaze on the beggar-clad guard and asked with a hint of urgency, \"How many of them came? Where are they now? Are they heading towards our Cheng family?\"","\"It’s that woman. I saw her clearly. It’s the woman in azure who sent us back with the message.\" The guard clenched his fist, feeling cold sweat seep through his palms and into his heart.","He took a deep breath before continuing, \"There are five of them in total. Besides the woman in azure, there’s a girl around fifteen or sixteen, a boy about eleven or twelve, and two younger children.\"","Hearing this, the Cheng family members exchanged bewildered glances. The family patriarch, his brow furrowed, pressed, \"Are you certain? That woman brought no other helpers, only a young girl and three children? No one else?\"","\"No, just those few. After entering the city, they headed straight for an inn. Upon seeing them, I hurried back to report.\""]},{"number":5046,"title":"Chapter 5046: Guess","paragraphs":["Upon hearing this, the Cheng family patriarch folded his arms behind his back, furrowing his brow in deep thought as he paced the hall.","The other supreme masters of the Cheng family listened in silence, heads bowed slightly, lost in their own thoughts.","Only Cheng Wanshan laughed immediately upon hearing the words: \"Old Predecessor, I believe your worries are unnecessary. She’s just a woman—how strong could she possibly be?\" Since she dares to come here like this, I’ll lead men there now and wipe them out without delay!\"","He had expected the Old Predecessor to agree with his words, but instead, the Old Predecessor’s gaze turned dark and cold as it fixed on him. Startled, the smile froze on his face, unable to retreat.","\"Brainless fool!\"","The Cheng family Old Predecessor’s voice was dark and furious as he rebuked him. He snorted heavily, swept his sleeve aside, and strode back to his seat at the head of the table. Staring at Cheng Wanshan, who was now drenched in cold sweat, he spoke in a grim tone: \"How on earth did you become the Cheng family Patriarch? You lack even the most basic discernment. The Cheng family now faces great calamity, and you will not escape blame!\"","This rebuke carried a strong sense of venting anger. Faced with an unavoidable family catastrophe, hearing these words only intensified his fury. It also served as an outlet for the anxiety and unease gnawing at his heart.","Rebuked before the entire assembly, Cheng Wanshan bowed his head, daring not to show discontent or anger. For the Old Predecessor was the ultimate authority in the Cheng family. Even if he were killed, no one would dare utter a word.","\"If it’s truly as the guard said—that she came with only one young woman and three children—then there’s only one possibility,\" an elder spoke up, his expression grave as he looked toward the Old Predecessor seated at the head. \"That her power has grown so formidable that she alone could shake the entire Cheng family to its core.\"","The hall fell silent at these words, quiet enough to hear a pin drop.","Truthfully, this thought had crossed the minds of several present. If she had brought reinforcements, it might be manageable. But if she truly came alone... her power would be terrifyingly formidable.","\"It suddenly occurs to me,\" another elder spoke up, his face now deathly pale and his demeanor unnervingly frail, \"that among women of this age possessing such formidable power, there seems to be only one.\"","\"Who?\" the others in the hall turned to him, their eyes demanding an answer.","The elder lifted his gaze to meet theirs. Taking a deep breath to steady his surging emotions, he uttered, \"Phoenix Empress.\"","\"Whoa! That... that’s impossible!\"","The Cheng family Old Predecessor sucked in a sharp breath. Seated at the head of the table, he leaned back in his chair, overcome by shock and dread. Though he declared it impossible, his expression betrayed that he too harbored this suspicion.","\"Besides her, who else could it be?\"","The elder looked at them and sighed softly. \"Who else possesses the power to single-handedly slay four Supreme-level experts? Who else would dare come to Longnan alone? We never uncovered the identity of that azure-robed woman because none of us considered that possibility. But now that we do, everything falls into place.\"","\"If it truly is that one, I say we needn’t fight this battle. No matter how we fight, we cannot defeat her. Remember, she single-handedly killed someone of the stature of the Great Emperor Northern Flame. How much more so for us?\" Another elder murmured, leaning back into his chair as if all his strength had been drained in that instant."]},{"number":5047,"title":"Chapter 5047: Course of action","paragraphs":["\"Heaven is set to destroy our Cheng clan!\"","The clan patriarch murmured, the fighting spirit that had sustained them vanishing in that instant. For they all knew that if it truly was that one, even summoning countless powerful allies would be futile.","\"Unless she shows mercy, our Cheng clan will face annihilation...\"","At this realization, the assembly fell silent. After a long pause, the Old Predecessor declared gravely, \"There is only one viable course of action left.\"","All eyes turned to him, seeking answers. \"What is your strategy, Old Predecessor?\"","\"We shall go to her to beg forgiveness and offer our lives, pleading for a sliver of hope for the future generations of the Cheng family.\" The family Old Predecessor took a deep breath, rose to his feet, and gazed at them. \"This is our only option now. If we wait for her to come here, I fear not a single soul of our family will survive.\"","The several Supreme Beings listened, falling silent for a moment. This course might indeed secure a sliver of hope for their descendants, but for them... it was a dead end.","Reaching their age hadn’t been easy! Naturally, they cherished their lives, but was there any other path forward now?","\"Is there truly no other way?\" one of them couldn’t help but ask.","The Cheng family patriarch remained silent. Instead, Cheng Wanshan glanced at the Old Predecessor and declared, \"I have a plan.\"","Hearing this, all eyes turned to him. \"What plan?\"","Even the Cheng family patriarch turned his gaze toward him, wondering what solution he could possibly propose.","Seeing the Old Predecessor looking at him, Cheng Wanshan’s mind stirred. He said, \"Didn’t the guards say she brought a young girl and three children? We could capture that girl and the three children. Use them to threaten her into leaving Longnan and never laying a finger on the Cheng family again.\"","\"Are you trying to die slowly?\"","The Cheng family patriarch’s face darkened, his expression turning grim. \"If we do that, we’ll be cutting off the very future of our Cheng family descendants.\"","\"But Old Predecessor, even if we beg for mercy, do you truly believe she’ll spare our descendants?\" Would she truly spare our entire family? If we follow my plan and succeed, our family might yet escape this calamity. None of you elders would have to die.\" Cheng Wanshan finished, his gaze sweeping over the assembled elders.","He knew some among them were swayed. After all, who would choose death over life?","\"I agree. This plan is worth a try.\"","An elder spoke up, looking at the family Old Predecessor. \"Wanshan is right. Even if we go to apologize, would she truly spare the rest of our family? Better to take a chance.\"","\"I agree too,\" another elder chimed in.","\"I think we should test the waters first,\" he said, looking at the others. \"Didn’t they say she’s at the inn? Let’s go check first! If it doesn’t work, we’ll take the next step.\"","Hearing their words, the Cheng family Old Predecessor sighed and said, \"Since you all feel this way, let’s go take a look first! Before that, we should send away the few experts we invited to the manor, lest they get dragged into this.\"","With that, they nodded in agreement and went to make preparations. After seeing off the powerful guests from the manor, they had the guards lead the way to the inn.","Meanwhile, Feng Jiu was soaking in the bath at the inn. The three children sat on the first floor, while Mi’er bustled about in the kitchen."]},{"number":5048,"title":"Chapter 5048: Query","paragraphs":["The moment the Cheng family elders stepped out, nearly every prominent family in the city learned of it instantly. Some sent spies to observe, while others came out personally, eager to see what was happening.","\"Old Predecessor, those three children arrived with that woman,\" the guard leading the way said, gesturing toward the three children seated by the first-floor window.","The Cheng family Old Predecessor looked over. He saw the three children sitting there, drinking water and eating pastries, chatting occasionally, and pointing at things on the street outside with smiles. Their ages were indeed as the guard had said—all quite young. However, it was immediately apparent that these three children were not from ordinary families; they were likely born into a distinguished lineage.","As they appeared, Hao’er also noticed them. After quietly observing them for a moment, Hao’er guessed these people must be from the Cheng family.","Perhaps sensing Hao’er’s gaze shift elsewhere, Mu Chen and Yue’er both looked toward the doorway. After a glance, they turned back. Yue’er asked, \"Why are they staring at us?\"","\"They must be from the Cheng family,\" Muchen said, finishing the water in his cup. He told Yue’er, \"Go check if Sister Mi’er has finished preparing the dishes.\"","\"Okay.\" Yue’er, seeing her brother dismissing her to the kitchen, didn’t protest. She simply nodded and headed toward the kitchen.","Because of their arrival, the inn’s patrons were swiftly cleared out by the Cheng family’s people. Only Hao’er’s table remained seated in the entire inn. Outside, Cheng family guards surrounded the area, preventing anyone from approaching.","\"Children, do you know the identity of the woman in green who traveled with you?\" the Cheng family Old Predecessor inquired as he approached.","Hearing this, Hao’er and Muchen exchanged glances. Hao’er spoke up, \"You’ve come all this way—don’t you already know?\"","The Cheng family patriarch’s eyes flickered. Seeing these two children sitting here without a trace of fear or panic, daring to speak to him like this, he couldn’t help but be slightly moved.","They truly weren’t children from ordinary families. Such composure at their age was truly rare.","In the kitchen, Yue’er approached Song Mi’er and said, \"Sister Mi’er, the Cheng family people are here outside! My second senior brother sent me to tell you.\" As she spoke, she tiptoed and secretly pinched a piece of meat, popping it into her mouth. Finishing, she even sucked her little finger into her mouth and licked it clean.","Upon hearing her words, Mi’er turned just in time to catch the sight. She gasped softly, \"Oh my! How could you lick your finger! Did you wash your hands just now? You shouldn’t put your fingers in your mouth.\" As she spoke, she led Yue’er to the sink to wash her hands. \"Are you hungry? Let me serve you some food to fill your stomach first.\"","Yue’er smiled brightly, letting her help wash her hands while saying, \"I did wash my hands just now.\"","\"Even if you did, you shouldn’t put your fingers in your mouth. It’s dirty.\" Mi’er said, washing her hands thoroughly before taking a bowl and chopsticks to serve her some food. She asked, \"Did the Cheng family arrive? Are your two Senior Brothers outside?\" She remained vigilant, mindful not to reveal their identities.","\"Mhm, they’re still sitting over there~\" Yue’er took the bowl and chopsticks, sat down at the small chair, and began eating.","Hearing this, Mi’er said, \"Then you eat here. I’ll go check.\" With that, she grabbed her own flat pan from the stove and started to head out, only to be pulled back by a small hand."]},{"number":5049,"title":"Chapter 5049: Seeking A Way Out","paragraphs":["While chewing her food, Yue’er said, \"My senior brother told me to come in and tell you—you’re not allowed to go out.\"","Hearing this, Mi’er widened her eyes. \"Not allowed to go out? How can that be? There are only two of them outside? You... cough, has the My lady been informed? I need to go check.\" With that, she pulled her small hand away and strode toward the exit.","Seeing this, Yue’er wanted to follow, but noticing the uneaten food in her bowl and the soup still simmering on the stove, she continued eating while watching the flames in the hearth.","With her Mother present, nothing untoward would happen.","Upstairs in the guest room, Feng Jiu opened the door and stepped out. Dressed simply in a light azure robe, her long black hair cascaded down her back. Fresh from a bath, she looked languid and relaxed.","She walked to the railing, standing there looking down. Her gaze fell upon the Cheng family members below, and she asked, \"Do you have business?\"","Seeing her, the Cheng family Old Predecessor and the others recognized her instantly. Observing her ordinary features and simple blue gown, they knew she had altered her appearance. Therefore, the Old Predecessor stepped forward and bowed respectfully.","\"I am the Old Predecessor of the Cheng family, paying my respects to My Lady.\" At that moment, his heart leapt with nervousness, pounding wildly with trepidation.","Feng Jiu descended the stairs slowly, saying, \"I hadn’t even sought you out, yet you’ve come to me of your own accord.\"","Hearing these words, the Cheng family members flinched inwardly, lowering their heads slightly, not daring to meet her gaze.","\"My lady, we have come to beg your forgiveness. We offer ten of the Cheng family’s most precious treasures and pledge to forfeit our cultivation. We implore you to show mercy and spare our family this time. Henceforth, we shall teach our descendants to do good deeds and never forget your great kindness.\"","Watching her descend the steps, the Cheng family Old Predecessor swept up his robe and knelt, delivering a heavy kowtow to her.","The crowd watching from outside the inn froze at this sight. Eyes widened in disbelief as they stared at the patriarch kneeling and kowtowing.","A figure who could send an entire town into turmoil with a mere stamp of his foot was now kneeling before an unassuming woman in green robes? Had they not witnessed it themselves, they would never have believed it possible!","Feng Jiu stood before him, her gaze flickering as she watched the old man kneeling with his head pressed to the ground. For people like them, self-destructing their cultivation meant nothing but waiting for death. And once their cultivation was gone, they wouldn’t have much time left to live.","She had a vague suspicion about why they had come to the inn seeking a way to survive. After all, these were powerful individuals who had lived for hundreds of years. Upon learning that the four people sent by the Cheng family had all died, they should have been able to guess the final fate of the Cheng family.","She walked slowly over and sat down at the table where the two children sat. Her voice was measured as she spoke: \"Though this world reveres the strong, one must always leave a sliver of hope. Since you have come to me seeking mercy, I might spare your Cheng family this once. However...\"","Hearing her words, the Cheng family Old Predecessor’s heart swelled with hope. He instinctively lifted his gaze toward her, only to pause mid-sentence as her voice trailed off, causing his heart to leap back into his throat.","\"Please speak, My Lady! If you are willing to show mercy and spare the descendants of the Cheng family, whatever you command, we shall obey!\" the Old Predecessor hastily declared."]},{"number":5050,"title":"Chapter 5050: Show Mercy","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu glanced at him and declared, \"The Cheng family must surrender all possessions and vacate Longnan within three days.\"","Hearing this, the Cheng family members were shaken. Surrendering all their wealth and leaving Longnan within three days...","Without their wealth to sustain them, the Cheng descendants, accustomed to a life of luxury, would plummet from heaven to hell. Deprived of both wealth and cultivation resources, it would be exceedingly difficult for any future generations of the Cheng family to produce another powerful cultivator.","Longnan was the ancestral homeland of the Cheng family, the very roots of their lineage. To leave Longnan meant uprooting themselves to settle elsewhere, effectively erasing the existence of the great Longnan clan, the House of Cheng...","Moreover, the powerful figures who guarded the family would struggle to survive. Their cultivation would be shattered, leaving them crippled and with only a short time to live. The Cheng family’s generations-old enemies would certainly not let this opportunity pass. When that time came, the members of the Cheng family would likely face even greater peril.","Contemplating these dire consequences, the Old Predecessor of the Cheng family felt his back involuntarily slump. He knew only that the future of the Cheng family was shrouded in darkness. Yet, if he agreed, the descendants of the Cheng family might have a sliver of hope for survival. If he refused, the entire clan would likely face annihilation...","Feng Jiu sipped her tea calmly, speaking without haste: \"You have no other path. Since you came, you must know my identity. Even if you had sent the Cheng family’s descendants away beforehand, you should understand that with my power, ending their lives would be as simple as uttering a single word.\"","Her words sent a shock through the Cheng family, especially the Old Predecessor. His lips trembled slightly, and his pupils contracted sharply. The hesitation that had lingered vanished in that instant, replaced by resolve.","\"This old man obeys My Lady. Please grant me three days to make arrangements. After three days, I shall personally present the Cheng family’s wealth before My Lady and lead them out of Longnan.\" He bowed slowly, his heart heavy with resignation. Yet he understood this was her gracious mercy, offering the Cheng family a sliver of survival.","Had the roles been reversed, they might not have shown such mercy to the Song family.","\"I can grant you three more days. As for them—their cultivation must be stripped immediately.\" Feng Jiu turned to the elderly men behind him, her voice cool and measured.","The elders exchanged glances, clenched their teeth, and declared, \"We thank you for your mercy, My Lady. We shall now forfeit our cultivation ourselves.\" With that, one raised his hand and severed his own cultivation.","Seeing this, the others followed suit, each severing their own cultivation. Sacrificing their cultivation was preferable to taking their own lives now. If they could find a way to extend their remaining lifespan within their dwindling years, perhaps—just perhaps—they might avoid death.","Holding onto this faint hope, they severed their cultivation. As their power vanished, their already aged faces grew even more withered. They slowly slumped to the ground, too weak even to stand, leaning against the wall and gasping for breath.","Seeing this, Feng Jiu finally spoke: \"Return now. I will wait for you here in three days.\"","\"Yes, thank you, My Lady,\" the Cheng family Old Predecessor replied in a trembling voice. Rising, he glanced back at the barely living figures slumped behind him. Taking a deep breath, he averted his eyes and called out: \"Someone, escort the elders back to the Cheng residence.\"","Clang!","Suddenly, the sound of a bowl crashing to the floor echoed from the kitchen.","Hearing the noise, Mi’er, standing nearby, paled. \"Little Qi!\""]},{"number":5051,"title":"Chapter 5051: Stunned","paragraphs":["Seeing Mi’er dash toward the kitchen, Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow and glanced at the Cheng family members. Her gaze swept over the Cheng family patriarch, the several elders stripped of their cultivation, and the guards before she asked, \"Where is your Patriarch?\"","The Cheng family Old Predecessor froze, only now realizing that Cheng Wanshan was missing. Recalling the commotion from the kitchen and the absence of Cheng Wanshan, his face instantly drained of color. He shouted in alarm, \"Where is Cheng Wanshan? Where did he go?\"","Behind him, cold sweat seeped through his clothes as his heart sank.","Please, let it not be what he feared...","\"My lady, Little Qi is gone. A bowl fell on the kitchen floor—it was the dish I served her just before coming out. The kitchen window was open; she must have been kidnapped through it,\" Mi’er said, her face filled with self-reproach.","It was all her fault for not watching her closely, leaving her alone in the kitchen.","Hao’er and Muchen exchanged a glance, then stood silently beside their Mother.","Feng Jiu sipped her tea before rising. \"Then we must go to the Cheng residence! Barring any surprises, she should be there.\" Her voice paused as her clear eyes shifted to the ashen-faced Cheng family Old Predecessor. A cold smile touched her lips. \"Wouldn’t you agree?\"","The Cheng patriarch knelt with a thud. \" My lady sees clearly. We truly know nothing. I’ll return immediately. If Cheng Wanshan is indeed responsible, I... I will personally kill him!\"","\"Doubt you have the guts,\" Feng Jiu remarked coolly, glancing at him before adding, \"Shall we proceed?\" She no longer worried about her three children. She trusted they could handle any danger themselves.","\"Yes, yes.\"","The Cheng family Old Predecessor hurriedly rose and led her toward the Cheng residence. At that moment, he despised Cheng Wanshan with every fiber of his being. If Cheng Wanshan was indeed responsible, such actions would render all their efforts utterly wasted. His sole hope now was that Cheng Wanshan hadn’t harmed the little girl. If he had, every member of the Cheng family would pay with their lives.","The patriarch personally escorted her to the Cheng residence, with Mi’er, Hao’er, and Muchen following behind. Yet, as the patriarch hurried to the front gate, a piercing scream erupted from within.","\"Aah...\"","\"Roar!\"","The screams were followed by a furious beastly roar. The sound carried the overwhelming pressure of a Sacred Beast, stunning the entire Cheng family into silence.","Especially the guards in the front courtyard. Their eyes widened in shock as they stared at the seemingly innocent little girl. Who could have imagined she would smile sweetly and summon a Sacred Beast? And to bite off the Patriarch’s leg while he was completely unprepared?","Gazing at the blood-soaked leg flung aside, then at the little girl standing nearby with an innocent, pure expression, everyone felt a chill run down their spines, their hair standing on end.","Before they even reached the door, Feng Jiu heard voices inside. Unsurprised, she arched an eyebrow, the corners of her lips curving into a faint, almost imperceptible smile.","Her daughter, Feng Jiu’s daughter, was no soft target for anyone to push around.","Behind her, Hao’er and Muchen wore equally calm, detached expressions. Clearly, they too had anticipated this very scene.","Only Mi’er hesitated for a moment, finally letting out a sigh of relief.","The Cheng family Old Predecessor abruptly pushed open the door and stepped inside, only to be stunned by the scene that met his eyes."]},{"number":5052,"title":"Chapter 5052: Incinerate","paragraphs":["Cheng Wanshan, missing a leg, lay sprawled on the ground, his face deathly pale as he screamed in terror and horror. He struggled desperately to escape, but a majestic Sacred Beast lay astride him, licking the blood from its mouth with its tongue. The beast’s immense weight pinned him down, rendering him utterly helpless.","Not far away, a severed leg lay in a pool of blood, discarded by the beast. Those nearby watched the scene in horror, none daring to approach.","Beside them, the little girl observed the spectacle. Her eyes crinkled with amusement, showing no trace of fear—only excitement and anticipation.","The Old Predecessor of the Cheng family, who had seen much in his life, was utterly stunned by the scene that greeted him upon his hurried return.","\"What... what on earth is going on?\"","\"Aunty!\" Yue’er’s face lit up with joy the moment she spotted her mother. Calling out in a soft, sweet voice, she scampered toward her. Out in the world, they couldn’t call her mother \"Mother,\" only \"Aunty.\"","Feng Jiu watched the little girl run over, smiling as she reached out to scoop her up. \"What brings you here?\"","Yue’er clung to her neck and explained, \"That bad man climbed through the window and kidnapped me. After dragging me here, he tried to tie me up, so I summoned my contract beast to bite him.\"","\"Arghhhhh! Old Predecessor, Old Predecessor, save me...\"","In that instant, Cheng Wanshan’s arm was torn clean off the ground. The brutal, bloody scene of flesh being ripped away sent chills down the spines of the Cheng family members watching.","The Cheng family Old Predecessor couldn’t understand why Cheng Wanshan, a man of considerable strength, had offered no resistance to this Sacred Beast’s attack.","Feng Jiu glanced at Cheng Wanshan, then raised an eyebrow at the little girl in her arms. \"Did you drug him?\"","\"Hehe, just a little bit.\"","She held up her little finger to measure. Who knew he’d get the evil idea to capture her? Since he wanted to grab her, she might as well join in the fun. After all, Mother was preparing to deal with the Cheng family. Even if she let the lion tear him apart, Mother probably wouldn’t blame her.","\"Snap!\"","\"Ah...\"","A sharp crack echoed, followed by another piercing scream. Everyone looked over to see the lion had snapped Cheng Wanshan’s neck. Yet, the instant his scream echoed, his soul fled the body. The corpse on the ground instantly became lifeless. A streak of light shot out from the body, hurtling toward Hao’er and Muchen without a moment’s hesitation.","He thought: If his soul escaped and found a new host body, he could still live. If that body belonged to one of these two boys, even this woman wouldn’t dare harm him!","But he had overestimated his speed.","\"You’re asking for death!\"","Feng Jiu’s voice rang out, cool and laced with icy intent. Almost the instant her words left her lips, a ball of flame shot from her hand, whooshing out to envelop the fleeing soul.","\"Sssh! Ah! No... I don’t want to die... No... Old Predecessor, Old Predecessor, save me...\"","A shrill, frantic scream pierced the air. The soul, trapped within the flames, writhed and screamed in agony. Yet, as the flames consumed it, not only did the soul perish, but it too was reduced to ashes, vanishing into thin air..."]},{"number":5053,"title":"Chapter 5053: Return to the Island","paragraphs":["The Old Predecessor of the Cheng family watched this scene unfold, his eyes narrowing sharply. His lips trembled slightly, yet not a single word escaped his mouth.","The might of Phoenix Empress had only been heard of before, but witnessing it firsthand revealed that even a powerhouse of his caliber could not help but feel his heart tremble at the sight.","Feng Jiu withdrew her hand, casting a cold glance at the corpse on the ground before turning her gaze to the Cheng family Old Predecessor. \"Since you’re all here, we’ll be staying right here,\" she stated.","\"Yes, yes. I’ll show you all to the courtyard to rest,\" the Cheng family Old Predecessor hastily replied, snapping back to his senses. Daring not utter another word, he swiftly led them toward the rear courtyard.","Originally planning to stay at an inn, Feng Jiu and her companions ended up lodging at the Cheng residence. This left the entire Cheng family on edge, tiptoeing around in fear of offending her with any misstep.","The sole consolation for the Cheng family patriarch was that, aside from the family’s few supreme elders and his Old Predecessor, the rest of the household remained unaffected. This offered a glimmer of hope for the Cheng clan—at least, not all of them were weaklings.","Over the course of three days, the family’s Old Predecessor surrendered all the estate’s wealth and resources to Feng Jiu. Of course, it was impossible to know if any of the younger generation or others had secretly kept something for themselves.","Outsiders sought to uncover the identity of that woman in azure and the nature of the Cheng family’s transgression, but all such inquiries met with silence.","Three days later, before Feng Jiu and the Cheng family’s principal elders, the old patriarch personally stripped himself of all cultivation. Carried away by his family, the group hastily departed the Cheng residence, leaving Longnan behind...","Feng Jiu and her companions lingered at the Cheng residence for one more day. After selling the estate, they too departed. Those curious about her identity watched them leave but dared not follow or inquire further. They could only see them exit the city, their destination unknown...","Half a month later, on the Immortal Isle, Yue’er, Muchen, and Hao’er played near the Rainbow Bridge. Yue’er’s laughter, like tinkling silver bells, frequently drifted on the breeze.","\"Big brothers, come chase me! Come catch me!\" Yue’er ran with a radiant smile, her feet moving like the wind as she called back to the two brothers behind her.","Hao’er and Muchen exchanged a glance, both wearing indulgent smiles. \"Then you’d better be careful,\" they said, \"lest we catch you and make you cry.\" \" No sooner had the words left their mouths than two figures shot forward like the wind, chasing after their little sister in her skirt.","\"Hehe, you’ll never catch me!\" Yue’er said with a smile. Seeing them chase after her, she immediately sped up to make them run after her. Her skills might not match theirs, but when it came to running away, the two of them might not be able to keep up with her.","The three children played across the island while their contract beasts roamed freely. Especially Yue’er’s newly arrived Sacred Beast lion was filled with wonder and curiosity about this place.","However, upon seeing the ancient Sacred Beasts and Super Sacred Beasts scattered everywhere across the island, it tucked its tail between its legs. It slunk over and sat quietly to one side, not daring to wander near those ancient Sacred Beasts and Super Sacred Beasts.","Feng Jiu pored over books within the palace halls. She had already gained some insight into unlocking the barrier between the Upper Immortal Realm and the Lower Immortal Realm. Since returning two days prior, she had devoted herself entirely to this research."]},{"number":5054,"title":"Chapter 5054: Yuan Jing’s Visit","paragraphs":["The Immortal Island was sparsely populated, inhabited only by cranes or maidens transformed from flower spirits. Within the grand hall, she stood alone, undisturbed by any sound except the faint rustling of pages as she leafed through the books.","Meanwhile, outside the island, a young guard and an elderly man escorted a man clad in white. The three stood at the entrance to the island.","Barred by the protective barrier, they could neither touch nor approach it, remaining halted before it.","\"Young Master, we have arrived,\" the old man said, gazing at the mist-shrouded island ahead, his voice tinged with excitement.","The white-robed man, Yuan Jing, fixed his lifeless gaze ahead. Though he knew the island before him belonged to the Phoenix Empress, his blindness rendered him surprisingly calm.","\"I am Yuan Jing, here to pay my respects to the Phoenix Empress.\"","His voice, imbued with spirit energy and an aura of authority, pierced through the clouds and barrier, carrying into the heart of the Immortal Island.","A sacred crane soaring through the island’s skies circled the entrance, listened to the words, and soon flapped its wings toward the main hall. Upon arrival, Shadow One transformed the crane into a beautiful immortal maiden who landed lightly before the hall’s entrance. She approached with delicate steps and reported softly: \"Master, a visitor has arrived. He claims the name Yuan Jing. Shall I grant him audience?\"","Hearing the voice from outside the hall, Feng Jiu paused briefly in turning the pages of her book before replying, \"Let them enter.\"","\"Yes, Master.\" The fairy responded softly, then turned and flew off to greet the visitor.","Yuan Jing and his two companions followed the fairy inside. Unable to see, he had no idea what kind of celestial wonderland lay beyond the gates of this immortal isle. Yet he distinctly sensed that the breathing of the two men beside him had changed.","\"Uncle Yuan, is the scenery inside truly beautiful?\" Yuan Jing asked, his gentle voice tinged with a hint of amusement.","\"Beautiful? It’s beyond description—a true paradise,\" the elder replied, his voice trembling with excitement. Yet he lowered his tone, mindful of the young master’s blindness. \"Young Master, when your eyes are healed, you too shall behold this celestial realm.\"","Hearing this, Yuan Jing smiled but said nothing.","Finally, they arrived before the grand hall. The fairy entered to announce their arrival, then led them inside before withdrawing.","\"Yuan Jing pays his respects to the Phoenix Empress,\" Yuan Jing bowed forward.","\"We pay our respects to the Phoenix Empress,\" the old man and the guard bowed deeply in a kneeling salute.","Feng Jiu closed the book in her hands, looked at the three figures in the hall, and said, \"Have a seat.\"","\"Thank you, Phoenix Empress.\"","Yuan Jing expressed his gratitude, allowing the old man to lead him to a seat nearby. The old man and the guard stood behind him, not daring to look around, standing quietly with their eyes half-lowered.","\"You found the it so quickly?\" Feng Jiu inquired, her gaze fixed on Yuan Jing. It must be said, the Immortal Realm certainly had no shortage of strikingly handsome men and beautiful women.","\"Yes. As soon as I obtained the fish eye, I brought it here.\" Speaking, he retrieved a box from his sleeve and handed it to the elder beside him.","The elder accepted it, bowed his head, and presented it with both hands in reverence: \"For the Phoenix Empress to examine.\"","Feng Jiu glanced at the box. As she opened it, a chill spread out, accompanied by a potent aura of spirit energy. Inside lay a pair of crimson eyes, crystalline and gleaming."]},{"number":5055,"title":"Chapter 5055: Who’s the Strongest?","paragraphs":["After a glance, she closed the box and said, \"Indeed, these are the mature crimson eyes, preserved remarkably well.\" Taking the box, she turned to Yuan Jing. \"Since you’re a friend of Mo Chen and he made this request, I can certainly heal your eyes.\"","\"Thank you, Phoenix Empress.\" Yuan Jing stood and bowed respectfully toward the front.","\"I need to extract spiritual essence from these fish eyes. For the time being, you may stay here. However, the two people with you must leave first.\"","Feng Jiu’s gaze shifted to the old man’s guards. With three children still present, she wouldn’t allow them to stay—too many people, too many eyes. As for Yuan Jing, she had confirmed with Mo Chen that he was indeed his friend. Moreover, Mo Chen had spoken highly of Yuan Jing. Given that, she naturally treated him with some leniency.","Hearing this, Yuan Jing paused, then turned to the two beside him. \"Uncle Yuan, you two should return first.\"","\"But... Young Master, you cannot see. Without us by your side, it will surely be inconvenient...\" the elder said with concern.","\"It’s fine. I can manage on my own,\" he replied with a gentle smile.","Seeing this, the elder and the guard finally agreed. They stepped forward and bowed to the Phoenix Empress seated at the head of the table: \"Phoenix Empress, our Young Master has troubled you.\"","\"Mhm.\" Feng Jiu responded, summoning a celestial maid to escort them away.","After they departed, she looked at Yuan Jing seated there, then slowly walked down and said, \"There are celestial maids here. Should you require anything, simply instruct them to attend to it.\"","\"Very well.\" Yuan Jing acknowledged, then paused before asking, \"Are there others here? Might my presence prove inappropriate?\" After all, he was a man. In such a vast place, his company might risk tarnishing her reputation.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow, gave him a once-over from head to toe, and curved her lips into a smile. \"Unseemly? You’re overthinking it.\" As soon as the words left her mouth, she summoned a celestial maid and instructed her to escort him away.","After he departed, she walked to the palace entrance and extended her divine sense outward. She sensed the three children chasing each other near the Rainbow Bridge. Seeing this, she gathered her qi and rose into the air, gliding toward them.","\"Mother!\"","Yue’er spotted her and immediately darted toward her, throwing herself into her arms and giggling, \"Mother, Mother! My brothers couldn’t catch me!\"","\"Mother.\"","Hao’er and Muchen soon arrived at their mother’s side, both with beads of sweat on their foreheads. They had chased Yue’er in a wide circle but failed to catch her, which genuinely surprised them.","\"Sister, how is your footwork is so fast?\" Muchen couldn’t help asking.","\"Hehe, of course! Master taught me. He said my skills aren’t as good as yours two, but I can win with speed, so I trained hard!\" she declared proudly, her face beaming with joy.","Feng Jiu smiled upon hearing this. \"It seems letting you two apprentice under the Azure Emperor was indeed the right choice.\"","\"Mother, I heard people say our master is very powerful. So who’s more powerful—our master, or Father and Mother?\" Yue’er lifted her head from Feng Jiu’s embrace, blinking her beautiful big eyes with curiosity.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu couldn’t help but smile, replying with a hint of jest, \"When the time comes, perhaps Father and Mother will have a spar with your master. Then you’ll know.\""]},{"number":5056,"title":"Chapter 5056: Bringing Food","paragraphs":["\"Huh?\"","Upon hearing this, Yue’er froze momentarily, then said anxiously, \"Mother, Mother! Please don’t fight with Father! He’s been so kind to us—don’t bully him!\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu couldn’t help but chuckle softly. She gently pinched her little nose and teased, \"So you know to protect your master now? Don’t you want to know who’s stronger—your father and mother, or your master?\"","\"Hmm...\" Yue’er pondered for a moment, her eyes twinkling mischievously. \"Father and Mother are the strongest. Master comes after them, but he’s still very strong too.\"","\"It’s good you know how to protect your master. That way, his kindness towards you won’t be in vain.\" Feng Jiu chuckled softly, gently tapping her nose. She then addressed the three of them, \"A man named Yuan Jing has arrived on the island to treat his eyes. Mother will help him refine the medicinal solution. You three can play on your own these days, but remember—play is play, yet don’t neglect your cultivation. Especially you.\"","She looked at her daughter in her arms and added, \"The Ancient Divine Whip your master gave you is a remarkable treasure. You must master its techniques thoroughly.\"","\"Yes, yes! Mother, rest assured. Yue’er will practice the whip techniques well!\" She nodded eagerly.","\"Mother, rest assured. We’ll keep an eye on our little sister and make sure she doesn’t get too carried away playing,\" Hao’er added.","\"Mother, I’ll work hard on my cultivation too,\" Muchen said.","\"Good, you’re all such good children—my precious treasures!\" She smiled, gathering all three into her arms and kissing each one. Seeing their delighted yet bashful expressions, she couldn’t help but laugh.","\"Alright, I must go now. If you want anything to eat, find Mi’er and she’ll cook for you. But remember—no sneaking off the Immortal Island.\" She instructed.","\"Yes, Mother.\" The three answered in unison. Watching her depart, they headed straight for the martial arts training grounds.","For Yuan Jing, this was unfamiliar territory. Blind, he didn’t even know the way out of the courtyard. So, after the celestial maid brought him to the guest quarters, he hadn’t stepped outside once all day.","Being blind, even if he went out, he wouldn’t see the beauty of the celestial realm. He might even cause trouble for the Phoenix Empress. Since that was the case, why not just stay within this courtyard?","Until evening fell.","\"Is this the place?\"","Mi’er peered out, surveying the courtyard. As dusk deepened, she saw no lamps or fires lit within—only pitch darkness. The man named Yuan Jing sat there.","\"Who’s there?\" Yuan Jing’s voice carried a hint of surprise as he turned toward the sound. Though he could see nothing, he at least faced the direction of the voice.","\"Oh, it’s me, Song Mi’er.\" Mi’er entered, carrying the evening meal. \"Why haven’t you lit any lamps here? It’s pitch black everywhere. I almost thought I’d wandered into the wrong guest quarters!\" She placed the evening meal on the table.","\"I’m blind. Lighting a lamp wouldn’t help me see,\" Yuan Jing said gently. He stood up, bowed toward the front, and added, \"Still, thank you for your kindness, young lady.\"","Mi’er, who had already started walking toward the guest rooms, glanced back. Seeing him bowing toward an empty space, she couldn’t help but smile warmly. \" No need for such formalities. I’m in charge of meals on this island—I brought you dinner. Sit down and eat! I’ve placed it right before you.\" With that, she headed toward the guest quarters, adding, \"There’s a night pearl in the room. I’ll remove the covering cloth for you, and it’ll brighten things up a bit.\""]},{"number":5057,"title":"Chapter 5057: Treatment","paragraphs":["Within the Immortal Island, many treasures like night pearls provided illumination, though they were usually covered with cloth to conceal their radiance when not in use. Upon entering the room, Mi’er removed the cover from the night pearl lamp. Instantly, its light flooded the entire chamber.","Stepping out of the room, Mi’er smiled. \"Young Master Yuan, if you need anything, just tell the celestial maids. Or you can send them to find me—I’m usually in the kitchen. If you’d like to explore, just ask a maid to guide you.\"","As she spoke, she approached the table and, seeing his blindness, asked, \"Can you manage your meal on your own? Should I call a maid to assist you?\"","\"I can manage,\" Yuan Jing replied softly.","\"Very well, I’ll leave you now! A maid will come in shortly to clear the table.\" With that, Mi’er turned and departed.","After she left, Yuan Jing ate his meal alone. He ate slowly and not much. Once the maid had cleared the dishes, he returned to his room to rest.","Over the next two days, though he could move about the Immortal Island, his blindness kept him indoors. He remained in his courtyard, practicing meditation and sitting quietly.","Two days later, Feng Jiu arrived at Yuan Jing’s courtyard. As soon as she entered, she saw him seated within.","Though Yuan Jing couldn’t hear, his hearing was exceptionally keen. He tilted his ear slightly, listening to the soft, measured footsteps approaching. Rising to his feet, he bowed in the direction of the sound: \"Phoenix Empress.\"","Feng Jiu glanced at him and said, \"I’ve processed the red-eyed spirit’s fish eyes into a medicinal liquid. I’ve brought it for you to try.\" With that, she stepped toward his room and added, \"Come inside.\"","Yuan Jing paused briefly before following her inside. Once in the room, he was instructed to lie down on the bed.","Watching Yuan Jing lie there, his hands nervously clutching the bedsheets, Feng Jiu chuckled softly. \"Relax. I won’t harm you.\"","Yuan Jing flashed a faint smile, his body gradually relaxing. He felt her examining his eyes and taking his pulse. After a moment, her fingers gently parted his eyelids, and a cool liquid dripped into his eyes. He felt a slight sting, but that sting was quickly soothed by the liquid’s coolness, gradually giving way to a deep sense of comfort.","\"How does it feel?\" Feng Jiu asked.","\"A slight sting at first, then coolness. Now my eyes feel very comfortable,\" Yuan Jing replied truthfully.","\"Good. Blink gently to help the solution seep into your eye sockets,\" Feng Jiu instructed, dripping two more drops into his other eye. Simultaneously, she channeled the Blue Lotus Qi through her palm, sending specks of azure light accompanied by pure spirit energy into his eyes.","\"Now it feels warm... and a bit itchy,\" Yuan Jing continued, describing the peculiar sensations in his eyes.","Feng Jiu remained silent, quietly channeling the Blue Lotus energy to complement the medicinal solution in his treatment. After about half an incense stick’s time, she withdrew her hand. By then, Yuan Jing had already fallen asleep, his breathing slow and peaceful.","Glancing at the sleeping figure, Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow. Without further comment, she stood and walked out.","With the elixir seeping in, combined with the spirit energy and the essence of the Blue Lotus, no wonder he’d drifted off in such comfort.","Stepping outside, Feng Jiu headed toward the main hall. Finding few children inside, she spotted Mi’er carrying pastries and asked, \"Where are the other three?\""]},{"number":5058,"title":"Chapter 5058: You’re Welcome","paragraphs":["\"Oh, the three of them went to the forest. They said they wanted to train and gain experience. But Fire Phoenix and Cloud Devouring went with them.\" Mi’er placed the pastries on the small table beside her and asked, \"Did Master need them for something? Shall I call them back?\"","\"Since they’re in the forest, let them wander around there for now!\" Feng Jiu said, picking up a pastry to eat while asking, \"Mi’er, have you improved your strength recently?\"","\"I have improved a bit. I can feel my combat power has grown significantly.\" Mi’er said with a smile, adding, \"I also asked Uncle Tie to forge another set of blades for me! It’ll just take a bit longer to complete.\"","\"Mhm.\" Feng Jiu nodded, sipping her tea. \"Keep an eye on Yuan Jing at the guest quarters. If he needs anything, make sure it’s provided.\"","\"Got it. I know.\"","Over the next few days, Feng Jiu treated Yuan Jing’s eyes almost daily, inquiring about his sensations during the process and any changes in his vision.","That day, as Feng Jiu once again treated Yuan Jing with the energy of the Blue Lotus, she continued to ask, \"How does it feel today?\"","\"My eyes feel warm, like a hot compress is pressing against them. It’s a bit itchy, but the stinging pain is gone,\" Yuan Jing replied.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu withdrew her hand and looked at him lying on the bed. \"Get up! Come outside and take a look.\"","Yuan Jing paused at his words but obeyed without hesitation. Following her into the courtyard, he stopped when he heard her footsteps halt ahead.","\"Open your eyes and tell me what you see,\" Feng Jiu instructed softly.","Yuan Jing froze, his closed eyelashes fluttering slightly. Throughout his treatment, he’d been instructed never to open his eyes. Meaning that since the very first day of therapy, he’d kept his eyes shut—even when walking around blindfolded. Hearing her tell him to open them now, he momentarily froze, unable to process the request.","\"Open your eyes. See if it’s still pitch black.\" Seeing him unresponsive, Feng Jiu prompted again.","At her words, Yuan Jing slowly opened his eyes, his gaze tinged with nervousness, caution, and unease. When he did open them, he still couldn’t make out the scenery before him. Yet, faintly, he could perceive blurred shapes and patches of white light.","His heart jolted, and his entire body trembled slightly. \"I... I think I see light...\"","Hearing his trembling voice, Feng Jiu waved her hand in front of him. \"And now? What do you see?\"","\"I don’t know what it is. Something fluttered past my face, partially obscuring the light.\" His voice faltered as he asked, his excitement unmasked, \"Phoenix Empress, does this mean my eyes are healing?\"","Feng Jiu withdrew her hand. \"That was my hand waving. Still, seeing light is a good sign.\" She handed him the medicinal solution. \"Since you can perceive light, you may administer the drops yourself from now on. Switch to three applications daily—morning, noon, and night. After each application, cover your eye with a cloth strip. I’ll return in three days to check on you.\"","\"Yes, thank you, Phoenix Empress.\" He responded, his gratitude mingled with unchecked joy and excitement.","\"You’re welcome. Helping you is only because of Mo Chen’s favor.\" Feng Jiu said, making no further stay. She turned and left the guest courtyard."]},{"number":5059,"title":"Chapter 5059: Farewell","paragraphs":["Another half-month passed.","That day, Yuan Jing felt only a wave of coolness in his eyes after the medicated drops were administered, he no longer felt the itching, dryness, and stinging pain .","He walked through his room, stepped outside, and only then slowly, cautiously opened his eyes. The blurred scenery before him gradually sharpened. The world that had always been pitch black now burst into vibrant colours.","His heart trembled as his gaze swept forward. He saw the greenery in the courtyard, the crimson blossoms in the corner, the verdant trees—that lush green was so beautiful. He even saw the leaves swaying as the breeze gently caressed them, occasionally a few drifting down, floating and swaying, landing softly in the courtyard...","\"I... I can see...\"","he murmured, his voice choked with emotion. His eyes welled up involuntarily, a faint mist gathering in their corners.","\"Is this the colour of the world?\" he murmured, dazed, taking steps forward. Step by step, he walked out of the courtyard, revealing even more beautiful scenery beyond.","The sky’s blue, the clouds’ white, the flowers’ myriad hues of purple and red, the trees—not just vibrant green, but also the yellow of withered leaves...","The rainbow’s seven colours in the distance, the clouds on the horizon—not just white, but also such beautiful red...","\"The colours of the world... so beautiful...\"","He murmured softly, a mix of emotion, admiration, and wonder. Like a newborn infant, he was filled with wonder and delight at everything.","In the sky, graceful cranes soared, while birds sang from the treetops. In the pond, lotus blossoms bloomed, lotus leaves floated on the water, and fish darted through the currents. All of this seemed so perfect, so beautiful, it was hard to tear one’s eyes away.","In the distance, a crimson figure approached at a leisurely pace. Her striking red gown made her visible from afar. As she drew nearer, her breathtakingly beautiful face gradually came into view.","He thought that all the beauty in the world couldn’t begin to describe the radiance she possessed.","Even if he had never seen her before, in this moment, the instant he laid eyes on her, he knew she was the Phoenix Empress, the Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu—the very Phoenix Empress who had been treating his eyes these past days.","He withdrew his gaze, daring not to look at her again, fearful of desecrating such a peerlessly noble being.","\"Yuan Jing greets the Phoenix Empress.\" \" As she approached, Yuan Jing bowed his head and presented a respectful salute.","\"Can you see now?\" Feng Jiu’s gaze settled upon him, resting on his eyes as he lifted his head.","\"Yes, when I opened my eyes today, I could see.\" He replied.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu nodded. \"Since you can see, you may return now.\"","Hearing this, Yuan Jing paused briefly before asking, \"How might Yuan Jing repay the Phoenix Empress?\" She had healed his eyes, yet never mentioned any reward—how should he show his gratitude?","Feng Jiu chuckled softly. \"No need for repayment! After all, I lack nothing here. If you truly wish to express thanks, direct it toward Mo Chen. Were it not for him, I would never have treated you.\"","Without waiting for his reply, she continued, \"Now that you’re healed, it would be inappropriate for me to keep you here. I’ll see you off. May we meet again when fate allows!\" As her voice faded, she swept her sleeve, and an invisible force carried Yuan Jing out of the Immortal Island."]},{"number":5060,"title":"Chapter 5060: Azure Emperor","paragraphs":["Before Yuan Jing could utter a word, a powerful aura enveloped him and swept him upward. In a flash, he was carried beyond the barrier of the Immortal Isle. As the force receded, his body plummeted downward.","Instantly, he gathered his spirit energy to stabilize his body. Hovering mid-air, he gazed back at the Immortal Isle and bowed with reverence and solemnity: \"Phoenix Empress, Yuan Jing, I am eternally indebted. Should you ever require Yuan Jing’s service, I am at your command.\"","After completing his bow, he cast one last lingering glance at the Immortal Isle before turning away.","Within the island, Feng Jiu smiled at Yuan Jing’s words, not taking them to heart. Instead, she sent a telepathic message to Mo Chen, informing him that Yuan Jing’s eyes had been healed and he had departed.","Afterward, she headed to her own residence. During this time, she had discovered a way to travel to the lower realm: by cultivating divine soul power, she could eventually tear open a passage in the void and return to the Lower Immortal Realm.","Due to the void barrier’s isolation, her teleportation jade couldn’t reveal any news from the Lower Immortal Realm, nor could it tell her how Mo Ze was faring. Having stabilized her position here in the Upper Immortal Realm, she now wished to return briefly to see if Mo Ze was about to awaken.","As for the remaining Great Emperors, they were now hiding like turtles with their heads tucked in, vanishing without a trace. Finding them would be difficult in the short term. Thus, she intended to use this time to check on Mo Ze’s condition.","After all this time, perhaps his immortal body had solidified sufficiently. If he needed her final push, she would give it to him, hastening his awakening and ascent to the Upper Immortal Realm. Then, with their combined strength, even if those three Great Emperors recovered and joined forces, they would stand no chance.","As for the three children, they had been training in the Beast Forest on the Immortal Island during this period. With the Fire Phoenix and others accompanying them, she had no need to worry about them.","Thus, upon returning to her residence, she gave a brief instruction before entering her spatial realm and plunging headlong into cultivation.","A month later, the Azure Emperor, who had been absent for some time, arrived outside Feng Jiu’s immortal island. Standing with his hands behind his back, he surveyed the mist-shrouded place. Extending his hand forward, a palpable surge of powerful energy materialized, followed immediately by the manifestation of a barrier.","The Azure Emperor’s eyes flickered slightly as he observed the scene before him. Withdrawing his hand, his deep voice, infused with spirit energy, pierced through the barrier and echoed toward the immortal island.","\"Feng Jiu.\"","At that moment, Feng Jiu was still cultivating her divine soul power within her spatial realm, utterly oblivious to his call.","It was Mi’er who caught the sound. Surprised, she flew over on her sword and demanded, \"Who is it? Who dares to address my master by name so boldly?\" Arriving at the gates of the Immortal Island, Mi’er frowned upon seeing the figure outside the barrier. Instinctively, she sensed danger emanating from him.","Could it be one of my Master’s enemies coming to seek revenge?","A thought flashed through Mi’er’s mind, and she instinctively took a step back. While her combat prowess could handle ordinary opponents, it was no match for such a dangerous individual.","\"I am the Azure Emperor.\" The Azure Emperor cast a cold glance toward the mist. With his formidable divine sense, he could detect the presence of someone within the clouds despite their obstruction.","\"The Azure Emperor?\" Mi’er froze, exclaiming in surprise, \"The Azure Emperor? Wait a moment, I’ll fetch someone to verify this!\" With that, she swiftly mounted her sword and departed.","After all, she didn’t recognize the Azure Emperor! She couldn’t just let anyone in, especially while her master was in seclusion. Fortunately, Hao’er and the others had only returned last night and were still asleep! Calling them over to confirm would be perfect."]},{"number":5061,"title":"Chapter 5061: No Doubt","paragraphs":["Outside the barrier of the Immortal Island, the Azure Emperor’s expression darkened upon hearing the words from within. He stood there with his hands behind his back, waiting.","Hao’er and Muchen had slept in a bit later than usual today, but by now they were already washed and dressed. They planned to do some calisthenics before exploring the surroundings. As they prepared to practice their skills in the courtyard, Mi’er came rushing in.","\"Oh? You two awake? Perfect timing! Quick, come with me.\" Mi’er hurried forward, speaking rapidly.","The two exchanged glances and asked, \"What’s going on?\"","\"A man arrived outside claiming to be the Azure Emperor. Our Master is currently in seclusion, and I’ve never seen the Azure Emperor either. So I came to ask you to go identify if that person is truly the Azure Emperor, lest we let our Master’s enemy in.\"","Hearing this, Hao’er and Muchen both showed a trace of astonishment on their faces. They spoke in unison, \" You left our master waiting outside the Immortal Island?\"","\"I just asked him to wait a moment!\" Seeing their stunned expressions, Mi’er explained, \"Come on, let’s go! Go see if it’s your master.\"","Hao’er suppressed his astonishment, a smile breaking free on his face. \"I don’t need to see him to know it’s our master.\" With that, he led the way outside.","Their master was the Azure Emperor! A powerhouse so revered that countless sought to curry favor with him—yet only Mi’er dared leave him waiting outside the Immortal Island.","Seeing his Big Brother depart first, Muchen turned to Mi’er: \"Yeah, I’m sure it’s our master too. With his reputation, no one would dare impersonate him.\"","No sooner had the words left his mouth than he too hurried outside.","Hearing this, Mi’er froze for a moment before calling out toward the room, \"Yue’er, your master is here! Get up quickly!\" With that, she swiftly followed the two men outside.","Half-asleep, Yue’er heard the mention of her master arriving and immediately leaped out of bed.","Outside, Hao’er and Muchen arrived at the barrier surrounding the Immortal Island. Spotting the familiar figure beyond, they called out immediately: \"Master!\"","Mi’er, who had followed them, heard their words and hurried forward to open the barrier with her token. She bowed awkwardly to the Azure Emperor: \"Song Mi’er greets the Azure Emperor. Azure Emperor, please enter, enter.\"","The Azure Emperor glanced at her before turning his gaze to the two beside her and asking, \"Where is Yun Qi?\"","\"Master, she just got up and is still in the courtyard,\" Hao’er replied.","\"Azure Emperor, please come into the hall for tea first,\" Mi’er gestured invitingly.","The Azure Emperor advanced, with Hao’er and Muchen following close behind. Upon reaching the main hall, Mi’er swiftly served him tea and pastries. Noting Hao’er and Muchen’s presence, she withdrew without lingering.","\"Master, have you finished your business? Are we returning to Yunxiao Mountain?\" Hao’er inquired. His first thought was that their master had finished his business and was taking them back. Once they returned, they likely wouldn’t see Mother again for quite some time.","After sipping his tea, the Azure Emperor glanced at the two of them and asked, \"Don’t you want to go back?\"","\"Not at all.\"","\"Not at all.\"","They answered in unison.","Seeing this, the Azure Emperor said no more, only adding, \"This journey was partly to attend to personal matters, but I also sought out weapons for you both. I’ve come to take you there to retrieve them personally.\"","Noticing his disciples’ slight surprise, he continued, \"What about your Mother? After informing her, you shall depart with me.\""]},{"number":5062,"title":"Chapter 5062: Guilty Conscience","paragraphs":["Hao’er and Muchen exchanged a glance before saying, \"Master, our mother is in seclusion.\"","\"Seclusion?\" The Azure Emperor paused slightly. \"With her current strength, why would she need seclusion to deal with anyone? Or is she planning another earth-shattering scheme?\"","Muchen looked at him, his small face wearing a mature expression. \"Master should know that our father is still in the Lower Immortal Realm. And it’s not just our father—many of our relatives are there too. I heard Mother say she wants to break through the void barrier of the Upper Immortal Realm, so the two realms can connect.\"","\"Hmph...\"","Azure Emperor chuckled softly upon hearing this. \"That sounds like something your Mother would attempt. But this matter is far from simple.\"","Setting down his teacup, he continued, \"The Upper Immortal Realm differs from other parts of the Lower Immortal Realm. What separates them isn’t merely a difference in spatial dimensions, but also the Nine Layers of Heavenly Dao. Achieving mutual access between these two realms is no easy feat.\"","\"Master!\"","A sweet, soft voice called out. At the sound, a gentle light softened the Azure Emperor’s eyes. He glanced toward the hall entrance, where the little girl dashed in like the wind and threw herself into his arms.","\"Master, Master! Yun Qi missed you so much!\"","Yue’er knew she had run away without permission. Now that her master had come looking for her, her first instinct was to find a way to win his favor. She threw herself into his embrace, rubbing her little head against him before tilting her face up, revealing a sweet, endearing smile.","Azure Emperor’s face remained impassive, his expression unreadable. His deep, calm eyes fixed on the little girl tilting her head up with that sweet smile. Hearing her words, he asked in a deep voice, \"You missed your master?\"","\"Mm hmm~\" Yue’er nodded eagerly.","\"But how does your master recall you disobeying me and sneaking out of Yunxiao Mountain?\"","His cool voice carried a low, unreadable tone, devoid of emotion. Not even a hint of expression or warmth graced his face. Yue’er’s heart skipped a beat. Feeling guilty and uneasy, she lowered her head, her small hands tugging at the hem of his robe, unsure what to say.","Seeing her slightly anxious expression, the Azure Emperor sighed inwardly and softened his tone. \"Do you think you’ll dare disobey your master again? Sneak out of the mountain?\"","Hearing this, she quickly lifted her head. \"I won’t, I won’t! Master, I promise I’ll be good and listen to you from now on. If you tell me not to leave the mountain, I won’t. Really, I swear.\"","\"Remember what you said today,\" the Azure Emperor said, watching her.","\"Mmm...\"","She nodded in agreement. Seeing his expression soften slightly, she beamed and asked, \"Master, why are you here?\" Didn’t you go to handle some business? Is it finished? Are you here to take us back to the mountain? Master, my Mother’s place is so beautiful. Would you like to stay here for a few days? Sister Mi’er’s cooking is so delicious, Master...\"","\"Enough.\" Azure Emperor cut her off. \"I know you wish to stay by your Mother’s side, but do not forget you are still my disciples.\"","He added, \"You already have the Divine Whip as your weapon. Yun Chen and Yun Yuan still lack suitable weapons, so I plan to take them to find swords that suit them.\"","\"Then can I come too?\" Yue’er asked, blinking her eyes.","Azure Emperor looked at her and said, \"Yes. Once we obtain the swords, we’ll return directly to Yunxiao Mountain.\""]},{"number":5063,"title":"Chapter 5063: I Know","paragraphs":["\"Is the Azure Emperor taking them away?\" Feng Jiu’s voice drifted over.","\"Mother!\"","Hao’er and the others called out, rising to their feet as she entered. Mu Chen asked, \"But Mother, weren’t you in seclusion?\" His gaze then fell upon Mi’er standing by the palace doors, whispering to him that she had come to fetch her.","Feng Jiu smiled as she approached. \"I instructed Mi’er to summon me if anything arose. Since your master has arrived, even if Mother were in seclusion, she must come out to receive him.\"","She walked over and sat down, looking at the Azure Emperor. \"Since you’ve come, Azure Emperor, why not stay for a few days?\"","Azure Emperor looked at her and said, \"I intend to take them to find suitable weapons. After that, we’ll return directly to Yunxiao Mountain, so Yun Qi will be coming with us as well.\"","His voice paused briefly before he added, \"No need for a stay. We’ll rest today and depart tomorrow.\" These words were meant for Feng Jiu, but also for the three children.","Hearing his words, Feng Jiu paused slightly. She glanced at him, then turned her gaze to Hao’er and Muchen. In truth, they already possessed weapons—both carried daggers and swords sharp enough to slice through iron like mud. Precisely because the swords they currently wielded were exceptional, she hadn’t considered replacing them.","Thus, when she heard Azure Emperor’s words, she was caught off guard. If Azure Emperor offered to seek weapons for them, the weapons he obtained would undoubtedly surpass their current ones.","She didn’t ask what kind of weapons he intended to seek. Instead, she replied, \"In that case, we’ll leave it to Azure Emperor’s kindness.\"","After exchanging a few more casual words in the hall, Feng Jiu personally escorted the Azure Emperor to the guest quarters to rest. She instructed the three children to accompany him and ordered Mi’er to prepare dishes for their guest...","The next morning, at the barrier guarding the exit of the Immortal Island, the three children, neatly dressed, stood beside the Azure Emperor, gazing at their Mother with lingering reluctance.","\"Listen carefully to your master’s teachings and train diligently. Mother will visit you when the opportunity arises,\" Feng Jiu told the three.","\"Yes, Mother, rest assured. We’ll obey our master,\" they replied, standing still beside their teacher. They dared not rush into their mother’s embrace, fearing they might cling tightly and never want to leave.","\"Qingdi, I entrust these three to your care,\" Feng Jiu said, bowing respectfully.","\"Mhm,\" Qingdi replied, glancing at the children. \"At this age, their minds are most unstable. It’s best to see them less often unless necessary.\"","Feng Jiu understood his meaning. She looked at the children, nodded, and smiled at them gently.","\"Mother, we’ll practice diligently and strive to grow stronger,\" Muchen declared earnestly, his voice solemn as if making a solemn promise.","\"Yes, Mother knows. You’re all good children.\" Though her heart ached with reluctance, she understood that staying with the Azure Emperor was the best choice for them.","\"Mother, Yue’er will miss you. But from now on, Yue’er won’t sneak out to find you anymore. Rest assured, Mother, Yue’er will be very good from now on and won’t cause Master or Mother any worry.\" The little girl added.","\"Mhm.\" Feng Jiu nodded, feeling deeply comforted.","\"Feng Jiu.\"","The Azure Emperor suddenly spoke, looking at her. \"The heavens and earth have their own rules. Above the Nine Heavens lies the Upper Immortal Realm, distinct from the other realms of the Lower Immortal Realm. For countless millennia, no one has ever attempted to merge or connect them. What you wish to do is no easy task. In fact, it may never be accomplished.\""]},{"number":5064,"title":"Chapter 5064: Dragon Abyss Sword","paragraphs":["His voice paused for a moment before he continued, \"Some things—many things—are nothing but obsessions.\"","Hearing this, Feng Jiu smiled faintly. \"I know. I understand exactly what I’m doing.\"","Seeing this, the Azure Emperor said no more. After bidding her farewell, he departed with the three children.","Watching their figures vanish into the depths of the clouds on the horizon, Feng Jiu finally withdrew her gaze and turned back.","\"Master, will they return?\" Mi’er approached as she came back and asked.","\"This is their home. Of course they’ll return someday. But who knows how many years that ’someday’ might be?\" She smiled faintly, shook her head, and said no more. Turning, she headed back to her quarters, preparing to retreat into seclusion once more.","Half a Year Later","On an island, the Azure Emperor stood with his hands behind his back, watching the sun rise over the eastern sea. \"Are you ready?\" he asked.","Beside him stood Muchen, clad in a form-fitting black robe. Over the past six months, he had grown nearly half a head taller. Though still young, he stood perfectly straight, his small face taut, his gaze radiating unwavering determination and a sense of inevitable victory.","\"I am ready!\"","He declared, his voice solemn and clear.","Not far behind them, Hao’er and Yue’er stood watching, keeping their distance.","The Azure Emperor listened, then turned his head slightly to look at Muchen. \"How many times have you descended into the sea? And how many times have you grasped the sword?\"","\"Master, this is my ninety-ninth time entering the sea! I’ve grasped the sword eleven times, yet failed to draw it each time. But this time, I will pull it out!\" Muchen’s voice carried unwavering resolve as his gaze fixed on the vast ocean ahead. His mind held but one thought: this time, he would draw the ancient divine sword, Dragon Abyss!","Half a year ago, his master had led them away from the Immortal Island to this place. He had told Muchen that a sword was embedded within these seas—an ancient divine blade named Dragon Abyss—and commanded him to pull it out.","Over these six months, he had dived into the sea ninety-nine times. Of those ninety-nine attempts, only eleven had allowed him to grasp the sword. The rest ended either in forced ascent due to unbearable pressure upon descending, or in failure to locate the sword’s position.","And on those eleven occasions when he found the sword’s location and grasped it, he still couldn’t pull it free.","But this time was different. This time, he believed he could do it!","\"This is your final attempt. If you fail to draw the sword now, you lose your chance forever.\" The Azure Emperor gazed out at the vast sea ahead and declared, \"Go!\"","\"Yes!\" Muchen pressed his lips together, gathered his breath, and soared into the air toward the ocean surface. After gliding a considerable distance, he took a deep breath and plunged headfirst into the sea.","Watching him enter the sea, Yue’er, standing nearby, asked with concern, \"Senior Brother, can Second Senior Brother pull out that sword?\"","\"He absolutely can!\" His gaze fixed on the sea ahead, his heart filled with conviction that Muchen would pull out that sword!","Hearing his words, Yue’er said nothing, only waiting quietly, watching...","Further away, some cultivators spotted the boy heading back into the sea and chuckled. \"Look, that kid’s going into the water again. How many times has this happened? What do you think he’s after?\"","\"Maybe there’s some treasure in the sea!\"","\"Ha ha ha! As if! If there was anything, it would’ve been scooped up long ago.\""]},{"number":5065,"title":"Chapter 5065: Famous Swords Choose Their Masters","paragraphs":["The cultivators over there were chatting freely, unaware of the few people nearby, so they spoke without restraint.","This stretch of sea bordered the Fierce Beast Forest. Aside from cultivators venturing into the forest to hunt beasts, it also served as a place for many cultivators to rest and seek treasures.","After all, the ocean held many treasures unknown to others, though it also concealed countless unknown dangers.","Muchen, submerged in the deep sea, was enveloped in a aura of spirit energy. Upon reaching the ocean floor, the ancient Sacred Beast’s aura emanating from him naturally released. Here, especially in the central depths, numerous sea beasts prowled below, hunting for prey. To avoid conflict, once he reached these depths, he unleashed the ancient aura, compelling those sea beasts to keep their distance.","After an unknown period, he reached a pitch-black area where a sword was embedded in a massive rock. Without careful observation, its presence would have gone entirely unnoticed.","He stepped forward, grasped the hilt, and channeled spirit energy into his palm, attempting to draw it. Yet the sword remained utterly immovable. Having lingered too long beneath the waves, his ears ached, and the crushing pressure of the deep sea made his entire being feel unwell.","He tried again and again to pull the sword free, but each attempt proved futile.","The pain in his eardrums, the pain in his eyes, the excruciating agony in his mind that felt like a knife gouging, and the lack of air all told him he had to go up.","But he refused to give up just yet, for he knew this was his last chance. If he couldn’t pull this sword out now, he would never have another opportunity!","His hand clenched the hilt tightly, exerting force again and again. Each attempt only brought him greater agony, his vision gradually blurring...","By the seaside, Hao’er and Yue’er stood beside Azure Emperor, watching the calm sea surface show no signs of disturbance. Yue’er couldn’t help but ask, \"Master, will Second Senior Brother be able to pull the sword out? He’s been down there so long, might he not be able to endure it?\"","\"Master, Yun Yuan has been down longer than any of his previous attempts. Such prolonged exposure... I fear he may not endure the depths.\" Hao’er’s voice trembled with genuine worry. Without the Water-Repellent Pearl, even a cultivator couldn’t withstand the depths for long.","Azure Emperor gazed at the sea and spoke, \"Do you truly believe he went down to draw the sword?\"","The two froze, then asked, \"Then isn’t that the case?\"","The Azure Emperor shook his head, hands clasped behind his back. \"This ancient Dragon Abyss Sword has always chosen its master—never the other way around. You must understand, renowned swords select their owners. I sent him down to test again and again merely to see if this ancient Dragon Abyss Sword would ultimately choose him as its master.\"","If it could be drawn and taken away directly, why would he have personally gone to Feng Jiu to bring them here? Why not just draw it and return to present it to him?","Hearing this, the two were taken aback. They knew that renowned swords would choose their masters, but they had assumed their master had sent them to seek the sword because it could be drawn. Yet, it turned out to be like this...","\"Master, does that mean that Second Senior Brother has no hope? He’s gone down so many times already. Could it be that the sword doesn’t approve of him?\" At this, Yue’er’s brow furrowed, her small face flushing with indignation."]},{"number":5066,"title":"Chapter 5066: The Legendary Sword Emerges","paragraphs":["In her eyes, the sword worn by her brother—such an exceptional man—should be the ancient divine blade her master spoke of. Anything less would be unworthy of him. But if this sword did not choose her brother, then when she grew up, she would pull it from its scabbard and cast it into the furnace to be reforged!","Meanwhile, deep beneath the ocean’s surface, a faint glow began to emanate from the pitch-black seabed. The light radiated from the very Dragon Abyss Sword.","By now, Muchen had fainted from exhaustion, yet his hand still clutched the Dragon Abyss Sword tightly as his entire body leaned against it.","Unseen by him, the Dragon Abyss Sword embedded in the boulder suddenly flew free. The blade, once covered in moss and rust, was now cleansed by the radiant light emanating from its surface, becoming razor-sharp.","The sword shot out, carrying the unconscious Hao’er out of the depths. In that instant, the entire sea surface trembled violently. Surging waves crashed upward, and the ground itself quaked faintly, making it impossible for anyone to stand steady.","\"What’s happening? Could it be an earth dragon stirring?\"","Cultivators cried out in alarm, hastily supporting those beside them as they retreated. Others, thrown off balance by the violent tremors, stumbled and fell onto the sandy shore. Just then, someone gasped, pointing toward the sea surface.","\"Ah! Look! What is that?!\"","Above the sea, a fiery cloud-like glow coalesced in the sky. The cloud spread across the water’s surface, casting faint rays of light onto the sea.","Above the churning, roaring waves, a whirlpool suddenly erupted from the sea. A sharp sword, radiating sword qi, emerged from the water, carrying a drenched little boy. With a whoosh, they shot toward the sandy shore.","\"It’s Senior Brother! And that sword!\" Yue’er cheered with delight, leaping to her feet.","Hao’er felt a wave of relief wash over him upon seeing the boy and the sword emerge, but his heart sank again moments later. \"He seems to have fainted.\"","The Azure Emperor watched silently, glancing only briefly at the perfect sunset hues before fixing his gaze on the sword and Muchen. He watched as the ancient divine blade carried the boy to the shore, gently setting him down before planting itself beside him.","In that moment, bathed in sunlight, all present witnessed the blade shimmering with a layer of flowing light. Its surface resembled a night sky, profound and mysterious, yet also like a coiled dragon, radiating a powerful, piercing aura and an intimidating brilliance.","\"A celestial omen! An ancient divine weapon has appeared! Whoa! This... this is the ancient Dragon Abyss Divine Sword!\"","A sharp-eyed cultivator recognized it, gasping sharply as his eyes widened in disbelief, staring fixedly at the treasure sword lying beside the child.","\"The ancient Dragon Abyss Divine Sword? Could you be mistaken? That sword vanished after its last master perished. Rumor has it the ancient Dragon Abyss Sword was sealed away—it could never reappear!\"","\"No mistake! No mistake! I recognize it! The ancient sword compendium depicts this very Dragon Abyss Sword! I recognize it! No mistake!\" the cultivator declared loudly, seemingly displeased at being contradicted.","Regardless of whether this was truly the ancient divine sword Dragon Abyss, the celestial phenomenon, coupled with the sword emerging from the sea carrying that child, made it abundantly clear to them—this was undoubtedly a treasure!","Instantly, the thoughts of the crowd began to stir."]},{"number":5067,"title":"Chapter 5067: Anticipation","paragraphs":["It had been several months since this master and his disciples arrived at the seaside. The master, accompanied by three children, remained an enigma—no one knew their sect or lineage. Day after day, they sent the young boy into the sea, and though others observed this, none understood their purpose.","Some curious souls had secretly followed him into the water, yet found nothing of note. Little did they expect to witness an ancient divine sword emerge from the depths today.","Just as someone was about to approach, the boy’s master and his companions appeared.","\"Second Senior Brother!\"","Yue’er hurried forward. Seeing him soaking wet and unconscious, she quickly checked him, pressing his abdomen. Soon, he coughed up water, cleared his throat, and slowly opened his eyes.","Hao’er approached, relieved to see him awake. He channeled spirit energy to dry the boy’s soaked clothes while asking, \"How are you? Feeling better?\"","Muchen nodded, glancing at his master approaching. Shame made him lower his head. \"Master, I failed. I couldn’t pull the sword.\"","He had tried, again and again, but the sword simply wouldn’t budge. In the end, he had even fainted, forcing his master to dive in and rescue him.","Hmm. At that moment, he still didn’t know that the ancient divine sword had carried him up. He thought he had fainted in the sea and that his master had dived down to save him.","Hearing this, the Azure Emperor’s lips curved slightly, revealing an almost imperceptible smile.","\"Second Brother, look at this,\" Yue’er said with a smile, gesturing toward the sword stuck in the ground nearby.","\"This sword brought you out of the sea,\" Hao’er added, a hint of amusement in his own smile.","Muchen froze, glancing over. When his gaze landed on the Dragon Abyss Sword, he stared blankly, a flicker of shock crossing his face. \"I... I clearly remember not pulling it out.\"","\"The ancient divine sword Dragon Abyss—do you truly believe it can be drawn at will? It is the sword that chooses its master, never the other way around.\" The Azure Emperor’s deep, indifferent voice echoed. He gazed at the Dragon Abyss Sword, stepped forward, and drew it from its sheath. A thread of energy coalesced from his fingertips, sweeping across the blade’s surface. He then handed it to Muchen, saying, \"From this moment onward, this sword belongs to you.\"","\"Thank you, Master!\" Muchen’s heart surged with emotion. He stood up, both hands clasping the Dragon Abyss Sword.","\"Second Senior Brother, hurry and perform the blood ritual to bind it!\" Yue’er said with a beaming smile, her heart brimming with joy. Her brother had found such a splendid weapon!","Thus, under the envious gazes of the surrounding cultivators, Muchen performed the blood ritual to bind the sword. After the binding, he felt an indescribable connection deepen between himself and the Dragon Abyss Sword in his grasp.","\"Master, now that Second Brother has such a splendid sword, what about Big Brother?\" Yue’er asked with a bright smile. Her brother possessed the ancient divine sword Dragon Abyss, while hers was the Divine Whip. Their master had found them both top-tier treasures. At this moment, she couldn’t help but anticipate what weapon their Big Brother would receive.","\"His sword, naturally, is no ordinary object,\" Azure Emperor said, folding his arms as he gazed into the distance. Then, turning to Hao’er, he added, \"Come. I shall take you to retrieve it.\"","\"Yes!\" Hao’er responded, a smile lighting up her face as anticipation welled within her heart.","However, just as the master and disciples prepared to depart, the surrounding cultivators closed in, refusing to make way."]},{"number":5068,"title":"Chapter 5068: Unrecognized","paragraphs":["Witnessing this scene, the Azure Emperor couldn’t help but snort derisively. \"You dare scheme against the Dragon Abyss Sword?\" How many years had it been? And now someone actually dared to block his path? It seemed he truly hadn’t ventured out often enough.","\"Heh heh, might I inquire which sect or lineage you hail from?\" A middle-aged cultivator spoke with a smile, offering a perfunctory bow. Seeing no response, he continued, \" Truthfully, we merely wish to borrow the ancient divine sword Dragon Abyss for a look. After all, it is an ancient divine sword, and I am genuinely curious.","\"You think you’re worthy?\" Azure Emperor’s voice was cool and detached. His deep, serene gaze swept over them, showing neither joy nor anger, yet it inexplicably sent a chill through their hearts.","\"Exactly! As if you’re worthy?\" Yue’er sneered, sticking out her tongue at them. \"The Dragon Abyss Sword belongs to my Senior Brother. Why should we show it to you?\"","Hmph! Shameless! They clearly want to steal the sword, yet claim they only wish to borrow it for a look. Utterly shameless!","\"Heh. Sir, with three children in tow, I’d wager that the Dragon Abyss Sword wouldn’t stay in your disciples’ hands for long. It might even bring them mortal peril. Wouldn’t it be better to entrust it to us instead?\"","The middle-aged cultivator spoke again, implying that even if he possessed formidable cultivation alone, he was still burdened with three children! If a fight broke out, they wouldn’t stand a chance. Rather than facing certain death, why not surrender it willingly?","Hearing this, the Azure Emperor’s lips curved slightly, revealing a faint, indifferent smile. Yet, his calm, profound gaze held not a trace of amusement. His voice carried a hint of casualness and coldness as he spoke, slow and measured.","\"You look down on this Emperor’s three disciples? Very well. Since you seek your own demise, why not grant you a swift end?\"","As the words fell, he turned to his three disciples beside him and commanded, \"Get rid of them.\"","\"Yes!\" The three answered in unison.","At this moment, the cultivators surrounding them, intent on seizing their possessions, were clearly no saints. In fact, to claim the Dragon Abyss Sword, they would have to kill Muchen first, severing the spiritual connection binding the sword to him. Thus, eliminating these attackers weighed not a bit on the disciples’ consciences.","They had always adhered to the principle of \"no provocation, no retaliation\"—a lesson instilled by both their Mother and their master. If someone dared to bully them at their doorstep, they would strike back fiercely!","When the cultivators heard that three children were to deal with them, they all froze for a moment. Then, in unison, they burst into loud laughter: \"Hahahaha! Did I hear that right?\" Three children to send us on our way? What kind of naive fool from some remote mountain peak came up with this? Three children want to fight and kill us? What a laughable joke!\"","Hearing them insult her master, Yue’er stepped forward. Her small face wore a sweet smile, but her eyes glowed with murderous intent: \"Insult my master? Do you think you can insult my master?\"","No sooner had the words left her mouth than her tiny form shot forward, targeting the cultivator who had laughed and called her master a fool. She didn’t use her whip; instead, she gripped a dagger in her hand, unleashing a deadly, ruthless strike from the very first move.","Whoosh!","\"Watch out!\"","The sudden surge of lethal intent, the piercing aura, and the ghostly-fast figure instantly put the cultivators on high alert. One cultivator behind instinctively yanked the one in front, barely pulling him out of the way of the throat-slitting strike."]},{"number":5069,"title":"Chapter 5069: That’s The Azure Emperor","paragraphs":["The cultivator who had been pulled back saw the sharp blade flash past his throat. The fierce killing intent made his face go pale, and a wave of dread washed over him.","Had he not dodged just now, he would likely have met his end right then and there!","He instantly shed his arrogance and carelessness, his entire being becoming alert. Just then, he saw the little girl lunge forward again, her dagger striking relentlessly at his vital points.","Hao’er and Muchen also moved in that instant. There were about a dozen cultivators closing in, and with their strength, dealing with them should pose no problem.","Muchen swung his Dragon Abyss Sword, unleashing a burst of sharp sword qi from its blade. The two approaching cultivators instinctively stumbled back under the onslaught.","Azure Emperor stood there, arms behind his back, observing without intervening. He watched the three of them join forces against the dozen or so opponents, studying their skills and combat prowess. He silently nodded in approval.","Talent truly was paramount. All three possessed extraordinary innate gifts, allowing them to cultivate faster than ordinary cultivators with no shortage of comprehension. Such combat strength at such a young age meant they would undoubtedly excel as they matured.","He stood there, his gaze seemingly fixed on their battle, yet his thoughts drifted elsewhere. Only when a figure roared and swung a sword at him did he snap back to attention.","\"Die!\"","Perhaps it was the vivid crimson blood of the corpses on the ground stinging his eyes, or perhaps it was witnessing the three children kill without so much as a flicker of an eyelid. In that moment, in a flash of madness, the cultivator swung his sword at the man standing motionless, hands behind his back.","\"Dare to attack my master? You seek death!\"","Yue’er spun around, her anger flaring at the sight of the cultivator striking toward their master. Though she knew he couldn’t harm their master, the act itself enraged her.","Her dagger flipped to her other hand as a whip shot out with a hiss. It coiled around the descending sword, yanking it back and flinging it far away. Simultaneously, the whip snapped back, whipping toward the man with a sharp crack.","\"You dared attack my master! Hmph!\"","The youthful voice carried anger, accompanied by the whoosh of the whip cutting through the air and the sharp crack as it struck the cultivator.","Further away, those merely observing the scene watched the events unfold, each feeling a chill rise from their feet, straight to their hearts.","Though they too coveted that ancient divine sword, they knew all too well that the man with the three children was no ordinary person. Thus, when the other cultivators closed in, they held back, merely wanting to see if those cultivators could wrest the Dragon Abyss Sword from the group.","Unexpectedly, the man didn’t even need to act. His three disciples alone utterly crushed the dozen or so cultivators.","The blood on the ground and the wide-eyed terror in the cultivators’ eyes as they died spoke volumes of their final moments of fear and regret. Simultaneously, it delivered a profound shock and awe to the onlookers.","\"Whoa!\"","Suddenly, one cultivator sucked in a sharp breath, eyes wide as he stared at the whip the little girl had swung. He cried out in disbelief, \"That’s the Ancient Divine Whip! That... that’s the Azure Emperor!\"","As the cry escaped his lips, the cultivator felt his legs go weak, and he collapsed, slumping to the ground."]},{"number":5070,"title":"Chapter 5070: News Spread","paragraphs":["Only when the last cultivator fell to the ground, eyes wide with terror, did the surrounding area finally grow quiet. No one spoke; all that could be heard was the sound of waves crashing.","The three seasoned veterans swiftly cleared the battlefield, collecting all the spoils before returning to their master.","The Azure Emperor cast a glance at the corpses on the ground and said to the three beside him, \"Let’s go!\" With that, he led them away.","Watching them vanish into streaks of light, the remaining cultivators finally relaxed their tightly clenched hearts. Cold sweat poured down their backs as a wave of dread washed over them.","The Azure Emperor... That was the Azure Emperor...","The Azure Emperor departed with his three disciples. From that day onward, rumors began to spread: celestial omens appeared, the ancient divine sword Dragon Abyss emerged to recognize its master—the Azure Emperor’s second disciple, Yun Yuan...","A month later, another rumor spread: the ancient divine sword, the Crimson Sky Sword, had been obtained by the Azure Emperor’s eldest disciple, Yun Chen. Instantly, sects, noble families, and factions across the Upper Immortal Realm were thrown into an uproar.","No one could have imagined that the long-reclusive Azure Emperor, upon emerging from Yunxiao Mountain, would first secure the Divine Whip for his youngest disciple as a protective weapon. Immediately after, he procured the ancient divine swords Crimson Sky and Dragon Abyss for his eldest and second disciples respectively. Such grand gestures left all who heard them utterly astonished.","It was common knowledge that ancient divine swords were not easily obtained. Moreover, the whereabouts of these two swords had long been unknown. Yet, unexpectedly, the Azure Emperor knew precisely where they lay.","Amidst the collective astonishment, many began discreetly investigating the backgrounds of the Azure Emperor’s three disciples. For it was widely understood that those chosen by such ancient divine blades were destined for extraordinary achievements. Thus, they sought to uncover the disciples’ origins early, hoping to cultivate ties with their families.","On the Immortal Island, Feng Jiu, emerging from seclusion, also heard the news—first relayed by Tie Song and Mi’er. Though one spent most days forging weapons in the rear mountains and the other often stayed in the kitchen perfecting new dishes, both remained remarkably well-informed about the outside world.","Feng Jiu ate her meal in the courtyard while listening to Mi’er’s chatter.","\"Word’s spread far and wide now—the Azure Emperor’s top disciple and second disciple both received ancient divine swords. Uncle Tie told me they’re truly the finest treasures imaginable.\"","Feng Jiu finished her bowl of soup, set it down, and wiped her lips. \"The Azure Emperor treats them exceptionally well, securing such rare swords for them.\"","Seeing she was full, Mi’er approached to clear the table, asking, \"Master, will you still be in seclusion?\"","Feng Jiu smiled, rising to her feet. \"No, I have matters to attend to. While I’m away, please take extra care of things here.\"","\"Understood,\" Mi’er replied without inquiring further. After tidying up, she prepared to withdraw.","Over the past year, her cultivation had steadily advanced, and she sensed a breakthrough approaching. Once her master departed, she could likely enter seclusion to advance her cultivation.","Moreover, with the Master off the island, no one else would come here. Even if someone did, she could simply ask them to return later. This period was thus the perfect time for her advancement.","\"This medicinal pill is for you.\" Feng Jiu handed over a pill. Seeing her staring at it in slight surprise, she smiled and added, \"Aren’t you preparing for advancement? Taking this medicinal pill then will be beneficial for you.\""]},{"number":5071,"title":"Chapter 5071: Three Years","paragraphs":["\"Thank you, Master!\" Mi’er snapped out of her daze, smiling happily as she quickly took it and tucked it away.","\"Inform Tie Song and Yueniang,\" Feng Jiu instructed. \"Should they require any alchemical materials, have them send word for delivery or procure them themselves.\"","\"Understood. I’ll relay the message,\" Mi’er nodded in agreement. She didn’t ask how long her master would be gone or when she’d return. Mi’er trusted her master would come back once the matter was settled. If things went as usual, it would likely only be a few months.","That day, Feng Jiu arrived at the forest within the Immortal Island. Here, she had established a teleportation array—an ancient formation. Complex patterns were woven by her spirit energy and Innate Heavenly Flame. As the array took shape and her spirit energy flowed along the patterns, flames erupted with a roar, igniting fiercely. A powerful radiance burst forth in that instant.","She stepped into the array, crossed her legs, and sat down. Spirit energy surged within her, coalescing in her palms. At that instant, her soul power unleashed, locking onto the void before her. As she attempted to tear open the void with her soul force, a mouthful of blood surged up from her throat.","\"Pfft!\"","A sudden spurt of blood erupted from her mouth. As the blood spilled forth, the luminous patterns of the formation beneath her gradually dimmed. The flames flickered and died, and the pervasive aura of spirit energy dissipated in that instant.","A sharp pain pierced her chest. She exhaled softly, easing the agony, then raised her hand to wipe the blood from her lips. Flipping her palm, a medicinal pill appeared in her hand, which she promptly tossed into her mouth and swallowed.","The Blue Lotus energy within her body began to circulate slowly, repairing the damage inflicted by the backlash. After a long while, she exhaled softly and murmured, \"No wonder the Azure Emperor used someone else’s body when he went to the Lower Immortal Realm. It really is this difficult.\"","From preparation to now, she had spent nearly a year, yet she never imagined that merely attempting to open the void would result in such severe backlash from the powerful forces of heaven and earth.","\"Could it be that those who ascend truly cannot return to the Lower Immortal Realm? No, impossible! That ancient text clearly states: all things are possible!\" With that, she closed her eyes to meditate. She must have made a mistake somewhere. She believed there had to be a way—she just needed to find it!","What she hadn’t anticipated was that her calculations and experiments here would consume her entirely. Once she began, three years slipped by in an instant...","Time flows swiftly in the mountains.","For cultivators, three years passed in the blink of an eye. Especially for someone like Feng Jiu, who was almost possessed by her research and experiments, she lost all sense of time, day or night.","Not only did outsiders have no idea she’d been stuck in the forest for three whole years, but even those on the same Immortal Island—like Mi’er, Tie Song, and Yueniang—were unaware. The master who had said she was going out had actually been in the island’s forest for three years.","As for the contract beasts, they knew their master had gone to the forest. However, she had long instructed them to guard the Immortal Island. Thus, they never mentioned her forest seclusion to anyone, for they understood: their master was attempting to open a divine gate to the Upper Immortal Realm within the Nine Heavens.","This endeavor had been attempted by no one in countless millennia."]},{"number":5072,"title":"Chapter 5072: Awakening","paragraphs":["Deep within the forest, Feng Jiu sat cross-legged at the center of an array formation. As she waved her hand, a pure essence of spirit energy coalesced in her palm, crystallizing into the void as she formed intricate seals with her fingers.","The intricate ancient patterns at her feet radiated a dazzling glow. Within this light, a faint greenish aura flickered, mingled with a wisp of primordial energy.","\"Open!\"","She uttered the command softly. With a flick of her wrist, a vortex of flame materialized before her. At its edges, the flames formed a ring of ancient patterns, while at its center, a swirling, deep-green void spun endlessly, its depths unseen.","Gazing at the void vortex that had materialized, joy welled up in her eyes, and a delighted smile spread across her face. \"I’ve succeeded! I’ve finally succeeded! Who said this barrier array within the Nine Heavens could never be breached? Who claimed this separation spanned nine layers of heaven? Now, within this ancient formation, the path to immortality has been opened!\"","Overcome with joy, she stood up laughing, only to notice her crimson robe was tattered from three years of repeated experiments. Her jet-black hair had grown considerably, and a few fallen leaves clung to her body.","Seeing this, she chuckled softly. Glancing at the flame teleportation path before her, she swept her sleeve and closed it.","If she must go, she should at least tidy herself first. She couldn’t very well appear before them looking like this and scare them off.","Glancing down at her disheveled state, she chuckled and shook her head. Though she could purify herself with immortal arts, she still felt a proper bath would be better.","Thus, she stepped out of the array beneath her feet, dispelled the surrounding barriers, and made her way toward a waterfall deep within the forest...","The coastal waters of the Lower Immortal Realm.","What Feng Jiu didn’t know was that over these three years, within these seas, Xuanyuan Mo Ze’s immortal body had solidified and taken shape, showing faint signs of awakening.","In these waters, Du Fan and the others continued to take turns guarding, never neglecting their own cultivation. They hoped that one day, they too could ascend successfully like their Master and join her in the Upper Immortal Realm.","All cultivated with this shared aspiration. Yet, at their current cultivation levels, ascension proved exceedingly difficult—perhaps even a faint hope. They might spend their entire lives unable to ascend, forever stagnating at their present power tier.","A figure approached from afar, sword-riding across the sea surface before landing at the airship.","\"Leng Hua, Luoyu, long time no see!\"","Guan Xilin, landing by the airship, laughed heartily. His deep voice carried with powerful resonance. Over the years, his cultivation had grown profoundly deeper. Yet, ascension remained an unattainable dream for him. Moreover, his home, his My lady and children, were all here. He couldn’t bear to ascend and leave them behind. Thus, despite his high cultivation, he held little obsession with ascension.","\"It’s been years. What brought you here?\" Luo Yu, who had been speaking with Leng Hua, smiled as he approached Guan Xilin. Patting his shoulder and giving him a once-over, he remarked, \"You seem to have put on weight over the years! Looks like you’re living the good life.\"","Guan Xilin chuckled. \"Life’s been quiet these past years, so I thought I’d drop by. By the way, how’s things with Mo Ze? It’s been several years now—still no movement?\"","\"We went down yesterday,\" Leng Hua replied softly, joining them. \"His immortal body has solidified, and there are faint signs he’s beginning to awaken.\""]},{"number":5073,"title":"Chapter 5073: Who Dares Cause Trouble?","paragraphs":["\"That’s right. Gray Wolf and Shadow One now manage Hell’s Lord’s domain. News came a few days ago that the energy there has stabilized considerably, and their Master’s divine consciousness has grown much stronger. I heard they plan to visit and should arrive within the next few days.\" Luo Yu smiled as he said to him, \" You’ve come all this way. Why not take a seat inside and rest while Leng Hua entertains you? I need to take some men out to patrol the sea surface.\"","\"It’s been a while since I’ve been here. I’ll join you on patrol! I also want to dive down and check on Mo Ze’s situation,\" Guan Xilin said.","Seeing this, Luo Yu and Leng Hua exchanged glances and laughed. \"Alright, let’s all go together.\" \" With that, the three led their men out to patrol the sea surface. After circling a few times, two of them guided Guan Xilin toward the depths.","Deep within the ocean, at the location sealed off by Feng Jiu’s barrier, the once-ethereal figure at its center had solidified. Its aura no longer felt faint and fragile, as if it might cease at any moment. Even separated by the barrier, they could sense its energy growing stronger.","The barrier prevented closer inspection, so after observing for a while, they departed, returning to the surface and heading toward the airship.","On board, they chatted, exchanging stories of their lives over the past years, with Feng Jiu being the most frequently mentioned.","\"Blink of an eye, and so many years have passed. I wonder how Xiao Jiu and the others are doing now? With the Nine Heavens separating us, it’s truly difficult to know her current situation!\" Guan Xilin sighed softly.","\"With the Master’s abilities, wherever she is, she must be doing well,\" Leng Hua said, gazing out at the sea. \"However, the Hell’s Lord is still here. She once said that if she could find a way back, she would return to visit.\"","Guan Xilin nodded, but said nothing more. Return? How could that be easy? Nine heavens separate us. If a celestial path could be forged, the cultivator from the Immortal Realm would have come here long ago.","\"By the way, where are Leng Shuang and the others? Weren’t they supposed to be here with you?\" Guan Xilin looked around, but saw no one else.","Leng Hua smiled gently. \"My sister and Qinxin went into town for supplies. They should be back around dusk.\"","\"Since you’re here for a rare visit, we’ll cook up a feast for you tonight. When you’re by the sea, you eat from the sea—and the ocean holds plenty of delicious sea beasts. I’ll have someone catch a big one for us.\" Luo Yu waved over a Phoenix Guard and gave instructions.","\"Hahaha! I plan to stay here for several days. Since I’m here, I won’t be leaving anytime soon. Over these days, bring up everything from the sea I haven’t tasted yet. If there’s any left, I can take it back for them.\"","Guan Xilin laughed heartily, pulling two jars of wine from his spatial storage. \"I know you don’t have much good wine around here. See? I brought two jars myself. Come, let me pour you a taste.\"","Luo Yu and Leng Hua exchanged a knowing smile. \"We don’t drink much these days. After all, we can’t afford any mishaps while guarding these waters. But a couple of sips won’t hurt.\"","Hearing this, Guan Xilin chuckled. \"A few more cups won’t hurt. Besides, who dares cause trouble in these waters? You’ve been guarding this area for years—nothing’s ever happened, has it?\""]},{"number":5074,"title":"Chapter 5074: Restless","paragraphs":["\"That may be true, but it’s still best to be cautious. After all, our Master is no longer here. If anything happens, we’ll be the ones left to deal with it.\" Luo Yu spoke with rare seriousness. \"Perhaps you haven’t paid much attention to the affairs of the various celestial realms while at the ancestral home, but we’ve recently received intelligence that some rulers are growing restless and beginning to stir.\"","Guan Xilin froze slightly at these words, his sword-like brows furrowing. \"Do you mean someone dares to target you? Setting aside Little Jiu’s absence, your strength alone is enough to intimidate any powerful figure. Who would be so reckless as to stir trouble?\"","\"They likely see that our master has ascended to the Immortal Realm and won’t return, so they’ve grown bold.\" Leng Hua said softly, pouring more tea for the two.","\"Recently, some rulers in the Celestial Realm have been annexing other territories to expand their influence. While no one has dared to target Master’s domain yet, they’ve already set their sights on it. We’ve received intelligence that several groups have been monitoring the Pill Tower for some time now. That’s precisely why Fan Lin and the others remain stationed there, maintaining vigilance to respond to any developments.\"","Luo Yu took a sip of tea before continuing, \"Since nothing has happened yet, we didn’t inform you—we didn’t want to worry you. Should they make a move, our strength is sufficient to handle it.\"","Guan Xilin frowned, his expression grim as he stared at the two men. \"That’s where you went wrong. How could you not inform me of such a matter? I am, after all, Little Jiu’s brother. With her absent, if her holdings are truly being targeted, I must step in to protect her interests.\"","\"Rest assured,\" Luo Yu replied with a smile. \"Should that day ever come, you will be the first to know.\"","Just then, a thunderous crash echoed across the sea, as if a massive boulder had plummeted into the water, sending countless splashes skyward.","\"What’s happening?!\" Luo Yu sprang to his feet, rushing to the bow and barking the question as his gaze fixed on the sea.","A Phoenix Guard swiftly returned to report: \"Captain, something plunged from the sky into the sea. Two guards have already gone down to investigate.\"","\"Why would something suddenly crash into the Eastern Sea Spirit Domain? Did you see what it was?\" Guan Xilin asked.","\"It came down too fast. I couldn’t make it out,\" the Phoenix Guard shook his head.","\"Look!\" Leng Hua suddenly exclaimed, a hint of astonishment in his voice.","The others turned to where he pointed. There, amidst the splashing sea, a vortex seemed to be forming. It grew larger and larger, deepening into the ocean.","\"Go check it out!\" Luo Yu declared, immediately rising on a surge of energy toward the vortex.","But just then, drumbeats echoed from behind the clouds on the horizon. Startled, they looked up to see figures gradually emerging from the white clouds.","A dense, dark mass of figures stood within the clouds, all clad in armor and wielding weapons. At the front, amidst the white clouds, three drummers beat three large drums. The rhythmic thudding echoed across the sky, its sound nearly piercing the heavens.","\"Dong! Dong! Dong! Dong-dong-dong-dong-dong!\"","The drumbeats carried a powerful spirit energy, forming visible sound waves that rippled outward, echoing across the sea and beyond."]},{"number":5075,"title":"Chapter 5075: If We Do Not Act Now, When Will We Ever?","paragraphs":["Capítulo 5075: If We Do Not Act Now, When Will We Ever?","“War drums!”","Luo Yu narrowed his eyes, a flash of icy killing intent crossing his gaze. “Looks like they’ve come to declare war on us.”","He fixed his gaze on the eight leaders at the forefront. Several faces were familiar—rulers from other celestial realms who had once come to congratulate Master upon his ascension. Little did they expect that in just a few short years, these same figures would return bearing war drums.","“That vortex is still sinking deeper. That place is precisely where Hell’s Lord’s immortal body resides. If we let the vortex sink any further, we might disturb him,” Leng Hua said, his brow slightly furrowed.","“I’ll retrieve that thing!” Guan Xilin declared, gathering his qi to plunge into the sea. But just as he prepared to enter the depths, a monarch blocked his path.","“I’ve long heard of Guan Xilin, the Phoenix Empress’ sworn brother. For a Mystical Cultivator, your prowess is remarkable. Today, I’d like to test your skills.” The speaker gripped a broad sword, his frame broad and imposing, radiating overwhelming presence.","Finding his path blocked, Guan Xilin’s expression darkened. He glared at the figure before him and demanded sharply, “Who are you? Have you no idea where this place is? Daring to cause trouble here—it seems you’ve grown tired of living!”","He truly hadn’t expected that, with Little Jiu having ascended to immortality only a few years ago, these people would already be unable to contain themselves. When Luo Yu had mentioned it earlier, he had found it hard to believe. Yet now, here they were. Who was backing these people? And who gave them the audacity to cause trouble right here?","“Hahahaha! Who doesn’t know the Phoenix Empress is peerless under heaven? Who doesn’t know her might reverberates across the eight directions? Every cultivator knows her name!” The burly cultivator roared with laughter, his voice carrying a surge of spiritual pressure that rippled out before pausing.","He glanced at Guan Xilin before him and let out an inexplicable smile: ” However, it has been several years since the Phoenix Empress ascended. Though I, Leiteng, may be unremarkable, I understand that ascending to the Immortal Realm is separated by nine layers of heaven. Even if the Phoenix Empress succeeded in ascending and attained the status of an Emperor or a great power, she will never be able to return to this realm in this lifetime.”","As he spoke, the smile on his face gradually widened, his eyes flashing with ambition. He continued: ” Feng Jiu may have ascended, but she left you to govern her realms. Yet now, Feng Jiu is no longer in this world. She has become a legend, even a myth. Even Hell’s Lord lingers half-dead in these seas, nourishing his body by absorbing the Spirit Energy of heaven and earth. Tell me, if we do not act now, when will we?”","As the words fell, the cultivator named Leiteng swung his greatsword, striking toward Guan Xilin. He bellowed, “Today, I shall begin the slaughter! Let Guan Xilin’s blood fuel your might!”","A formidable pressure surged forth, accompanied by a fierce killing intent. Above the clouds, the war drums beat with increasing force, their sound growing ever louder. Each beat seemed to stomp on every note, each thud landing directly on the hearts of the crowd, echoing in their ears.","“What a boastful claim! I’ll see if you have the skill to make Guan Xilin’s blood stain the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm red!”","Guan Xilin roared, his aura of mystical power surging with fierce battle intent. He drew a great broadsword, gripped it firmly, and swung it diagonally toward the sea. Simultaneously, his figure streaked like a flash of light, charging toward his opponent.","Watching the two engage in battle, Luo Yu’s gaze fixed on one of the rulers within the clouds. His voice was low and icy: “Nancheng Monarch, are you declaring war against us?”"]},{"number":5076,"title":"Chapter 5076: Full Force","paragraphs":["Amidst the clouds, the Nancheng Monarch, standing alongside the other sovereigns, heard Luo Yu's words. His gaze flickered slightly as he replied, \"Luo Yu, it is not that this sovereign seeks to oppose you. Rather, each serves their own master.\"","\"Each serving their own master?\"","Hearing this, Luo Yu and Leng Hua's hearts stirred slightly. They exchanged a glance, then Luo Yu said in a deep voice, \"As a Monarch ruling over a domain, how can you say you serve your master? Could it be...\"","\"The dead needn't know too much.\" A nearby monarch interjected, glancing at the Nancheng Monarch beside him. \"Just kill them and take Xuanyuan Mo Ze away. Why waste words?\"","His voice trailed off, replaced by an enigmatic smile. \"I hear this Luo Yu is one of the Eight Phoenix Guard Captains under Feng Jiu. How about... the Nancheng Monarch deals with him?\"","The Nancheng Monarch looked at Luo Yu and said, \"Your power is formidable, Yuanling Monarch. Why not let us witness it?\"","\"Hmph! Since that is the case, Nancheng Monarch, watch closely. See how I take his life!\" The monarch spoke, and as his voice fell, a flash of Shadow One appeared. In the blink of an eye, a palm strike was already hurtling toward Luo Yu's face.","Luo Yu met the attack head-on without evading. His palm gathered spirit energy, unleashing a counter-strike. The palm strike, infused with spirit energy, expanded several times in size mid-air. With a thunderous crash, it collided with the attack launched by the Yuanling Ruler.","\"Boom!\"","The two palms collided, erupting in a thunderous impact. As the sound rippled out, two powerful currents of air exploded outward, sending waves crashing dozens of meters high.","\"Whoosh!\"","As waves splashed around them, the two figures clashed head-on. Both were exceptionally powerful, now locked in a fierce exchange. Intense currents of energy radiated from their bodies, while the deadly force of their palm strikes crashed into the sea surface with thunderous booms.","Though Yuanling Monarch possessed considerable strength, Luo Yu was one of the Eight Captains under Feng Jiu. His skills and prowess were honed under her direct tutelage—how could he be compared to just anyone? Especially in this one-on-one confrontation.","Their battle lasted but a moment before Luo Yu unleashed a palm strike. The lightning-fast strike, carrying immense force, slammed heavily into Yuanling Monarch's chest.","\"Boom!\"","As the thunderous impact echoed, Yuanling Monarch—who had been brimming with confidence moments before—felt his internal organs shift violently with the strike. Agonizing pain surged through him as a torrent of blood shot up from his chest, erupting from his throat in a violent spurt.","\"Pfft!\"","As his body was sent flying dozens of meters toward the sea surface, another mouthful of blood spurted out, causing gasps of shock from those watching from the clouds.","\"Your Majesty!\"","A figure darted out, swiftly reaching the spot where he had been knocked down to catch him, preventing his entire body from plunging into the deep sea.","\"Lord Yuanling, you're nothing special!\" Luo Yu said coldly. With a flick of his sleeve and a swift hand movement, a sharp, icy blade appeared in his grasp, pointing diagonally toward the sea.","He stared at the other lords watching coldly from the clouds and declared, \"Who else wants to come down and fight? I, Luo Yu, will see you through to the end!\"","War drums thundered, as if rallying Leiteng Monarch battling Guan Xilin. Yet Leiteng Monarch was steadily forced back.","Across the battlefield, blades flashed and whirled. Overwhelming pressure surged between them. Guan Xilin unleashed his full might, his fighting spirit surging, his killing intent thick in the air!"]},{"number":5077,"title":"Chapter 5077: The Primordial Treasure Umbrella","paragraphs":["\"Take this from your Grandfather Guan! Ha!\"","With a swing of his massive broadsword, a fierce and powerful blade aura whistled toward his opponent. Its momentum was as fierce as a tiger descending the mountain, sharp and unstoppable!","The blade descended like a bamboo splintering, ferocious beyond measure. The overwhelming blade aura and his intense battle intent erupted outward. Yuanling Monarch's heart skipped a beat as he instinctively tried to dodge, but his evasion proved too slow to escape the falling blade.","\"Aah!\"","A piercing scream erupted as an arm was cleanly severed, spinning through the air before plummeting into the sea. Crimson blood spattered in that instant, falling from mid-air onto the water's surface like scattered blood-red plum blossoms blooming in the ocean, only to vanish instantly.","The war drums abruptly fell silent. As if stunned by this unexpected turn, the three cultivators beating them stared wide-eyed, their hands frozen mid-strike.","\"Gah! Guan Xilin! I shall never rest until you are destroyed!\"","Yuanling Monarch roared in agony, his voice thick with hatred and murderous intent. Clutching his severed arm, blood gushed forth like a fountain, soaking through his palm and staining his robes crimson.","\"Whoosh!\"","Guan Xilin held his greatsword at an angle, pointing toward the sea. His tiger-like eyes, brimming with fierce battle intent, fixed sharply on the man. \"We shall never coexist? Hah! Today, you shall meet your end beneath my blade, your blood staining the Eastern Sea Spirit Domain!\"","As the words fell, he drew in a deep breath and soared into the air. His entire form shot forward like an arrow released from a bow, mesmerizing and unstoppable!","\"Quick! Quick, help me!\"","The Yuanling Monarch's face paled. Clutching his severed arm, he retreated rapidly while crying out in alarm, seeking aid from the other monarchs within the clouds.","The others exchanged glances before descending, splitting into groups to offer aid.","Their arrival this time, commanded by their sovereign and involving multiple rulers, stemmed from their apprehension toward Feng Jiu's followers. Unable to win one-on-one, they resorted to two-on-one, three-on-one tactics! They refused to believe their combined strength couldn't overcome these opponents!","Standing at the bow, Leng Hua saw Guan Xilin and Luo Yu each facing two or three sovereigns working together against them. Meanwhile, the whirlpool at sea grew ever deeper. Worried it might disturb Hell's Lord, the divine soul of the sea's temperature difference, he leapt into the water.","\"Stop him!\"","A monarch bellowed, ordering his men to intercept Leng Hua's descent into the sea. The moment his voice faded, the cultivators they brought plunged into the air. Some engaged the Phoenix Guards, while others dove into the sea to block Leng Hua's path.","War drums thundered as both sides clashed, their battle fervor reaching its peak!","News of the battle in the East Sea Spirit Domain and the thunderous drumbeats spread, alerting numerous powerful beings. Those nearby came to observe, but upon seeing the clash between sovereigns, they recoiled in alarm, retreating to a safer distance to watch.","Meanwhile, the drumbeats shook half the heavens, prompting Leng Shuang, Qin Xin, and Ye Feifei to race back at breakneck speed while swiftly alerting others.","Deep within the ocean, he submerged beneath the waves and witnessed the burrowing object—resembling a colossal iron umbrella. Its formidable aura, accompanied by terrifying air currents, plunged relentlessly into the depths. When the iron umbrella reached the lower layers and collided with the defensive barrier, its speed visibly slowed, becoming sluggish.","\"It's the Primordial Treasure Umbrella!\""]},{"number":5078,"title":"Chapter 5078: Bloodstained East Sea","paragraphs":["Leng Hua's eyes narrowed as he recognized this umbrella as no ordinary object. At that moment, a powerful air current surged from the tip of the canopy, burrowing toward the barrier. He feared that if unchecked, this Primordial Treasure Umbrella would shatter the barrier!","Yet, just as he prepared to move forward, the surrounding cultivators closed in, weapons raised to attack him. Instantly, his situation grew more perilous—trapped in the water, he had to evade their encircling assault while simultaneously striving to reach the Primordial Treasure Umbrella.","The battle raged in the sea, churning waves churning, faint traces of blood seeping into the seawater and dissolving.","Compared to Feng Jiu, Leng Hua was considered a slow cultivator. His cultivation base couldn't compare to Luo Yu and the others. Now, surrounded by those cultivators in the sea, his body was slashed by sword qi, blood staining his off-white robe crimson...","\"Clang!\"","A piercing qin melody suddenly rang out. Though the source remained unseen, the sound waves already surged toward the cultivators battling the Phoenix Guards.","Simultaneously, lightning-eagles screeched in the sky. Bolts of lightning crashed down from above, striking the besieging cultivators. At the same moment, Leng Shuang's sleek, black figure darted out like a ghostly apparition. Her long sword slashed downward, its killing intent blazing like a rainbow!","\"Luo Yu, I'm coming to aid you!\"","The moment Leng Shuang's voice rang out, she charged toward Luo Yu, who was being besieged by three Monarchs. Despite his formidable combat prowess, Luo Yu was now covered in wounds, blood dripping from his body.","Hearing Leng Shuang's voice, Luo Yu's heart steadied slightly. Without turning his head, he shouted back, \"I can hold on! Go to the sea and help Leng Hua! That entire group of cultivators is surrounding him alone at the bottom of the ocean. Do your best to stop that vortex from sinking deeper—don't disturb Hell's Lord!\"","Hearing this, Leng Shuang looked toward the sea. She saw the whirlpool churning, with faint figures of cultivators lurking beneath the surface. Blades and sword qi erupted, slicing through the water and sending waves crashing.","\"Alright! Hold on!\"","Leng Shuang immediately leapt into the sea. She knew her brother Leng Hua's combat prowess was slightly inferior to Luo Yu and the others, especially when fighting underwater and under such overwhelming attack.","And that vortex—if it sank any deeper, it would inevitably disturb Hell's Lord. They had faithfully guarded this place all these years under their Master's command. Now that their Master was absent, how could they allow Hell's Lord, who lay dormant in the sea nurturing his divine soul, to be disturbed?","The gravity of the situation left her without a moment's hesitation. She simply told Luo Yu to hold on. Because their reinforcements were nearly here!","\"Strike there!\"","Ye Feifei, perched on the Lightning Eagle's back, gripped its feathers with one hand while wielding her sword against the approaching cultivators. Simultaneously, the eagle lunged at the several Monarchs attacking Luo Yu.","As a Sacred Beast, the Lightning Eagle was a combat-oriented bird. Its talons tore fiercely at the cultivators while striking the Sovereigns besieging Luo Yu.","\"Crackle!\"","A crackling bolt of lightning shot forth, striking one of the Sovereigns with a sharp crack. The Sovereign was jolted by the current, letting out a startled cry as his body froze for an instant. In that split second, Luo Yu's sword thrust straight toward his throat.","\"Get out of the way!\" Another monarch grabbed him, yanking him backward as he shouted, \"Go deal with that lightning eagle!\"","The monarch who had been pulled back caught his breath, his gaze fixed on the Lightning Eagle above and the woman perched upon it. A cold, murderous intent flashed through his dark eyes. In the next instant, his figure blurred like a shadow as he darted toward the woman atop the Lightning Eagle."]},{"number":5079,"title":"Chapter 5079: In Peril","paragraphs":["\"Zheng!\"","The piercing notes of the zither assaulted the sovereign in that instant. Each note felt like a sharp blade, not striking the man's body, but piercing his very soul.","\"Hiss!\"","Caught off guard by the assault on his soul, the monarch sucked in a sharp breath, feeling a violent impact within his spirit. Regaining his balance, he scanned his surroundings and saw a woman seated cross-legged atop the airship, her fingers dancing swiftly across the strings. Each note shot straight at his soul!","\"So it was you!\"","The monarch's voice darkened as murderous intent flashed in his eyes, fixed on the woman playing. In the next instant, he swept his hand, sending a surge of energy hurtling toward the airship's roof.","Whoosh!","As the fierce killing intent surged, Qin Xin spun upward, clutching her zither. From playing with both hands, she shifted to holding the instrument with one arm while plucking with the other. Her fingers danced across the strings with increasing speed, blurring into mere shadows. Simultaneously, waves of attacks erupted from the zither, sweeping out in all directions.","\"Ssshh!\"","Some cultivators were struck in their divine souls, letting out agonized screams as they clutched their heads and tumbled into the sea.","\"Water conducts electricity! Zap them!\" Ye Feifei shouted, blocking an attacking cultivator's sword before leaping up and delivering a flying kick.","The moment her voice rang out, the Lightning Eagle seized the opportunity, unleashing an electric current attack toward the sea where the cultivators had fallen. Instantly, a chorus of agonized screams erupted below.","\"Enough! Be careful—Leng Shuang and the others are in the water! Don't hurt them!\" Ye Feifei shouted urgently.","\"Seeking death!\"","\"Feifei, watch out!\"","Suddenly, a voice brimming with murderous intent echoed from behind Ye Feifei, accompanied by Qin Xin's startled cry.","In that instant, Ye Feifei felt every hair on her back stand on end. An overwhelming aura and terrifying killing intent froze her completely, leaving her unable even to turn around.","\"Thud!\"","A heavy palm slammed into Ye Feifei's body, sending her flying off the Lightning Eagle's back and plummeting toward the sea.","\"Pfft!\"","Blood spurted from Ye Feifei's mouth. She couldn't even attempt to steady herself, feeling as though that single blow had shattered her internal organs. The excruciating pain radiating outward from within turned her face deathly pale, her vision darkening. Even her hearing seemed to fade, leaving her only aware of her descent.","Seeing her fall, the Lightning Eagle abandoned its attack on others, swiftly folding its wings to dive down and catch her.","\"Master!\"","Crashing onto the Lightning Eagle's back, Ye Feifei's mouth overflowed with blood. Her eyes remained open, her hand still clutching the sword as she tried to rise. Yet her body offered no strength whatsoever. Finally, darkness swallowed her...","\"Feifei!\"","Qinxin cried out in alarm, her heart racing as she tried to rush to her side. Yet the Sovereign had locked horns with her, striking out to block her path.","Deep within the ocean, the same crimson hue spread. Blood-red water stained the sea, and murderous intent lurked beneath the waves.","Leng Hua gripped the handle of the Primordial Treasure Umbrella, channeling spirit energy into it to fold it shut while pulling it upward. His sister, Leng Shuang, stood guard beside him, slashing at the besieging cultivators.","Two against many—it was bound to be a bloody battle. The blood spreading through the sea water—who could say whether it belonged to their enemies or to themselves..."]},{"number":5080,"title":"Chapter 5080: She Has Arrived","paragraphs":["What they hadn't anticipated was that not only were they under siege here, but even the Heavenly Pill Tower where Du Fan and the others were stationed was now under enemy attack...","The Pill Tower was nearly completely destroyed. Qi Kang and Wei Feng, along with the Phoenix Guards, were fiercely battling the enemy. However, not long ago, they received separate messages from Leng Hua and Leng Shuang, informing them that the East Sea Spirit Domain was also under attack.","Therefore, some of them remained here to defend the Pill Tower, while others rushed to the East Sea Spirit Domain. Compared to the Pill Tower, the East Sea was far more critical—because the Hell's Lord was there!","Before Feng Jiu's ascension, she had left them many items, among which was a teleportation axis. Yet, when Du Fan, Fan Lin, and the others appeared in a flash of light from the axis, what they witnessed was Qin Xin being struck down into the sea.","\"Qin Xin!\"","Fan Lin's heart leapt as he cried out, his figure darting forward. Yet, having emerged from the teleportation axis, they landed near the shoreline. Even with their speed, reaching the location of the airship—the site of their battle—would take time. Thus, no matter how swiftly they moved, they couldn't catch Qin Xin before she plunged into the sea.","Fortunately, the Lightning Eagle, dodging wildly while carrying the unconscious Ye Feifei, spotted Qinxin's injury and swiftly descended to catch her. Spotting Du Fan and the others approaching, it immediately flapped its wings and flew toward them.","\"Damn it!\"","Seeing the situation, Gu Mo cursed under his breath, his face darkening. He swiftly joined the fray, rushing to aid Luo Yu, who was covered in wounds.","\"Whoosh! Bang bang bang!\"","Sword qi imbuesd with ice slashed out, striking directly at the several monarchs. As the powerful sword qi cut through the air, it sliced across the sea surface, sending up sprays of water and rippling air currents.","\"Can you still hold on?\" Gu Mo arrived beside him, offering a hand to support him as he asked.","\"Ughhh! You finally made it. If you'd been any later, I really wouldn't have held out.\" Luo Yu exhaled softly. Covered in blood, he flashed a wicked grin, his gaze icy as he fixed it on the several monarchs. Like a bloodthirsty demon, he showed no trace of fear—only pure killing intent.","Gu Mo joined Luo Yu to assist him, while Lu Yun went to Guan Xilin's side. Fan Lin swiftly produced medicinal pills to feed Qin Xin and Ye Feifei, preserving their vital energy. Fang Cheng aided Feng Wei in battling the other cultivators, and Du Fan entered the sea to support Leng Shuang and Leng Hua.","With their combined efforts, the initially outnumbered group swiftly turned the tide. Yet, at that very moment, a voice echoed down from the clouds.","\"Those left behind by Feng Jiu—it seems they've nearly all arrived, haven't they?\"","The voice sounded like a soliloquy, yet also like a question directed at someone. Gu Mo and the others frowned, looking up, but saw no one speaking. They could only sense a powerful, oppressive aura permeating the air.","\"Come out! Kill them all! This vast expanse, with its countless small worlds, will soon be ours!\"","As the voice echoed, eight more monarchs emerged from the clouds, accompanied by numerous powerful cultivators, descending toward the battlefield. The sound of war drums thundered, each beat louder than the last...","The stench of blood permeated the sea. The deafening drumbeats mingled with the screams of battle. Just as Luo Yu and his companions had gained the upper hand, they were plunged back into a desperate struggle.","Unnoticed by anyone, a crimson figure appeared silently at that very moment..."]},{"number":5081,"title":"Chapter 5081: How Lively","paragraphs":["Dressed in dazzling crimson, the peerlessly beautiful Feng Jiu arrived at the coast. Upon witnessing the chaotic battle raging upon the sea, her eyes turned cold. A powerful aura radiated from her body, The overwhelming pressure surged outward, swiftly spreading toward the horizon, nearly enveloping the entire expanse of sky and earth. A soft, measured voice, tinged with icy coldness and a bloodthirsty aura, echoed out at that moment.","\"How lively!\"","The voice was unhurried, yet it carried a terrifying weight and icy chill. Though merely a soft utterance, it struck the ears of the crowd like thunderclaps. Shock and disbelief flashed across the faces of the gathered rulers.","The instant they heard that voice, every monarch—even the cultivators—felt an icy chill surge from their soles, piercing straight to their hearts.","Whether from sheer shock, utter dread, overwhelming fear, or the overwhelming pressure permeating the air, every combatant in the chaotic fray froze in place.","One by one, they halted. The sea, which had been filled with the constant clamor of screams, the clang of clashing weapons, and the relentless beat of war drums, now fell silent. Only the rhythmic lapping of waves against the shore echoed through the air.","Every figure remained frozen in their original combat stances, their heads stiffly turning toward the source of the voice. As they looked, their eyes suddenly narrowed in shock.","By the shore, a dazzling crimson figure strode toward the sea. As she advanced, her form soared into the air. Her brilliant red robe billowed in the sea breeze, her jet-black hair flying wildly. Her peerlessly exquisite beauty grew ever clearer to all who saw her!","Feng Jiu! How... how is this possible!","The monarchs' hearts lurched violently. To them, this peerlessly beautiful woman in crimson now resembled the grim reaper and demoness come to claim their lives. Terror drained their faces, robbing them even of the courage to flee.","\"Seems I've arrived just in time.\" Feng Jiu, gliding across the sea surface along with the breeze, as her voice reverberated.","In stark contrast to the monarchs' and cultivators' terror, Luo Yu and his companions felt only joy and excitement at her sight.","Seeing that familiar dazzling crimson robe, that familiar exquisite beauty, and recognizing the expression on her face and the sound of her voice, their hearts surged with indescribable emotion.","\"Master!\"","\"Master!\"","\"Master!\"","\"Master!\"","Each cry of \"Master\" rang out with unmistakable excitement and joy. Almost the moment the words left their lips, they rushed toward that crimson figure. Even suspended mid-air above the sea, they bowed reverently and fervently.","\"We humbly welcome your return, Master!\"","The words rang out in unison, strong and resonant, filled with excitement and joy, echoing through the air above the sea.","Feng Jiu stood poised upon the breeze, one hand resting on her abdomen, the other clasped behind her back. She stood silently in the void, yet the formidable pressure and commanding aura radiating from her were so overwhelming that it compelled submission and made direct gaze impossible.","Her crimson robes and jet-black hair fluttered in the wind. Her gaze fell upon Luo Yu and the others kneeling before her, swords clasped in their hands as they saluted with fists pressed together. Her clear, serene eyes narrowed slightly when she saw the splotches of blood staining their bodies."]},{"number":5082,"title":"Chapter 5082: Feng Jiu’s Fury","paragraphs":["\"Little Jiu! You're finally back! Those monarch-level cultivators, thinking you'd never return, actually dared to attack Mo Ze, who was nurturing his divine soul in the deep sea!\" Guan Xilin strode over to her side, his voice brimming with fury.","Hearing this, Feng Jiu's gaze fell upon the sea surface ten meters ahead. There, a vortex swirled, currents surging. She extended her hand forward, and a surge of spirit energy shot out, instantly drawing the object beneath to the surface.","Whoosh! Splash!","The object shot out with a whoosh, spraying countless droplets as it broke the surface, accompanied by a roaring cascade of water. Emerging alongside it was Leng Hua, her grip tight around the umbrella's handle.","\"Master!\"","\"Master!\"","Du Fan and Leng Shuang burst from the sea, their hearts surging with joy at the sight of Feng Jiu before them, their eyes brimming with emotion.","Feng Jiu looked at them. Each bore wounds covering their bodies, even her brother drenched in blood. More importantly, these people dared to attack Mo Ze in the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm while she was away. It was truly unforgivable!","\"I recall issuing a decree during my ascension: this Eastern Sea Spirit Realm nurtures Xuanyuan Mo Ze's divine soul. None shall disturb his tranquility. How many years have passed? Have you forgotten my words so swiftly?\"","Her steps were light as she glided forward on the breeze. With each stride, the oppressive aura enveloping the land grew heavier. Her soft voice, each syllable, each word, struck their ears like thunderclaps, pounding into their hearts and causing their blood to boil and surge chaotically within them, filling them with agony.","Yet behind her, Luo Yu and the others felt not a trace of that pressure. That overwhelming, awe-inspiring force seemed consciously directed only at the monarchs and cultivators.","\"Arghhh!\"","\"Arghhhhhhhh...\"","The cultivators, whose strength paled beside the Monarchs, screamed in agony. Blood gushed from their seven orifices like pillars, and one by one, they plunged into the sea amidst their cries.","\"Pfft!\"","\"Pfft!\"","\"Pfft!\"","Even the monarch-level powerhouses could not stem the blood surging toward their throats. Their mouths opened, blood spurting violently as their bodies swayed violently, nearly toppling them.","Their faces turned ashen, bodies trembling in the wind...","\"Since you've forgotten, I can remind you once more.\" Feng Jiu continued walking forward at a leisurely pace, the oppressive aura within the space gradually contracting as she drew nearer.","\"Those who touch my inverse scale, I will make them wish they were dead!\"","\"Pfft!\"","As she pronounced each syllable with deliberate emphasis, the monarchs felt an immense, terrifying pressure suddenly crush down upon them. The overwhelming force left them no chance to catch their breath, forcing each to spew another mouthful of blood.","Those monarchs who had barely managed to steady themselves now felt as if two colossal mountains were crushing them from above and below. Their bones shattered, their bodies instantly compressed to the size of children. Yet they weren't killed outright; instead, they retained clear consciousness while enduring excruciating, bone-piercing agony.","\"Arghhhhhhh...\"","The agonized screams finally tore from their throats. At this moment, not a single one could endure it any longer—even these ancient monarchs who had ruled their domains for centuries."]},{"number":5083,"title":"Chapter 5083: Blood Flows Like A River","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu halted her steps, watching them with a cold gaze. Yet the oppressive aura weighing down upon them did not recede. Not only did it not recede, but she flipped her palm, sending a ball of her innate heavenly flame hurtling toward the soles of those monarchs' feet.","\"Let you taste this death roasted over flames. Perhaps you'll find it to your liking.\" Her indifferent voice carried a chill as she watched coldly, her eyes devoid of any warmth.","Yet among these monarchs, she spared only the Nancheng Monarch. But even without Feng Jiu's direct intervention, witnessing the pitiful state of his fellow rulers left him too stunned to speak.","Who could have imagined Feng Jiu would return?","Who could have imagined Feng Jiu would ever come back?","Clearly, clearly, for tens of millions of years, none who ascended had ever returned. How had she managed it?","Had he known Feng Jiu would return, even with ten times the courage, he would never have dared commit today's act. Now, regret and terror twisted within him, his body trembling uncontrollably. Yet he could only stare wide-eyed in horror, watching the rulers beside him endure agony worse than death.","\"Arghhhhh!\"","\"Arghhhh...\"","Once mighty rulers, in this moment, were nothing but endless screams, regret, and terror.","Some, unable to bear this agony worse than death, attempted to abandon their physical forms and flee. Yet the moment their divine souls transformed into a halo of light and fled their bodies, Feng Jiu seized them with a single hand.","\"Did I allow you to escape? Do you truly believe you could get away?\"","Feng Jiu's indifferent voice echoed. Without moving a muscle, she stood there, her hand grasping at the void. The halo of divine soul light fell into her palm.","\"Now that you're in my grasp, you won't even get the chance to be reincarnated.\" As she spoke, flames surged from her palm. She closed her hand, crushing the soul's halo between her fingers. Amidst piercing screams, ashes scattered in the wind, drifting into the sea.","Watching this scene, the Nancheng Monarch froze in terror. He tried to beg for mercy, but overwhelming fear rendered him speechless. He could only stare helplessly as Feng Jiu tortured the rulers of various realms to death before his very eyes—leaving not even their divine souls behind.","\"Do you know why I spared you?\" Feng Jiu turned to the Nancheng Monarch, asking coldly.","\"Feng... Feng... Phoenix Empress, spare my life!\" His entire body was limp, unable even to stand, yet a force dragged him forward.","Feng Jiu watched him, her lips curling into a faint, cold smile. \"You should know that those who touch my reverse scales have no chance of survival.\"","\"I kept you alive merely to learn what had transpired here during my years of absence.\" \" As she spoke, she stepped forward, coming to stand before him. Under his terrified gaze, she extended her index finger and pressed it against his brow, beginning the soul search.","After a long moment, she withdrew her finger. The once-terrified Nancheng Monarch now had eyes that were vacant and lifeless. With a flick of her sleeve, a ball of flame ignited, reducing him to ashes.","She turned, her gaze falling on the umbrella Leng Hua clutched tightly nearby. It was a Primordial Treasure Umbrella, now forced shut by her oppressive aura and held firmly in Leng Hua's grasp.","Walking over to the blood-soaked Leng Hua, she offered a faint smile. \"You still lack a proper weapon. This Primordial Treasure Umbrella is yours.\""]},{"number":5084,"title":"Chapter 5084: The Earth Trembles","paragraphs":["As she spoke, under Leng Hua’s stunned gaze, she swept her hand and erased the soul contract from the Primordial Treasure Umbrella.","At the very moment she erased the soul contract from the Primordial Treasure Umbrella, somewhere within the celestial realms, a figure suddenly spat out a mouthful of blood. With a grim, murderous glint in his eyes, he gritted his teeth and growled, \"Feng Jiu!\"","Upon the sea surface, Leng Hua stared at the Primordial Treasure Umbrella in his hand. It no longer seemed intent on flying away amidst the tremors but had settled steadily in his grasp. Startled, he snapped back to his senses and exclaimed, \"Leng Hua thanks Master!\"","He swiftly dripped blood to claim the artifact as his own. After that, he felt a new layer of affinity and familiarity with the Primordial Treasure Umbrella.","Only then did Feng Jiu turn to the others, speaking to them deliberately, one word at a time: \"I, Feng Jiu, have returned!\"","Gazing upon their master, radiant as the sun against the wind, the group’s hearts swelled with joy. Genuine smiles blossomed on each face. The alliance of rulers had waged a fierce, brutal battle against them, but for their master, one alone had been sufficient!","\"Master, when we received Leng Shuang’s message and rushed back, the Pill Tower was already under siege,\" Du Fan hurriedly explained.","Feng Jiu nodded upon hearing this. \"I know.\"","Her voice barely faded as her gaze swept toward the sea. She released her divine sense, probing downward. Seeing the defensive barrier she had cast beneath the waves still intact, she knew the fierce battle hadn’t disturbed Mo Ze’s soul. She then addressed the others: \"Tend to your wounds and rest first. I’ll go check on the Pill Tower.\"","With that, she swept her sleeve, conjuring a teleportation vortex before her.","Meanwhile, at the Pill Tower, Qi Kang and Gray Wolf, left to defend the tower, were fighting together against the enemy. However, besides the monarch, the enemy forces were numerous—a dense, dark mass so overwhelming that no one dared approach within a hundred li.","The fierce battle between the Pill Tower defenders and these monarchs left many stunned and horrified. Even though Feng Jiu had ascended years ago, her lingering influence remained. Her formidable subordinates were still present—each a capable warrior in their own right. How could anyone dare attack them? And with such overwhelming force that the entire Pill Tower had been destroyed?","The entire city was shrouded in the monarchs’ oppressive aura, forcibly isolating the surroundings. The cultivators from the city’s noble families were already struggling to survive and were utterly powerless to aid the Pill Tower.","Qi Kang, Gray Wolf, and the others, fighting tooth and nail, were warriors capable of taking on a hundred foes alone. Yet even they could not withstand this relentless wave after wave of attacks.","\"If I survive today, I’ll slaughter every last one of them!\" Gray Wolf growled, parrying an incoming strike with his sword.","\"Watch out!\"","Qi Kang, locked in combat with two Monarchs nearby, bellowed the warning. Yet he couldn’t spare a hand to aid Gray Wolf, forced to watch helplessly as a blade pierced the warrior’s abdomen from behind.","\"Hmph!\" \" Gray Wolf grunted, whirling to strike the cultivator. His fierce blow cleaved the man clean in two, though the sword remained lodged in Gray Wolf’s abdomen.","\"There are too many of them! Our men are dying in droves. If this continues, we’ll all perish here!\" Shadow One declared. His words had barely left his mouth when the earth suddenly shook violently, as if something massive were charging toward them."]},{"number":5085,"title":"Chapter 5085: Ten Thousand Beasts Storm Forth, Bai Xiao arrives","paragraphs":["Gray Wolf clutched the wound in his abdomen as he retreated to stand beside Shadow One. Cold sweat beaded on his forehead, his face pale as he asked, \"What’s that sound?\"","\"Sounds like a fierce beast running?\" Shadow One hesitated before speaking. Regaining his composure, he steadied Gray Wolf with one hand. Seeing the sword still lodged in his abdomen, blood seeping freely, he asked, \"How are you?\"","\"Hmph! Won’t be dying anytime soon.\"","Gray Wolf snorted, took a deep breath, and reached behind him to grasp the sword. With a surge of spirit energy, he snapped the blade clean through at the point where it pierced his waist.","\"Clang!\"","The blade snapped clean in two, emitting a crisp, metallic clang. He didn’t pull out the broken piece, knowing that doing so might cause unstoppable bleeding.","The battle wasn’t over yet, and he could still fight!","\"It’s Bai Xiao!\" Qi Kang declared, a gleam flashing in his eyes. \"He’s arrived just in time! As long as he ties up those cultivators, we have a chance to win!\"","\"Roar!\"","\"Howl!\"","His words had barely fallen when, amidst the thundering vibrations, a series of beastly roars echoed through the air.","Simultaneously, the expressions of the several monarchs darkened. Turning their heads, they noticed a massive eagle soaring toward them from the distance. Upon its back stood a man clad in green, holding a flute and playing it.","No one heard the sound of the flute, yet they could see rings of musical energy emanating from it.","\"Awoo!\"","Hundreds of powerful fierce beasts charged forward, lunging at the cultivators below. Their attacks were immediate, tearing and biting, plunging the group accompanying the monarchs into chaotic battle against the beasts.","\"Are you all right?\" Bai Xiao twirled his flute and called out to Qi Kang and the others below.","\"If you’d arrived any later, we probably wouldn’t be doing so well,\" Gray Wolf replied with a faint, pale smile.","Seeing the conspicuous wounds covering each of them, Bai Xiao explained, \"The beasts I command can only handle those cultivators. They’re no match for those monarchs.\"","The monarchs’ power and aura were too overwhelming. These fierce beasts were not ancient Sacred Beasts. They could handle the cultivators, but they dared not approach those monarchs.","\"We’ll deal with them!\" Qi Kang declared, twirling his sword. He fixed his gaze on the monarchs, whose faces darkened as they watched the ensuing battle between humans and beasts. His voice barely faded before he leapt into the air, sword raised, charging toward one of the monarchs.","Seeing this, Bai Xiao leapt from the eagle’s back and grabbed the Gray Wolf, who was holding his sword and about to charge into battle. \"Are you out of your mind? You’ve got a broken sword lodged in your belly, bleeding!\"","\"I won’t die! I’m going to take out a few more!\" Gray Wolf said, pushing him aside and preparing to advance.","\"Stay back!\" Shadow One frowned, instructing Bai Xiao to keep watch. Only then did he gather his strength and dart toward the remaining lords.","\"Leave the rest to us! We’ll take them all down!\" After slashing through several cultivators, Xu Duo also charged at the lords.","In terms of combat prowess, the eight Phoenix Guard captains were all equally formidable. Trained personally by their Master, they were confident they could handle the troublesome cultivators and eliminate the remaining lords!","Amidst the constant clamor of battle and beast roars, Bai Xiao saw the situation and pulled him halfway back."]},{"number":5086,"title":"Chapter 5086: Whose Death Anniversary","paragraphs":["Surveying the chaotic battlefield, Bai Xiao rexclaimed, \"How could the Heavenly Pill Tower","be wrecked to such an extent?! Where are the others? Why are only a few of you left here?\"","Gray Wolf caught his breath, cold sweat dripping from his forehead. \"They’ve been plotting this for a long time. They split into two groups. Besides the Heavenly Pill Tower","here, the Eastern Sea Spirit Domain was also attacked. So, aside from us few holding the fort here, everyone else rushed over there.\"","\"Eastern Sea Spirit Domain?\" Bai Xiao gasped. \"Do they intend to target Hell’s Lord? Where do they get the nerve?\"","\"My lady has been gone for years, leaving only us to guard this place. Naturally, they wouldn’t accept this situation forever. Moreover, it seems there are other matters at play. There’s a mastermind behind this. Be careful!\" As Gray Wolf spoke, he let out a low cry, grabbing Bai Xiao and pulling him back while simultaneously swinging the sword in his hand toward the front.","\"Ah!\"","A cultivator preparing for a sneak attack screamed and collapsed. Gray Wolf staggered back several steps.","Bai Xiao supported him, watching the chaotic scene unfold. \"Let me get you to safety first. Apply some hemostatic medicine to your wound.\"","Just as he was about to step back, he saw Qi Kang locked in combat with a Sovereign mid-air ahead. Not far away, another Sovereign seized the opportunity to strike from behind. Startled, he shouted, \"Qi Kang, watch your back!\"","Yet despite his warning, Qi Kang was now ensnared by a golden silk net cast by the front monarch. As he struggled, the net tightened further, leaving him utterly defenseless against the fatal strike approaching from behind.","\"Stay here! I’ll help him!\" Bai Xiao, seeing this, disregarded his own inferiority against monarch-level power and charged toward Qi Kang with a burst of energy.","\"You old bastard, you actually have such a treasure!\" Gray Wolf cursed, gripping his sword and charging forward with all his might, completely disregarding the broken sword still lodged in his own body.","\"Get out of the way!\"","Unable to block the monarch’s strike, Bai Xiao saw the blade descending toward Qi Kang. He lunged forward, colliding with Qi Kang and sending both tumbling through the air. They landed squarely on the back of a fierce beast below, only to be shaken off and rolled toward the ruins of the Heavenly Pill Tower’s walls.","\"Seeking death!\" The monarch’s face darkened as his sword sliced through empty air. His eyes blazed with icy killing intent, sweeping over Qi Kang and Bai Xiao.","\"Do you think you’ll survive today? Mark my words—next year on this day will be your death anniversary!\"","As he spoke, the spirit energy within his blade coalesced once more. A powerful sword qi erupted from the blade’s edge. With a swift raise of his hand, the sword shot forward, pointing directly at the two figures huddled in the corner of the ruins.","\"Is that so?\"","Suddenly, a cold, clear voice cut through the air, jarringly abrupt. Those who recognized it froze in shock.","Even the monarchs paused at the sound of that unexpected, icy female voice, a vague sense of foreboding rising within them.","They looked toward the source of the voice and saw a vortex appear in the air not far from them. A dazzling red figure emerged from the swirling vortex, and as she stepped out, the vortex behind her vanished instantly.","\"Master!\"","\"My Lady!\"","Recognizing that familiar figure, Qi Kang, Gray Wolf, and the others were overcome with excitement and joy after their initial shock—even disbelief."]},{"number":5087,"title":"Chapter 5087: Please Punish Us","paragraphs":["Even if those who had never seen Feng Jiu, they had heard of her formidable reputation. They knew she possessed a face that could topple cities and favored crimson robes!","Yet now, seeing Feng Jiu suddenly appear here, they were utterly bewildered.","\"Feng... Feng Jiu? Impossible!\"","How many years had it been since Feng Jiu ascended? How could she still be here? Could this be an imposter?","Yet, the moment this thought arose, their faces drained of colour, turning ashen. For with each step she took through the air, an aura and pressure hundreds of times more formidable than their own closed in. Before her, these mighty sovereigns found even breathing difficult.","\"Perhaps you’re unaware,\" Feng Jiu’s voice carried with deliberate slowness, yet it carried an icy chill and palpable intent to kill.","\"This time next year will mark not only their death anniversary, but yours as well.\" \" As she spoke these words, blood began seeping from the seven orifices of those sovereigns, leaving them utterly speechless.","\"Pfft!\"","The overwhelming pressure caused their qi and blood to surge chaotically within their bodies. Their vision blurred as blood filled their eyes, and a mouthful of blood gushed forth. Unable to even stand mid-air, they plummeted downward.","Below, the vast, dark mass of fierce beasts—countless in number—had moments before been locked in savage combat with the cultivators. Yet the instant Feng Jiu’s voice echoed, the instant she arrived, every one of those brutal creatures lay obediently on the ground, not even daring to lift their heads.","As for the cultivators, they lay prostrate on the ground, trembling violently, not daring to move a muscle. Those who had seen Feng Jiu before were particularly terrified, some even fainting on the spot.","Qi Kang and the others watched as their master raised a hand. Several cold gleams instantly shot into the foreheads of the rulers. Shattering their divine souls, the life force within them extinguished in that very instant.","You dared destroy my Heavenly Pill Tower? You have some nerve.","The indifferent voice sent a chill through every cultivator present. They knew this day marked not only the anniversary of those rulers’ deaths, but their own.","Sure enough, moments after the voice faded, one by one they collapsed with muffled groans. They never saw Feng Jiu strike, for she hadn’t moved at all—instead, her overwhelming pressure alone crushed their divine souls.","\"Xiao Bai, have these fierce beasts withdraw from the city.\" Feng Jiu spoke, her gaze turning to Bai Xiao crouched in the corner.","\"Yes!\" Bai Xiao responded immediately, rising to his feet and looking up at the sky. With the deaths of those sovereigns, the barriers and auras they had cast into the air dissipated.","He drew his flute and began to play, driving the fierce beasts out of the city and back into the forest.","\"We pay homage to our Master!\"","Led by Qi Kang and the others, along with the Phoenix Guards who had protected the Heavenly Pill Tower, they knelt respectfully on one knee, their eyes brimming with excitement as they gazed upon their Master.","They did not know why their master, who had already ascended, had returned. They only knew that seeing her again was truly a blessing!","\"Rise, all of you!\" Feng Jiu said, stepping forward slowly. Seeing the wounds covering their bodies and the ruins of the Pill Tower behind them, he couldn’t help but sigh.","\"Master, we failed to protect the Heavenly Pill Tower. Please punish us!\""]},{"number":5088,"title":"Chapter 5088: How did you get back?","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu looked at them kneeling before her and said, \"You all did your best. If it’s destroyed, so be it! As long as no one’s hurt.\" Her gaze fell on Gray Wolf, whose abdomen still held a broken sword fragment, his face deathly pale. \"Find a place to tend to your wounds first,\" she instructed them.","Though the Heavenly Pill Tower was destroyed, they still had courtyards here. Thus, they headed first to the secondary estate, leaving some Phoenix Guards to guard the ruins and organize the site.","Watching Feng Jiu and the others depart for the secondary estate to tend to their wounds, the entire city’s aristocratic families and various factions erupted into turmoil.","Feng Jiu had returned! Feng Jiu, the Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu, had actually returned!","Amidst the shock and disbelief, the news spread rapidly. Some rejoiced, others grew uneasy...","In the courtyard, Gray Wolf was helped onto a bed in a room, where he lay half-reclined. Feng Jiu sat beside him, while Bai Xiao assisted nearby.","\"The spot where the sword pierced will bleed profusely if pulled out. But don’t worry—with me here, you won’t die.\" Feng Jiu spoke, watching Gray Wolf grin despite his pain, then shook her head.","\"My lady, it’s so good you’re back! My lady, how did you return? Did you visit my master in the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm? Is he about to awaken? Hehehe, with you here, I know I won’t die for sure.\" Gray Wolf’s weak face wore a huge smile, filled with both excitement and joy at seeing her.","\"Over at the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm, Luo Yu and the others were all injured. This time, quite a few sovereigns came to besiege them. Rumor has it they’re after Mo Ze.\" As she spoke, taking advantage of his distraction, she exerted force with her hand and pulled the broken sword lodged in his body out.","\"Ugh!\"","Gray Wolf grunted, as if struggling to catch his breath.","As the blade came free, a spurt of blood gushed forth. Immediately, a torrent of blood surged out. Feng Jiu swiftly sealed the surrounding acupoints to staunch the flow and clean the wound.","After finishing, she heard no further sound from him. Looking up, she saw he had already fainted. Seeing this, she couldn’t help but shake her head and smile. Examining the wound, she extended her palm, gathering a stream of Blue Lotus energy to heal him.","Beside them, Bai Xiao supported Gray Wolf as he watched the wound in Gray Wolf’s abdomen heal at a visible speed under her treatment. By the end, not even a scar remained.","\"Hm...\"","Gray Wolf let out a soft groan, like someone roused from deep sleep. He stirred slightly, then suddenly snapped his eyes open. There stood My Lady, washing her hands, and Bai Xiao beside her, staring intently at his abdomen.","\"What are you doing?!\" Grey Wolf glared, his hand instinctively flying to cover his bare stomach. Yet, the moment his hand touched his abdomen, he froze. Looking down, he saw not a single wound and couldn’t help but be slightly surprised. He turned to Feng Jiu, who had just finished drying her hands, and said, \"My lady, did you use the Blue Lotus’s power to heal me?\"","\"What? Think it healed too quickly?\" Feng Jiu raised an eyebrow, glancing at him with a hint of amusement.","\"No, no, no, how could that be! \" Gray Wolf hurriedly protested, jumping up joyfully. He swiftly retrieved his clothes and began dressing while asking, \"My lady, is the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm still all right? Is my Master okay? How are they all? My lady, how did you return? Didn’t you say you couldn’t come back after ascending? How did you...\"","\"Stop.\" Feng Jiu raised her hand helplessly, cutting off his barrage of questions."]},{"number":5089,"title":"Chapter 5089: Not Good","paragraphs":["She looked at Gray Wolf and said, \"Once your wounds heal, you should leave! The outside is still in chaos, and I don’t have time to waste here. As for your questions, I’ll answer them once things settle down.\" As she spoke, she already began walking toward the exit.","The door opened. Qi Kang and several others were outside helping bandage the wounds of some Phoenix Guards. Seeing her emerge, they stepped forward. \"Master.\"","\"How are the injuries?\" she inquired, her gaze sweeping over the Phoenix Guards.","\"None are fatal, but they’re serious. Besides the wounded, we lost Seventeen brothers,\" Qi Kang reported, his expression grave. These Phoenix Guards were trained by their own hands, and this time, Seventeen had fallen.","Upon hearing this, Feng Jiu fell silent for a moment before saying, \"Give them a proper burial.\" Most of the Phoenix Guards were orphans raised from childhood. They had no family to speak of, and the Feng family was their home. She was their Master, and she was their family.","\"Yes, Your Highness. Understood.\"","Qi Kang added, \"Master, what of the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm? Should we send reinforcements? With so many rulers slain, chaos will surely erupt across the celestial realms. And that figure behind the scenes—he orchestrated this entire affair.\"","Before coming here, I searched the soul of the Nancheng Monarch and learned the basics of their affairs,\" Feng Jiu said, her gaze drifting toward the distant sky. \"This person behind the scenes is revered as the Firmament Monarch. Several years ago, he somehow obtained the Black Lotus, which had been lost to the world. Moreover, this Firmament Monarch is a descendant of an emperor from the Upper Immortal Realm.\"","Her voice paused slightly as she continued, \"Beyond targeting you, their primary objective was to use Mo Ze against me. They never anticipated my return at this moment.\"","Hearing this, the group felt a wave of dread wash over them. Had their Master not returned just then, they might truly have been unable to protect Hell’s Lord within the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm.","\"The Heavenly Pill Tower has been destroyed. There’s no need to rebuild it. For now, there are other matters requiring your attention,\" Feng Jiu stated, her gaze fixed upon them.","\"Master, please give your orders.\"","\"My lady, please instruct us.\"","They spoke in unison, their gazes fixed upon her. With her here now, whatever task she assigned them, their hearts were filled with unwavering confidence.","\"Secure the Heavenly Realm territories. With so many sovereigns now fallen by my hand, chaos is inevitable. You...\" She spoke, but suddenly, as if sensing something, her expression abruptly changed.","\"Not good!\"","With a flick of her sleeve, a teleportation vortex appeared before her. A crimson figure swiftly darted inside.","Qi Kang and the others nearby froze in surprise. As they snapped back to reality, seeing the vortex about to close, Qi Kang bellowed, \"Gray Wolf, follow her!\"","Almost the instant his voice fell, Gray Wolf’s figure darted forward, leaping into the vortex. Simultaneously, the vortex vanished.","\"Could something have happened in the Eastern Sea Spirit Realm? Master looked so alarmed—this must be connected to Hell’s Lord.\" Many murmured beside him, his expression grave and filled with concern.","Shadow One pressed his lips together, saying nothing. He knew Xu Duo’s conjecture was likely spot on.","\"Hell’s Lord has his own master to handle. We must focus on resolving matters here and fulfilling the tasks our Master assigned us,\" Qi Kang said in a solemn tone. After glancing at them, he led the way out."]},{"number":5090,"title":"Chapter 5090: The Barrier Breaks","paragraphs":["In the Eastern Sea Spirit Domain, shortly after Feng Jiu departed, the sea surface erupted with towering waves. It seemed as though something had plunged from the sky into the ocean in that instant, sending a spray of water flying amidst the colossal swells.","The commotion on the sea surface alarmed Du Fan and the others. They rushed out to investigate, only to see waves surging over ten meters high, rolling majestically toward their airship.","\"What’s going on? How could waves suddenly appear with no wind?\" Luo Yu stepped outside and froze upon seeing the colossal waves.","\"Weren’t all those monarchs killed? Who could be causing trouble now?\" Guan Xilin frowned, his gaze fixed on the towering waves as their airship began ascending higher.","\"Something’s wrong!\"","Luo Yu’s eyes narrowed sharply. \"Before our master arrived, there was another figure hiding behind the clouds!\"","Hearing this, they recalled the moment and immediately declared, \"Dive into the sea and investigate!\"","The figure concealed behind the clouds—they had heard its voice but never seen its form. Especially when their Master arrived, not even a trace of its presence remained, as if it had vanished long ago.","But now, gazing at the churning sea surface without wind, their hearts sank.","Yet, just as they plunged into the ocean, a colossal surge of energy erupted from the depths. It felt like an explosion, its force so immense that the energy waves radiating outward were clearly visible even beneath the water.","\"Boom!\"","\"CRASH!\"","Amidst the deafening roar, a terrifying current surged forth. In that instant, the entire sea convulsed violently. Water erupted upward, and even those who had just plunged into the depths were violently flung back to the surface by the overwhelming, terrifying pressure of the torrent.","\"Boom! Boom! Boom!\"","As if a wave of air pressure erupted from the ocean depths, it violently hurled them out of the sea. Just as they were flung upward, they quickly regained their footing while retreating, shock evident in their eyes.","\"The barrier set by our Master has been breached!\" Du Fan’s expression darkened, his heart sinking with a vague sense of foreboding.","\"With the barrier broken, Hell’s Lord might...\"","Luo Yu’s expression was equally grave. They watched the turbulent currents still surging outward. The seawater now resembled boiling water, bubbling violently from the ocean depths to the surface. The sheer power of that current was unimaginable.","\"Who could possibly break through Little Jiu’s barrier? What will happen to Mo Ze down there? No, I must go down and see for myself.\" Guan Xilin’s heart filled with worry, and he prepared to leap back into the water.","\"You can’t get in, and even if you did, it would be useless now. Once the barrier breaks, the Master should sense it.\" Du Fan grabbed his arm, his gaze fixed on the sea surface.","His words had barely left his mouth when a whirlpool erupted. A crimson figure streaked across the water like a flash of light, followed closely by Gray Wolf.","\"Master!\"","They hurriedly called out, reporting the incident: \"A massive wave suddenly erupted in the sea. We tried to dive down to investigate but were flung back by violent currents below. It seems... it seems the barrier you set has been breached.\"","Feng Jiu narrowed her eyes at the churning currents and dispersing aura on the sea surface. \"Breaking my barrier alone wouldn’t cause such a commotion. This aura... it resembles the turbulent currents created when someone self-detonates and collides with a barrier.\""]},{"number":5091,"title":"Chapter 5091: Something’s Wrong","paragraphs":["As she spoke, her divine sense probed downward, searching for Mo Ze’s location. Yet, the moment she probed, her heart sank.","Seeing her face turn extremely grim, Du Fan and the others exchanged glances and asked, \"Master, how is Hell’s Lord?\"","\"Gone.\"","Feng Jiu’s voice was slightly deepened, coldness evident in her eyes. \"A trace of Black Lotus aura lingers in the depths of the sea. It was the Firmament Monarch who took action.\"","She hadn’t expected that a mere sovereign could break through her barrier, especially while she was en route to the Heavenly Pill Tower. The lingering aura of the Black Lotus in the sea was accompanied by a distinct scent of blood, which deeply unsettled her, stirring an urge to unleash a bloody rampage.","She drew in a breath and soared into the air, her murderous intent pouring forth in that instant. A crimson figure streaked out like a flash of light, vanishing instantly into the clouds.","Her speed was too swift—so swift that Du Fan and the others had no chance to follow. Watching her depart, Du Fan remarked, \"Our Master must be going after that Firmament Monarch.\"","\"Should we follow and assist?\" Gray Wolf inquired.","Luo Yu shook his head. \"Our Master moves too swiftly for us to catch up. Moreover, her power is formidable—our presence would be of no help. With so many Sovereigns slain, chaos is inevitable. Our duty now is to quell the uprisings across the realms, ensuring our Master faces no distractions.\"","Hearing this, Gray Wolf glanced at him. \"That’s exactly what My Lady told Qi Kang earlier.\" His voice trailed off as he gazed toward the horizon, his voice tinged with worry. \"But now that our Master is gone, could something have happened?\"","\"I don’t believe Hell’s Lord will come to harm. Even if he hasn’t regained consciousness yet, the Firmament Monarch intends to threaten Master. Hell’s Lord will certainly not allow anything to happen to Hell’s Lord. Otherwise, if Hell’s Lord truly met with misfortune, the Firmament Monarch wouldn’t survive either.\" Du Fan spoke slowly, his gaze fixed on the sea surface where the air currents were gradually dissipating. \"Although he is no longer beneath us, I believe it is necessary to go down and investigate.\"","\"I’ll go with you,\" Leng Hua declared.","Du Fan looked at him and nodded. \"Alright.\" With that, both plunged into the sea.","\"Let’s return and make arrangements,\" Luo Yu said, turning toward the airship.","The towering waves had receded at some point, and the churning sea gradually calmed. Yet, a heavy weight settled in everyone’s hearts—for Hell’s Lord was gone.","Inside the airship, Fan Lin was assisting Qin Xin and Ye Feifei with their treatment. Stepping out of the cabin, he saw them return and asked, \"How did it go?\"","The others shook their heads and briefly recounted the situation.","Hearing their words, Fan Lin and the others couldn’t help but frown. \"This is troublesome.\"","\"My lady has already gone after her. She’ll be fine,\" Gray Wolf stated, though it was unclear whether he was reassuring them or himself.","After a long while, Du Fan and Leng Hua returned from the ocean depths, landing back in the airship. Both pressed their lips tightly together, their expressions grim.","\"How did it go? Did you find anything?\" Guan Xilin asked urgently.","Du Fan and Leng Hua exchanged a glance before Leng Hua replied, \"We found some extremely small fragments of bodies on the seabed. Our master said it was triggered by her self-destruction spell breaking her barrier, but under those circumstances, we feel something isn’t quite right.\"","\"It’s impossible for someone to have taken Hell’s Lord away while the self-destruction spell was active. And that air current was so powerful, so...\" Du Fan paused, his expression grave."]},{"number":5092,"title":"Chapter 5092: Can’t Find","paragraphs":["Listening to their words, the group frowned and said, \"If one person triggered a self-detonation to break through the barrier, there must have been another person present to carry away Hell’s Lord. But from the moment the commotion occurred until we came out to investigate, it was only a split second—we didn’t see anyone leaving the sea surface at all.\"","\"I suspect they departed directly from the ocean floor. Moreover, under those circumstances, even a sovereign-level power couldn’t safely carry Hell’s Lord away while another sovereign triggered a self-detonation,\" Du Fan stated, turning to them. \"I must travel to the celestial realm governed by the Firmament Monarch.\"","He needed to verify certain matters. If things unfolded as he suspected, then... trouble would be inevitable.","Upon hearing this, Luo Yu and the others replied, \"Very well. Since only you are going, see if there’s anything we can assist with. Should you find any trace of Hell’s Lord, remember to inform us.\"","\"Mhm.\" Du Fan acknowledged, then gathered his qi and soared skyward.","Leng Hua remained silent, deep in thought beside him, lost in her own musings.","Having previously searched the soul of the Nancheng Monarch, she knew precisely where the Firmament Monarch’s domain lay. As dusk fell, she arrived at this region.","Her silent approach went unnoticed. She headed straight for the Firmament Monarch’s palace, discreetly probing its surroundings.","Along the way, she pondered: How had the Firmament Monarch compelled a sovereign to detonate themselves to breach her barrier? And how had he survived the explosive shockwave’s devastation to carry away Mo Ze?","Could it be that the Firmament Monarch possessed some life-saving artifact? What else could explain it all?","The heavily guarded palace was patrolled by sentries everywhere, yet navigating through them proved effortless for her. With their limited strength and cultivation, detecting her was utterly impossible.","Without alerting anyone, she thoroughly scouted the palace, yet found no trace of the Firmament Monarch.","Not here? Had he fled to hide elsewhere? Was that even possible?","The vast expanse outside could never match the security of this familiar palace. Moreover, she was certain some subterranean chamber or secret passage must exist within these walls. Perhaps the Firmament Monarch had hidden himself and Mo Ze somewhere deep within the palace.","After searching in vain, she drew a deep breath, suppressing her irritation and murderous intent. Calming her mind, she unleashed her divine sense to scan the entire palace.","The moment her divine sense began its search, several cultivators within the palace who possessed considerable strength and cultivation instantly detected it.","\"Who goes there!\"","A commanding shout echoed from various corners of the palace. Simultaneously, figures darted out from all directions, hovering mid-air. Their piercing gazes, radiating an intimidating aura, scanned the palace for the unwelcome intruder daring to probe with divine sense.","When their gazes swept through the darkness and landed upon the crimson figure that remained distinctly visible even in the night, some eyes narrowed involuntarily, filled with shock and disbelief.","\"Ghost Doctor Feng Jiu!\"","They were here, yet had received no word of Feng Jiu’s return. Thus, seeing someone who should not have been here at this moment left them utterly stunned and bewildered."]},{"number":5093,"title":"Chapter 5093: Underground Chamber","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu glanced at them, her icy voice carrying through the night breeze: \"Where is the Firmament Monarch?\"","\"The... Monarch hasn’t returned,\" one of them stammered, his face turning deathly pale at her sight.","\"Is that so?\"","Her tone remained detached, yet in the next instant, a long sword glowing with a bluish light appeared in her hand. Its sharp tip pointed diagonally toward the ground, releasing a fierce, chilling sword qi from its blade—a presence so fierce and terrifying it sent shivers down the spines of those present.","That murderous intent was palpable even to the cultivators a hundred meters away. The moment they saw her draw the sword, their eyes narrowed. Some turned and fled, while others immediately knelt, crying out, \"Ghost Doctor, spare our lives! I... I know there’s a secret chamber in the Monarch’s palace! Perhaps he’s hiding there! I can lead you to it!\"","Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!","As the cultivators turned to flee, the fierce sword qi surged forth. Several cold gleams, carrying terrifying killing intent, shot straight toward them. A few agonized screams pierced the night air, followed by the sound of bodies collapsing.","Among the fleeing cultivators, only the one who had knelt trembling remained alive.","A crimson robe swept through the night, appearing before the surviving cultivator in an instant. \"Lead the way.\" Feng Jiu’s icy voice cut through the darkness with piercing clarity, her aura of lethal intent sending shivers down the spine.","\"Yes, yes.\" The cultivator wiped cold sweat from his brow, trembling as he rose to lead her toward the palace below.","However, the deaths of those cultivators and the sound of their bodies hitting the ground below alerted the night patrol guards. Instantly, chaotic footsteps echoed from below, accompanied by a sharp shout.","\"Who dares trespass into the Firmament Palace at night!\"","Both the night patrol guards and the shadow guards lurking in the darkness surged forth simultaneously, swiftly encircling the two. Though these guards and shadow guards had never seen Feng Jiu before, they recognized the trembling cultivator beside her. Just as they were about to demand answers, a wave of murderous intent spread out, and cold gleams flashed through the night.","She didn’t crush them with overwhelming pressure; she killed them outright. For the rage boiling within her now could only be quelled by bloodshed!","The cultivator beside her watched the scene, his lips quivering. The encircling guards and shadow guards numbered at least a hundred. Yet in the blink of an eye—before he could even discern how she had appeared—they fell one after another.","Blood splattered the ground, severed limbs scattered everywhere. The bloody scene sent a chill through his heart, despite his experience with such sights.","\"Let’s go.\"","The cold, clear voice rang unexpectedly in his ear, startling him. He jolted upright and hurriedly led the way.","Entering the main palace, guided by the cultivator, they reached the door to the secret chamber. As the cultivator opened it, an icy chill seeped out from within.","Feng Jiu glanced around. This place was layered with countless barriers and formations; without this person leading the way, it would have been nearly impossible to find in such a short time.","She glanced at the cultivator and asked, \"What is your role here? How did you know of this chamber’s existence?\" Logically, such a place should be unknown to anyone but its master.","\"I... I once secretly entered this palace and saw the ruler enter this chamber. That’s how I... how I know.\""]},{"number":5094,"title":"Chapter 5094: Frozen Abyss","paragraphs":["His voice trembled as he whispered, stealing a glance at her. Seeing her expression remained impassive, he quickly added, \"Ghost Doctor, I’ve never entered this secret chamber. I don’t know what lies within. But if the sovereign has returned, his hiding place must be here. So... so, you see, could I... could I possibly...\"","He dared not follow further. What if he failed to find the monarch inside? What if the Ghost Doctor flew into a rage and killed him? Or worse, even if the monarch was indeed there, if he followed in, he likely wouldn’t survive.","Whoosh!","\"Arghh!\"","A sharp, icy gleam sliced through the air, followed by a piercing scream. Blood spattered as the cultivator collapsed to his knees, one arm severed and lying on the ground, the wound gushing crimson blood.","\"Get out.\"","Feng Jiu didn’t even glance at him, her voice cold and indifferent.","\"Yes, yes. Thank you, Ghost Doctor, for sparing my life,\" he said gratefully. He kowtowed to her once before clutching his severed arm and hurrying out.","Compared to the others who had been killed outright, losing only an arm was a tremendous mercy. He felt as if he’d been granted a second chance at life. Daring not linger, he fled the palace swiftly.","Feng Jiu stepped into the secret chamber and descended the stone steps. Inside, she sensed not only the icy chill in the air but also an intensely potent aura of spiritual energy.","As she descended, the space before her grew ever larger. This was no ordinary underground chamber—it was an entire subterranean palace.","Fist-sized night pearls and glass lamps dotted the walls, illuminating the space brilliantly. Yet a faint mist hung within, seemingly condensed from the cold.","As she advanced, a ferocious beast suddenly lunged toward her. Its momentum was fierce, its force immense, stirring the air into a howling wind.","Her eyes narrowed as spirit energy surged around her. In an instant, her crimson figure darted forward, not evading but charging straight into the fray. Her blade struck with lightning speed, slashing viciously at the fierce beast.","Whoosh!","Roar!","A fierce sword qi, carrying the weight of ancient might, spread out. Instantly, a piercing beastly howl echoed through the mist, followed by a thunderous crash—as if the fierce beast’s corpse had collapsed.","The mist dispersed under the surge of spirit energy, clearing the view. Feng Jiu looked down at the ground ahead, where a divine beast-level fierce beast lay split in two by a single sword strike. Head and body lay severed, blood gushing forth and staining the earth crimson.","She withdrew her gaze indifferently and continued walking forward. As she advanced deeper, she faintly sensed the aura of the Black Lotus. After moving about ten meters further, she encountered a barrier radiating the essence of the Black Lotus.","\"Break!\"","With a clear shout, she thrust her hand forward. A powerful force surged forth, instantly shattering the barrier.","\"Boom!\"","A muffled explosion echoed—not loud, yet accompanied by a visible wave of air that rippled outward, spreading through the surroundings. The black lotus energy within this air permeated the area, yet dared not approach Feng Jiu.","Feng Jiu swept her sleeve aside, dispersing the currents. She stepped forward, unlocking a stone door within. As it swung open, a world of ice and snow unfolded before her eyes..."]},{"number":5095,"title":"Chapter 5095: Found","paragraphs":["It resembled an ice cellar, entirely white within, with frigid air pouring out so intensely that she could feel the bone-chilling cold even standing by the stone door.","The intense cold had crystallized the surrounding air into a blanket of snow-white ice. In one corner, upon an ice bed that seemed carved from the heavens themselves, Xuanyuan Mo Ze lay clad in black robes, appearing as though in deep slumber.","Spotting him, she strode inside, approaching the ice bed and calling out, \"Mo Ze!\"","Her voice echoed unanswered. There was no sign of the Firmament Monarch within.","She gazed at Mo Ze, now lying on the icy bed. It had been years since she’d seen him up close. This time, she hadn’t even had the chance to visit him at the ocean depths before he was brought here.","She reached out to gently stroke his face. Feeling the solidity of his immortal body and the steadiness of his aura, the worry in her heart finally eased.","\"As long as you’re alright,\" she murmured softly, exhaling a small sigh of relief before a faint smile touched her lips. \"Mo Ze, I’m back. Do you know that?\"","She clasped his hand, feeling its icy chill, then glanced around at the surrounding frozen landscape. \"This place must be a spiritual vein. The Spirit Energy here is exceptionally abundant, and it carries a cold, icy essence. This energy actually complements you. Compared to the depths of the East Sea Spirit Domain, the energy here is far more suitable for your divine soul.\"","She stepped back slightly, watching him as he slept. \"I’ll give you a hand,\" she said. \"I’ll channel this icy cold energy and the spiritual vein’s essence into your body.\"","As she spoke, her hands gathered energy, channeling the spirit energy and frigid aura toward him.","With Feng Jiu’s aid, a steady stream of spirit energy and icy qi flowed into his body, swiftly absorbed and transformed into vital energy within him.","As the spirit energy and frigid aura surged into Mo Ze, the air’s spirit energy gradually weakened. The surrounding frozen landscape began to thaw, with droplets of melted ice and snow silently falling to the ground.","By the end of the night, the entire frozen landscape had vanished, revealing the stone walls hidden beneath the ice. The underground palace now resembled a parched, dry well, utterly devoid of any spirit energy.","Feng Jiu withdrew her hand, exhaled softly, and glanced at the damp surroundings before preparing to lead Mo Ze away. Just then, she faintly heard Du Fan’s call.","\"Master!\"","\"Master!\"","Du Fan entered the palace hall, where corpses littered the floor everywhere, their deaths horribly gruesome. The entire hall was deathly quiet, devoid of any living soul except for the dead strewn across the floor.","Seeing this scene, he knew his Master had been here, but whether he was still present remained unknown. Just as he prepared to scan the area with his divine sense, his Master’s voice reached him.","\"I’m in the underground palace beneath the main hall. Come here!\"","Hearing the voice, he hurried toward the main palace. Finding his way inside, he entered the underground chamber only to see, besides his master, what appeared to be Hell’s Lord present as well. Instantly quickening his pace, he rushed forward, asking as he approached, \"Master, how is Hell’s Lord?\""]},{"number":5096,"title":"Chapter 5096: Something’s Off","paragraphs":["\"I was just about to take him back. Your arrival is perfect timing—come help me carry him!\" Feng Jiu said, glancing at Du Fan as he swiftly approached. She then asked, \"How did you find us so quickly? Have you been here before?\"","\"No, but I had people investigate the Firmament Monarch, so I knew the location of his palace.\" Du Fan replied, approaching her side. After glancing at the sleeping Hell’s Lord, he surveyed the surroundings and asked, \"Master, have you found the Firmament Monarch?\"","Feng Jiu shook her head. \"Strange as it may seem, I came here to find Mo Ze but didn’t see the Firmament Monarch. Mo Ze was placed here, and the original environment was highly beneficial for him. However, the area was originally sealed with Black Lotus energy, yet beyond this place, I can’t detect any trace of Black Lotus energy.\"","She sensed something was amiss, yet couldn’t pinpoint the source of the problem.","\"Master, I have something to report,\" Du Fan said, glancing at the slumbering Xuanyuan Mo Ze.","Noticing this, Feng Jiu turned to look and asked, \"What is it? Speak.\"","\"Before coming here, Leng Hua and I descended into the deep sea to investigate. We discovered fragments of a broken body that had breached the barrier you set. Master also mentioned it was a self-detonation, and only a monarch-level being could breach Master’s defensive barrier. But there’s one thing I can’t figure out: the chaos and terrifying air currents caused by such an explosion were immense. How did the Firmament Monarch survive under such circumstances, and even take Hell’s Lord away?\"","\"My guess is he must have possessed some protective artifact,\" Feng Jiu said, pausing before continuing, \"It’s highly likely he harnessed the power of the Black Lotus to control a Monarch, forcing them to sacrifice themselves as a shield to breach my barrier. Simultaneously, he used some treasure to shield himself while carrying Mo Ze away.\"","She briefly pondered before saying, \"As a descendant of the Great Emperor of the Upper Immortal Realm, this Firmament Monarch could very well possess some life-saving artifact.\"","Hearing this, Du Fan paused and turned to Hell’s Lord. \"Has Master examined his body? Did anything seem amiss?\"","Feng Jiu, who had been deep in thought, looked up at him in surprise. \"What do you mean? Do you suspect something’s wrong with Mo Ze?\"","As she spoke, she glanced at the reclining Mo Ze. Before Du Fan could respond, she continued, \"I examined him last night. Perhaps due to the energies here, his immortal body is exceptionally well-formed. Moreover, I used the spirit energy from the veins within and the frigid aura of this place to fortify his immortal physique. It’s possible he may awaken soon.\"","She had indeed examined him thoroughly; everything appeared normal. This was precisely what puzzled her. Why had the Firmament Monarch brought him here only to vanish, leaving Mo Ze behind? What could be the reason? Where had he gone?","Hearing her words, Du Fan’s heart finally settled. He replied, \" \"If you say Hell’s Lord shows no signs of trouble, that’s excellent news. This place is rather damp. Master, shall we return?\"","\"Mhm.\" Feng Jiu nodded, helping Mo Ze to his feet as they stepped outside. A teleportation vortex materialized in her palm, and in the next instant, all three vanished into its swirling depths."]},{"number":5097,"title":"Chapter 5097: So It Was Hiding Here","paragraphs":["Feng Jiu and Du Fan brought Mo Ze to the villa where Qi Kang and the others were staying. After a night of handling the situation, Qi Kang and his group had already brought things under control. Seeing the three of them appear suddenly, they were startled and hurried forward.","\"Master, what happened to Hell’s Lord?\"","\"Master!\" Shadow One swiftly stepped forward to help support him.","Feng Jiu let Shadow One and Du Fan escort him inside, saying, \"An incident occurred. There’s no longer any need to guard the Eastern Sea Spirit Domain. Send word to Luo Yu and the others—tell them we are here now.\"","She paused, then added, \"Also, inform my brother to tell my grandfather and the others not to worry. They needn’t come all this way, lest...\" Her words trailed off as Du Fan’s startled cry echoed from inside.","\"Master! Come see!\"","Hearing the commotion, Feng Jiu abandoned all else and hurried inside. The moment she entered, an icy chill permeated the air, accompanied by the aura of the Black Lotus surging from Mo Ze’s body.","Du Fan and Shadow One stepped back, overwhelmed by the overwhelming energy. Their hearts raced with concern, yet they dared not approach abruptly.","Feng Jiu entered to find Mo Ze lying on the bed, his body pulsing with an icy chill. Simultaneously, the aura of the Black Lotus surged from him. The two energies seemed locked in a struggle, saturating the entire room with both the bitter cold and the dark lotus essence.","\"You two, step outside,\" Feng Jiu ordered, gesturing for them to leave.","Seeing this, they quickly exited, closing the door behind them and remaining vigilant by the threshold. Du Fan’s expression grew solemn as he lowered his eyes, lost in thought.","Shadow One kept glancing back at the room, unable to contain his curiosity. \"What’s going on? Who brought the Master out from the deep sea? Has his immortal body already been fully formed? And what about that frigid aura and the black lotus energy earlier?\"","\"Du Fan, you’ve been by the Master’s side. You should know what’s happening! Tell us!\" Qi Kang and the others stepped forward.","Du Fan lifted his gaze to meet theirs. \"The Firmament Monarch shattered the defensive barrier that Master had cast beneath the sea and took Hell’s Lord away. Master pursued him to the Palace of the Heavens and found Hell’s Lord within its subterranean chambers. When I arrived, the Firmament Monarch was nowhere to be seen. I merely brought Hell’s Lord back. As for the rest... I don’t fully understand it yet.\"","Hearing this, the group exchanged glances but said nothing further, choosing instead to wait there.","Inside the room, Feng Jiu stood by the bed, observing the two energies battling within Mo Ze’s body. Her eyes flickered. Within the frigid aura, she sensed the faint presence of the Green Dragon. Yet within the black lotus energy, she vaguely detected an essence that did not belong to Mo Ze.","As if recalling something, her heart stirred. She tapped her finger against his brow, sending a thread of divine consciousness into his sea of consciousness.","Within the sea of consciousness, white and hazy, an icy chill pervaded. Her thread of divine consciousness entered and saw Mo Ze slumbering within, along with the form of the Green Dragon faintly taking shape from the energy currents around him, and that sliver of divine soul.","\"Firmament Monarch! So you were hiding here!\"","Feng Jiu’s icy voice carried a palpable intent to kill. Yet she did not advance, merely halting her steps to observe the scene. Firmament Monarch’s soul sought to devour Mo Ze’s soul and possess his body. However, he had underestimated Mo Ze’s inherent strength."]},{"number":5098,"title":"Chapter 5098: Clash","paragraphs":["Even in his slumber, Mo Ze instinctively countered the attempt to devour his divine soul and possess his body. The dormant energy of the Green Dragon coiled around him, now tightly binding the divine soul of the Firmament Monarch.","However, the presence of the Black Lotus’ mark within the Firmament Monarch’s divine soul complicated matters.","Though she had entered, this was Mo Ze’s sea of consciousness. She could not act to destroy the Firmament Monarch’s soul for him, lest she also wound Mo Ze’s own soul and sea of consciousness. At this moment, only Mo Ze himself could annihilate the Firmament Monarch.","\"Feng Jiu! Once I possess him, we’ll see how you dare to be so arrogant! Hahahaha...\" A face brimming with malevolence emerged, its vicious, cruel laughter echoing through the sea of consciousness.","Feng Jiu stood motionless, watching him silently. A faint curve touched her lips as she replied, \"Is that so? Do you think possessing him will be so easy? Even now, while he sleeps, he still holds you captive. Do you truly believe you have a chance?\"","Her voice grew soft and detached as she continued unhurriedly, \"You may be hiding here, but your descendants won’t be so fortunate. With my current power and abilities, Feng Jiu, they’ll fall into my hands even if they flee to the ends of the earth. Tell me, how should I kill them then?\"","\"Skinning them alive? Grinding their bones to dust? Or perhaps annihilating their very souls? Condemning them to eternal torment?\" Her voice drifted softly, yet the chill and murderous intent within it were so terrifying they sent shivers down one’s spine.","\"Reduced to such a state, tell me—would they thank you? Or would they curse you?\"","Her voice drifted out, faint and eerie, like a demonic chant that unsettled his mind. His soul grew unstable, and he screamed wildly: \"Shut up! Stop talking! Stop it! Ah!\"","His mind in turmoil, his soul grew even more unstable, its aura weakening by the moment.","\"No!\"","The fading of his soul made him cry out in terror. He felt the dragon energy of the Green Dragon binding him like an unbreakable rope, leaving him no chance to struggle. Moreover, the power of the slumbering Xuanyuan Mo Ze’s soul was so overwhelming that the soul attempting to devour him was being slowly consumed by it instead.","This realization filled him with terror from the depths of his being: \"No! I will succeed! I will succeed! Arghhhhhhhhhhhh!\"","His furious shouts, thick with resentment and malevolence, intensified the black lotus energy surging through him. In that instant, his soul power, the black lotus energy, and the Green Dragon energy within Mo Ze erupted simultaneously, filling the entire sea of consciousness. Startled, Feng Jiu spun away, instantly exiting the sea of consciousness.","\"Pfft!\"","The moment she exited Mo Ze’s sea of consciousness, she stumbled backward, spitting out a mouthful of blood.","Hearing the commotion inside the room, Du Fan and the others guarding the door outside were startled. They quickly pushed open the door and rushed in: \"Master!\"","Entering the room, they found Feng Jiu leaning on the table with one hand while wiping blood from the corner of her mouth with the other. They hurriedly helped her sit down. \"Master, how are you?\"","\"I’m fine.\" Feng Jiu shook her head, motioning for them to step back. Rising to her feet, she gathered a surge of Blue Lotus energy in her hands, enveloping Mo Ze on the bed and sealing off the Black Lotus energy entirely."]},{"number":5099,"title":"Chapter 5099: Everyone’s Here","paragraphs":["After catching her breath, she walked over to the table and sat down. Looking at Mo Ze on the bed, she said, \"The divine soul of the Firmament Monarch is hidden within Mo Ze’s sea of consciousness.\"","\"What?!\" Shadow One gasped, her entire expression changing.","Du Fan, however, had long suspected as much. Hearing her words, his heart sank slightly. He asked, \"Master, is there a way to extract and destroy it?\"","Feng Jiu shook her head and replied slowly, \"When I checked his pulse earlier, I found nothing unusual. The Firmament Monarch must have concealed himself. The commotion now stems from his attempt to devour Mo Ze’s soul and possess his body. However, he underestimated Mo Ze’s strength. His devouring failed, and now he’s bound by the Green Dragon’s energy.\"","Her voice paused as she gazed at Mo Ze on the bed. \"The Firmament Monarch hides within his sea of consciousness. No one can aid him now. Only he himself can destroy that Firmament Monarch.\"","\"But this black lotus...\" Qi Kang’s brows furrowed slightly, worry evident.","Feng Jiu sighed softly. \"That is precisely my concern. If Mo Ze’s soul devours the Firmament Monarch’s soul, this Black Lotus will likely become imprinted upon his own soul. Yet if he does not consume the Firmament Monarch’s soul, he risks being possessed and taken over—a fate that leads to certain death.\"","\"Is there truly no other way?\" Bai Xiao couldn’t help but ask.","Feng Jiu shook her head. \"We’ll see. For now, let’s wait until he gets through this ordeal.\" Her gaze fell upon Mo Ze on the bed as she instructed Qi Kang and the others beside her, \"I’ll keep watch here. You may go about your business. It won’t be decided in the next hour or so.\"","\"Understood.\" They responded in unison, exiting the room. Qi Kang and the others departed first, while Du Fan and Shadow One remained behind to guard the courtyard.","Aware of the situation here, Guan Xilin, Luo Yu, and the others arrived the next day after concluding their affairs in the East Sea Spirit Domain. Along with them, the injured Ye Feifei and Qin Xin were also transferred to this location.","Both were severely injured. Despite Fan Lin’s treatment and medicinal pills, they hadn’t recovered yet. Since everyone had gathered here, they were brought along for easier care.","Guan Xilin strode in and saw Du Fan and Shadow One in the courtyard. \"Why are you two guarding here? How is Mo Ze? Has he woken up?\"","\"Not yet. The Master is keeping vigil inside. We can’t help by going in, so we’re waiting outside. If the Master has any instructions, we can respond immediately.\" Du Fan spoke, glancing at the others who had followed him in. \"Has everyone arrived?\"","\"Everyone’s here. With matters in the East Sea settled, we thought it best to gather here since the Master is present. That way, if anything arises, we can discuss it together.\" Luo Yu said, looking at them and asking, \"I heard from Qi Kang that the divine soul of the Firmament Monarch is hidden within Hell’s Lord’s sea of consciousness. What’s the current situation? Any results?\"","\"None.\" Shadow One said, gazing at the tightly closed door, his heart filled with worry.","\"That old bastard’s got some nerve, trying to possess our master’s body. He’s so powerful, even if nothing comes of it now, he’ll definitely end up dead!\"","Gray Wolf spat out the words with venom, striding over to sit at the table in the courtyard. He kept glancing toward the room and asked, \"How long has My lady been in there? Should we let her rest? We can take turns guarding.\""]},{"number":5100,"title":"Chapter 5100: Devouring the Soul","paragraphs":["\"She’s been inside since returning yesterday. We asked earlier, but Master said it wasn’t necessary. If anything happens while she’s in there, she can handle it immediately.\" Du Fan spoke, noticing Leng Shuang present. \"Leng Shuang, have the kitchen prepare some of the Master’s favorite dishes! She hasn’t eaten anything since yesterday.\"","\"Understood.\" Leng Shuang replied before turning to leave first.","\"By the way, how are Feifei and Qin Xin?\" Du Fan turned to ask Fan Lin.","\"They’ve been settled in. Their injuries are quite severe, mostly internal. Even with the medicinal pills, it’ll take some time for them to recover.\" Fan Lin explained. Thinking of their injuries, he added, \"Fortunately, the Master left us a substantial supply of medicinal pills. Otherwise, injuries like theirs would have been fatal.\"","A full-power strike from the Monarch leaves almost no chance of survival. Thankfully, they arrived in time and administered prompt treatment.","Just as they spoke, the door opened, and Feng Jiu emerged.","\"Little Jiu!\"","Guan Xilin rushed forward upon seeing her emerge. Noticing her troubled expression, he reassured her, \"Don’t worry too much. Mo Ze will be fine. The Firmament Monarch cannot take his soul.\"","\"Yes, Master! Hell’s Lord will definitely be fine! He is blessed by the heavens—nothing can harm him!\"","\"Yes, Master, don’t worry. Hell’s Lord will awaken eventually.\"","\"Master, you must believe in Hell’s Lord. He will surely overcome the Firmament Monarch.\"","Watching them all comfort her, each looking as if they feared she might worry too much, she couldn’t help but let a faint smile touch her lips: \" I know. I came out to tell you all that the divine soul of the Firmament Monarch has been devoured by Mo Ze. Moreover, by consuming his divine soul power, Mo Ze’s own divine soul power has grown even stronger.","Hearing this, the crowd froze, then erupted into cheers.","\"Wonderful!\"","\"I knew Master would be fine!\"","\"Truly worthy of Hell’s Lord!\"","\"Hahaha, my Master is the mightiest!\"","The group laughed joyfully, their happiness coming from the depths of their hearts. There was no other reason—originally, because Mo Ze was still in slumber, if he were awake, ten Firmament Monarchs wouldn’t stand a chance against him. But with him asleep, it was anyone’s game. So upon hearing this news, they breathed a sigh of relief and felt nothing but joy.","Du Fan remained relatively composed. He recalled his master mentioning that if Hell’s Lord consumed the divine soul of a Firmament Monarch, the Black Lotus would become imprinted upon Hell’s Lord’s divine soul. Thus, he turned to Feng Jiu and asked, \"Master, what of the Black Lotus? What has become of it?\"","The ancient black lotus could corrupt the human heart, unleashing the darkest parts within and driving one deeper into demonic possession. If that lotus now resided upon the sleeping Hell’s Lord’s soul, it would spell real trouble.","A soul imprint was no easy thing to erase.","Feng Jiu’s smile faded slightly as she replied, \"As expected, the ancient black lotus has now imprinted itself upon his soul. However, it is not a fully bloomed black lotus, and its power is relatively weak. Let us wait until he awakens before we devise a plan to erase it.\"","For now, this was the only option. There was no other way.","\"Right. One thing at a time. Things will work out for the best. Don’t worry too much.\" Guan Xilin patted the Gray Wolf’s shoulder beside him, then turned to Feng Jiu and asked, \"Little Jiu, how is Mo Ze’s condition? When will he wake up?\""]}]);
